       & "                <div id=""mdbook-content"" class=""content"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                    <main>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""iec-62304-software-safety-classes""><a class="
       & """header"" href=""#iec-62304-software-safety-classes"">IEC 62304 Software Safety"
       & " Classes</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>IEC 62304 defines three software safety classes (A, B, C) for the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "medical-device software lifecycle, ranked by the severity of the harm a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "failure could cause. adacovex assesses compliance against all three by"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "re-labelling the same four evidence checks it computes for DO-178C: HLR"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "traceability, no orphan tags, passing tests, and a minimum SPARK proof level"
       & ".</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""level-definitions""><a class=""header"" href=""#level-definitions"">Level"
       & " Definitions</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><th>Class</th><th>Severity</th><th>Possible Consequence</th><th>Example<"
       & "/th></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>C</td><td>Highest</td><td>Death or serious injury possible</td><td>I"
       & "nfusion-pump dosing, radiation-therapy control</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>B</td><td>Moderate</td><td>Non-serious injury possible</td><td>Diagn"
       & "ostic imaging, patient-monitor alarm logic</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>A</td><td>Lowest</td><td>No injury or damage to health</td><td>Admin"
       & "istrative/scheduling software, data logging</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""assessment-criteria""><a class=""header"" href=""#assessment-criteria"">A"
       & "ssessment Criteria</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex evaluates the same four criteria for every class; only the class"
       & " name"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and the minimum proof bar change.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""1-hlr-traceability""><a class=""header"" href=""#1-hlr-traceability"">1. "
       & "HLR Traceability</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><th>Class</th><th>Requirement</th></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>A"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "C</td><td>All high-level requirements (HLRs) traced to source-code tags (<co"
       & "de>-- HLR-XXXX</code>)</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""2-orphan-tags""><a class=""header"" href=""#2-orphan-tags"">2. Orphan Tag"
       & "s</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><th>Class</th><th>Requirement</th></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>A"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "C</td><td>Every in-source HLR tag must correspond to a defined HLR in HLR.md"
       & "</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""3-test-passfail""><a class=""header"" href=""#3-test-passfail"">3. Test P"
       & "ass/Fail</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><th>Class</th><th>Requirement</th></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>A"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "C</td><td>100% tests passing</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""4-minimum-spark-level""><a class=""header"" href=""#4-minimum-spark-leve"
       & "l"">4. Minimum SPARK Level</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><th>Class</th><th>Minimum SPARK Level</th></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>C</td><td>Gold</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>B</td><td>Silver</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>A</td><td>Bronze</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""mapping-to-the-shared-rigor-tier""><a class=""header"" href=""#mapping-t"
       & "o-the-shared-rigor-tier"">Mapping to the shared rigor tier</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>IEC 62304 safety classes map onto the same A"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "E rigor tier DO-178C uses, so one"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "assessment satisfies both standards at once:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><th>Class</th><th>Shared tier</th><th>DO-178C equivalent</th></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>C</td><td>A</td><td>DAL-A</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>B</td><td>B</td><td>DAL-B</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>A</td><td>C</td><td>DAL-C</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""cli-selection""><a class=""header"" href=""#cli-selection"">CLI selection"
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code class=""language-bash"">adacovex --target=. --class=A          # as"
       & "sess at safety Class A"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "adacovex --target=. --class=C          # assess at safety Class C (requires "
       & "Gold SPARK)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "adacovex --target=. --standard=iec62304 --dal=C   # Class A via the shared t"
       & "ier"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "adacovex --target=. --standard=all     # badges for DO-178C + ISO 26262 + IE"
       & "C 62304"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>See <a href=""../standards.html"">Standards</a> for the full cross-standard"
       & " tier mapping,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a href=""adacovex-dal-levels.html"">DAL Levels</a> for the DO-178C criteria t"
       & "his page"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "generalizes, and <a href=""adacovex-spark-levels.html"">SPARK Levels</a> for t"
       & "he per-level"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "proof bar.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""assessment-output""><a class=""header"" href=""#assessment-output"">Asses"
       & "sment Output</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The tool reports each criterion as met/unmet and a final Achieved/Unmet s"
       & "tatus,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "labelled with the safety-class name:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code>Target level: Class A"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Status: Achieved"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "HLR traced:  24 /  24"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Orphan tags: No"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Tests passing: Yes"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Min SPARK level met: Yes"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                    </main>"
