       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""docstring-annotation-specification""><a class"
       & "=""header"" href=""#docstring-annotation-specification"">Docstring Annotation Sp"
       & "ecification</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""supported-tags""><a class=""header"" href=""#supported-tags"">Supported T"
       & "ags</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Tags are placed immediately before the subprogram declaration (canonical "
       & "Ada"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "convention). Placement is also supported after the declaration for backward"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "compatibility. No blank lines between tags and declaration.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><th>Tag</th><th>Format</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>@param</code></td><td><code>--  @param Name  Description.</cod"
       & "e></td><td>Subprogram formal parameter</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>@parameter</code></td><td><code>--  @parameter Name  Descripti"
       & "on.</code></td><td>Alias of <code>@param</code></td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>@return</code></td><td><code>--  @return Description.</code></"
       & "td><td>Function return value</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>@returns</code></td><td><code>--  @returns Description.</code>"
       & "</td><td>Alias of <code>@return</code></td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>@field</code></td><td><code>--  @field Description.</code></td"
       & "><td>Record component</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>@formal</code></td><td><code>--  @formal Name  Description.</c"
       & "ode></td><td>Generic formal parameter</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>@brief</code></td><td><code>--  @brief Summary.</code></td><td"
       & ">Short summary; marks a subprogram documented</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>@summary</code></td><td><code>--  @summary Description.</code>"
       & "</td><td>Summary; marks a subprogram documented</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""conventions""><a class=""header"" href=""#conventions"">Conventions</a></"
       & "h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Prefix: <code>--  </code> (two dashes + two spaces) for all doc lines. T"
       & "he single-space"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>-- </code> and tab-separated (<code>--&lt;TAB&gt;</code>) comment styl"
       & "es are also recognised, so"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "generated or third-party code using those conventions counts toward coverage"
       & "."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "A bare <code>--</code> or <code>---</code> (divider) line is <strong>not</st"
       & "rong> a docstring.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Summary first, then tag lines, then declaration "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " no blank lines.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Descriptions capitalized, end with period.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Two spaces between tag name and description (alignment padding).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>A plain summary line (<code>--  Does a thing.</code>) is sufficient to m"
       & "ark a subprogram"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "as documented; tags are not required for no-param procedures.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""examples""><a class=""header"" href=""#examples"">Examples</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code class=""language-ada"">-- Returns the sum of two numbers."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "-- @param A  First operand."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "-- @param B  Second operand."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "-- @return  Sum of A and B."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "function Add (A, B : Integer) return Integer;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>@parameter</code> / <code>@returns</code> aliases and the common si"
       & "ngle-space style are"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "equivalent:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code class=""language-ada"">-- Increments the counter."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "-- @parameter Amount  Amount to add (alias of @param)."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "-- @returns The new value (alias of @return)."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "function Incr (Amount : Natural) return Natural;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code class=""language-ada"">-- A clock timestamp with node ID."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "-- @field Node    Replica identifier."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "-- @field Time    Logical timestamp value."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "type Clock_Time is record"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   Node : Replica_Id;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   Time : Natural;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "end record;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code class=""language-ada"">-- Generic priority queue."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "-- @formal Element_Type  Queue element type."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "-- @formal Max_Size      Maximum number of elements."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "package Priority_Queue is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   ..."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "end Priority_Queue;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""google--sphinx-styles""><a class=""header"" href=""#google--sphinx-style"
       & "s"">Google / Sphinx styles</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The scanner also recognises the two most common non-Ada docstring convent"
       & "ions,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "so the same subprogram can be documented in Ada, Google, or Sphinx style.</p"
       & ">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""google-style""><a class=""header"" href=""#google-style"">Google style</a"
       & "></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A <code>Args:</code> or <code>Args: ...</code> header opens a parameter b"
       & "lock: deeper-indented"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "following comment lines count as parameters. A <code>Returns:</code> header "
       & "marks the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "return-value description.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code class=""language-ada"">-- Do something useful."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "--"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "-- Args:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "--   X:  The first argument."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "--"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "-- Returns:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "--   The result."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "function Foo (X : Integer) return Integer;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""sphinx-style""><a class=""header"" href=""#sphinx-style"">Sphinx style</a"
       & "></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>:param Name:</code>, <code>:parameter Name:</code>, <code>:type Nam"
       & "e:</code>, <code>:return:</code>, <code>:returns:</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and <code>:rtype:</code> fields are all recognised.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code class=""language-ada"">-- Do something else."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "--"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "-- :param X: The argument."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "-- :returns: The result."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "function Bar (X : Integer) return Integer;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""coverage""><a class=""header"" href=""#coverage"">Coverage</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Docstring coverage measures: documented subprograms / total subprograms."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "A subprogram is "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "documented"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " if it has at least one docstring annotation tag,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "a <code>@brief</code> / <code>@summary</code> tag, or a summary comment line"
       & " (any recognised prefix)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "immediately preceding or following it.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Coverage is displayed in terminal reports and SVG badges.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""hlr-traceability-tags""><a class=""header"" href=""#hlr-traceability-tag"
       & "s"">HLR traceability tags</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>HLR (High-Level Requirement) tags use the format <code>-- HLR-XXXX</code>"
       & " on their own"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "comment line:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code class=""language-ada"">--  HLR-SCAN: Source scanning"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Multiple HLR tags can appear on one line:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code class=""language-ada"">--  HLR-ARCH: Version constant  HLR-ARCH: Pa"
       & "ckage hierarchy"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Tag IDs map to the requirement index in <code>docs/HLR.md</code>; the sca"
       & "nner matches"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "in-source tags against that index for the DO-178C traceability assessment.</"
       & "p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""see-also""><a class=""header"" href=""#see-also"">See also</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><a href=""../target-projects.html"">Target projects</a> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " what a target must provide, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "how strict mode counts vendored code</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><a href=""../architecture.html#patch-system"">Architecture "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " Patch System</a> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " overlay"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "docstrings on vendored code without modifying the originals</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><a href=""adacovex-dal-levels.html"">DAL Levels</a> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " how HLR tags feed the traceability"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "criterion of the compliance assessment</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
