       & "                        <h1 id=""adacovexparsers""><a class=""header"" href=""#ad"
       & "acovexparsers"">Adacovex.Parsers</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Read one physical line from F into Line and report Last as usual."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "When the physical line is longer than Line"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "Length, drain (discard) the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "trailing part so the file is positioned at the next line."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Set Overflow to True.  Report an error to standard error that names"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "File_Path (with Line_Num when non-zero) and the buffer size."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Callers must treat Overflow as an explicit parse failure.  Do not"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "process the truncated content because it produces partial results."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "@param F  Open input file positioned at the line to read."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "@param File_Path  Path of the file, used in the overflow error message."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "@param Line_Num  Physical line number (1-based), or 0 to omit it."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "@param Line  Output buffer receiving up to Line"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "Length characters."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "@param Last  Index of the last valid character in Line."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "@param Overflow  True when the physical line exceeded Line"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "Length.</p>"
