       & "<code>tests: N passed, M failed</code> and consumed by the DAL "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "Tests passing"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & ASCII.LF
       & "criterion;</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>per-category metrics</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>Categories</code> (name, count, status), consumed"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "by the dashboard"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s Tests chart and the <code>--emit-metrics</code> export;</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>the summary lines below.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""markdown-table-native-test-runner""><a class=""header"" href=""#markdown"
       & "-table-native-test-runner"">Markdown Table (native test runner)</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The built-in <code>test_runner</code> executable produces this format, an"
       & "d any"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Markdown table with the same shape is accepted:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code>  | Category            |  Tests | Status   |"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "  |---------------------|--------|----------|"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "  | Types conversions   |  67 | PASS     |"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "  | Server routing      |  25 | PASS     |"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "  | DAL compliance      |   2 | FAIL     |"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "  |-----------------------------------------|--------|----------|"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "  Passed: 92  Failed: 2"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""format-rules""><a class=""header"" href=""#format-rules"">Format rules</a"
       & "></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Columns separated by <code>|</code>. The header row and <code>|---|</cod"
       & "e> separator rows are"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "ignored (they have no numeric count cell).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Two row layouts are accepted</strong> (the count cell is detecte"
       & "d by its"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "digits in either):"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>with a leading index cell: <code>| - | Category | N | PASS |</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(the AUnit-report style),</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>plain: <code>| Category | N | PASS |</code> (the native <code>test_runne"
       & "r</code> style).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Category</strong> cell: arbitrary text (leading/trailing spaces "
       & "are trimmed).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Tests</strong> cell: a positive integer, optionally space-padded"
       & " to the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "column width (<code>| 67 |</code>). Header and separator rows have no such c"
       & "ell.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Status</strong> cell: <code>PASS</code> (anything else counts as"
       & " <code>FAIL</code>).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Each row ADDITIONALLY adds its count to the totals.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>A summary line containing <code>Passed:</code> and <code>Failed:</code> "
       & "followed by numbers"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<strong>overrides</strong> the totals (the last such line wins). This is the"
       & " footer"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "of the native <code>test_result.md</code>, so files with both rows and a foo"
       & "ter"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "report the footer"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s totals.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""tap-test-anything-protocol""><a class=""header"" href=""#tap-test-anythi"
       & "ng-protocol"">TAP (Test Anything Protocol)</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The protocol used by Perl"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <code>prove</code>/<code>Test::Harness</code> toolchain (also emitted"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "by many dynamic-language test frameworks):</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code>1..5"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "ok 1 - add works"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "not ok 2 - remove edge case"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "ok 3 - merge works"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "ok - unnamed pass"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "not ok - unnamed fail"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>ok ...</code> lines increment the passed counter.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>not ok ...</code> lines increment the failed counter.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>The <code>1..N</code> plan line and anything else are ignored.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""automake-test-suite""><a class=""header"" href=""#automake-test-suite"">A"
       & "utomake test-suite</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code>PASS:</code>/<code>FAIL:</code>/<code>SKIP:</code> lines emitte"
       & "d by GNU Automake"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <code>make check</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>testsuite.log</code> / <code>test-suite.log</code> style):</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code>PASS: basic"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "FAIL: edge case"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "SKIP: needs network"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>PASS:</code> increments passed; <code>FAIL:</code> increments fail"
       & "ed; <code>SKIP:</code> is ignored.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""maven-surefire""><a class=""header"" href=""#maven-surefire"">Maven Suref"
       & "ire</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The summary line of Maven"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s Surefire JUnit runner ("
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "Tests run:"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " line from"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the console/log output):</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code>Tests run: 5, Failures: 1, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0, Time elapsed: 0"
       & ".1 s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Failed = Failures + Errors; passed = Tests run - failed. The last summary"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "line wins.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""unity""><a class=""header"" href=""#unity"">Unity</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The summary line of the <a href=""https://github.com/ThrowTheSwitch/Unity"""
       & ">Unity</a> C"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "test framework:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code>-----------------------"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "5 Tests 1 Failures 0 Ignored"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "OK"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Failed = Failures; passed = Tests - Failures. The <code>N Failures</code>"
       & " count may be"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "separated from the number by spaces.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""aunit-ada""><a class=""header"" href=""#aunit-ada"">AUnit (Ada)</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>AdaCore"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s AUnit runner output "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " either its tabular report (the indexed"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>| N | Category | Count | PASS |</code> layout with a leading index or "
       & "<code>-</code> cell,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "including the optional <code>Passed:</code>/<code>Failed:</code> footer) or "
       & "a Markdown table with"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the same columns. Both are handled by the generic Markdown-table parser"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "above; AUnit report lines that match TAP/Automake patterns are additionally"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "accepted.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""usage""><a class=""header"" href=""#usage"">Usage</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The parser (<code>Adacovex.Parsers.Tests.Parse_Test_Result</code>) reads "
       & "from a file;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Parse_Test_Stdout</code> reads from standard input. When no explicit f"
       & "ile is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "given, <code>Parse_Test_Result_From_Project</code> auto-discovers the test s"
       & "ummary in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the target project, trying conventional file names (<code>test_result.md</co"
       & "de>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>test_results.md</code>, <code>test-result.md</code>, <code>test_report"
       & ".md</code>, <code>test_output.md</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>.txt</code>/<code>.log</code> variants, and <code>docs/</code> mirrors"
       & ") in order.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code class=""language-bash""># Parse a test result file"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "adacovex --target=../Ada_CRDT"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "# The parser auto-discovers test_result.md (or any conventional variant) fro"
       & "m the target project"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""see-also""><a class=""header"" href=""#see-also"">See also</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><a href=""../target-projects.html"">Target projects</a> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the test-summary file"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "auto-discovery rules and missing-data behaviour</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><a href=""adacovex-parsers-tests.html"">Test parser API</a> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>Adacovex.Parsers.Tests</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><a href=""adacovex-dal-levels.html"">DAL Levels</a> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " how the passing-tests criterion"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "feeds the compliance assessment</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
