       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""adacovex-architecture-decisions""><a class=""h"
       & "eader"" href=""#adacovex-architecture-decisions"">adacovex Architecture Decisio"
       & "ns</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""dependency-management-alire""><a class=""header"" href=""#dependency-man"
       & "agement-alire"">Dependency Management: Alire</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex uses <a href=""https://alire.ada.dev/"">Alire</a> as its packaging"
       & " and delivery mechanism. The publishing manifest <code>alire.toml</code> dec"
       & "lares <strong>zero dependencies</strong>. It declares no libraries beyond th"
       & "e GNAT runtime. It declares no tool dependencies.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>In particular <code>gnatprove</code> is <em>not</em> a declared dependenc"
       & "y. adacovex analyses <code>gnatprove.out</code> files produced externally. T"
       & "he <code>prove</code> subcommand resolves a gnatprove executable at run time"
       & " (per-project manifest, <code>$PATH</code>, cached toolchain, or download). "
       & "Development-only tools (<code>gnatprove</code>, <code>gnatdoc_bin</code>, <c"
       & "ode>gnatformat_bin</code>) are declared in <code>alire-dev.toml</code>, whic"
       & "h is never published to the Alire community index.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""manifest-distinction-aliretoml-vs-alire-devtoml""><a class=""header"" h"
       & "ref=""#manifest-distinction-aliretoml-vs-alire-devtoml"">Manifest distinction "
       & "(<code>alire.toml</code> vs <code>alire-dev.toml</code>)</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong><code>alire.toml</code></strong>: The clean publishing manifest."
       & " Declares no dependencies at"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "all, so <code>alr install covex</code> (or <code>alr build</code> from sourc"
       & "e) pulls nothing beyond"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the binary and the GNAT compiler. Used for SBOM generation and dependency"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "graph scanning.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong><code>alire-dev.toml</code></strong>: The development manifest. "
       & "Extends <code>alire.toml</code> with"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dev-only tools (<code>gnatprove</code>, <code>gnatdoc_bin</code>, <code>gnat"
       & "format_bin</code>) needed for"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>make prove</code>, <code>make doc</code>, and <code>make fmt</code>. U"
       & "sed for toolchain resolution when"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "running <code>alr exec</code>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>When both files exist, <code>Build_Dependency_Graph</code> reads <strong>"
       & "both</strong>: a dependency"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "declared in <code>alire.toml</code> is classified <code>Scope_Base</code> (e"
       & "xplicit/clean dep) and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "one declared only in <code>alire-dev.toml</code> is <code>Scope_Dev</code>. "
       & "The scope is surfaced in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the SBOM as the <code>adacovex:dep_scope</code> property (<code>base</code> "
       & "/ <code>dev</code> / <code>transitive</code> /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>vendored</code>), so it is always clear which file a dependency came f"
       & "rom."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>alire-dev.toml</code> is also consulted for gnatprove detection"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>Manifest_Declares_GNATprove</code> checks both manifests).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""gnatprove-toolchain-resolution-prove-subcommand""><a class=""header"" h"
       & "ref=""#gnatprove-toolchain-resolution-prove-subcommand"">GNATprove toolchain r"
       & "esolution (<code>prove</code> subcommand)</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex declares <code>gnatprove</code> only in its own <code>alire-dev."
       & "toml</code> (keeping the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "publishing <code>alire.toml</code> clean). The <code>prove</code> subcommand"
       & " resolves the <code>gnatprove</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "executable in this order:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Per-project manifest (authoritative)</strong>: if <code>&lt;targ"
       & "et&gt;/alire.toml</code> /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>&lt;target&gt;/alire-dev.toml</code> declares a <code>gnatprove</code>"
       & " dependency, the pinned"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "gnatprove binary crate is deployed standalone into <code>~/.adacovex/toolcha"
       & "in/</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "via <code>alr -n get gnatprove=&lt;version&gt;</code> and executed directly "
       & "(the version-set"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "expression, for example <code>^16.1.0</code>, is reduced to the bare version"
       & " alr"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "accepts). This isolates the proof run from the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s other dev-manifest"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tools and never swaps manifests. A manifest pin always wins. When the pinned"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "version cannot be deployed, the run fails instead of falling back.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Global version pin</strong>: the <code>ADACOVEX_GNATPROVE_VERSIO"
       & "N</code> environment"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "variable or the <code>[prove] gnatprove-version</code> key in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>~/.adacovex/adacovex.toml</code>, deployed standalone via"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>alr -n get gnatprove=&lt;version&gt;</code>. It uses the same never-fa"
       & "ll-back"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "semantics. It is folded into the proof result-cache identity.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong><code>$PATH</code></strong>: a <code>gnatprove</code> already in"
       & "stalled (for example <code>alr install gnatprove</code>).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Cached toolchain</strong>: <code>~/.adacovex/toolchain/</code>. "
       & "The download layout"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>&lt;toolchain&gt;/bin/gnatprove</code>) is used. A previously <code>a"
       & "lr get</code>-deployed"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>gnatprove_*/</code> crate is also used.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Download</strong>: last-resort platform toolchain bundle.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Effective order: <strong>manifest pin &gt; global pin (config/env) &gt; P"
       & "ATH &gt; cache &gt;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "download</strong>. If a project manifest declares <code>gnatprove</code> but"
       & " <code>alr</code> is missing,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "install Alire first. The remaining fallbacks then apply.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code>make doc</code> / <code>make fmt</code> targets still swap <cod"
       & "e>alire-dev.toml</code> over"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>alire.toml</code> for the duration of <code>gnatdoc</code> / <code>gna"
       & "tformat</code> (the <code>_dev_cmd</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Makefile recipe backs up <code>alire.toml</code> / <code>alire.lock</code> /"
       & " <code>alire/</code>, swaps, runs,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and restores via a <code>trap</code>). <code>prove</code> does not use that "
       & "swap. It deploys only"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the single gnatprove crate.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The assessment and SBOM pipeline always scans the publishing <code>alire."
       & "toml</code>, so"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dev-only tool declarations never leak into dependency graphs or SBOMs.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""system-tool-dev-dependencies-sbom""><a class=""header"" href=""#system-t"
       & "ool-dev-dependencies-sbom"">System-tool dev dependencies (SBOM)</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Beyond the Alire graph, <code>Discover_System_Dev_Deps</code> adds the sy"
       & "stem binaries a project interacts with at development time (<code>python3</c"
       & "ode>, <code>git</code>, <code>gnatprove</code>, <code>make</code>, and more)"
       & " as <code>Scope_Dev</code> SBOM components. It scans the project"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s dev-facing files (Makefile variants, <code>.sh</code> / <code>.py</code> /"
       & " <code>.gpr</code> / <code>.yml</code> / <code>.toml</code> / <code>.ads</co"
       & "de> / <code>.adb</code>) for a curated toolchain list and registers every re"
       & "ferenced tool that is actually installed on <code>$PATH</code> under a <code"
       & ">pkg:generic/&lt;tool&gt;</code> purl. Tools referenced nowhere in the proje"
       & "ct, or referenced but not installed, are skipped. A Makefile at the project "
       & "root implies <code>make</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The scan runs after the cached manifest graph is resolved (so cache hits "
       & "and misses agree). Each registered tool"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s version is probed by running <code>--version</code> (or a tool-specific su"
       & "bcommand such as fossil"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <code>version</code>) and extracting the version token, so the SBOM record"
       & "s the installed version. A probe that fails or prints no digit token leaves "
       & "the version empty. The source file declaring the <code>System_Tools</code> t"
       & "able is skipped by the scan.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Otherwise, every installed tool on the list can be registered as a self-r"
       & "eference.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""vendored-components-and-test-labelled-dependencies-sbom""><a class=""h"
       & "eader"" href=""#vendored-components-and-test-labelled-dependencies-sbom"">Vendo"
       & "red components and test-labelled dependencies (SBOM)</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>Discover_Generic_Vendored</code> walks the target tree for vendor r"
       & "oots"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>node_modules</code>, <code>vendor</code>, <code>third_party</code>, a"
       & "nd the other recognised names)."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Each directory inside a vendor root that carries an ecosystem manifest"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>package.json</code>, <code>Cargo.toml</code>, <code>go.mod</code>, <c"
       & "ode>pyproject.toml</code>, <code>composer.json</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Gemfile</code>, <code>pom.xml</code>, <code>Package.swift</code>, <cod"
       & "e>requirements*.txt</code>) becomes one"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "component with its ecosystem purl (<code>pkg:npm/...</code>, <code>pkg:cargo"
       & "/...</code>, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "more).  Its scope defaults to <code>vendored</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A component is classified <code>test</code> when the project manifest tha"
       & "t owns the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "vendor root declares it under a test-only label:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>package.json</code> sections whose key contains <code>test</code> "
       & "(for example"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>testDependencies</code>);</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Cargo <code>[dev-dependencies]</code> (Cargo"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s native test-only section) and any"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "section containing <code>test</code>;</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>composer <code>require-dev</code>;</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Gemfile <code>group :test</code> blocks;</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>pom.xml</code> dependencies whose <code>&lt;scope&gt;</code> is <c"
       & "ode>test</code>;</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>pyproject.toml</code> test extras and Poetry <code>[tool.poetry.gr"
       & "oup.test.*]</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "sections;</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>Package.swift</code> dependencies declared inside a <code>.testTar"
       & "get(...)</code> block.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <strong>name heuristic</strong> is the fallback for every ecosystem. "
       & " A component"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "whose name starts or ends with the literal word <code>test</code> is test-la"
       & "belled."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "The check covers the full name and then the last segment after any <code>/</"
       & "code> or"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>:</code>, so <code>@playwright/test</code>, <code>test-case</code>, <c"
       & "ode>github.com/stretchr/testify</code> and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>org.testng:testng</code> all match.  Ecosystems without a native test-"
       & "only"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "section (<code>go.mod</code>, <code>requirements*.txt</code>) rely on this h"
       & "euristic.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The heuristic also applies to <strong>lockfile-resolved names</strong>:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>pnpm-lock.yaml</code> / <code>package-lock.json</code> / <code>yarn.lo"
       & "ck</code> entries next to an"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "owner <code>package.json</code>, <code>Cargo.lock</code> crate names, and <c"
       & "ode>alire.lock</code> crates"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "that the manifest sets leave transitive.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The scope is surfaced as the SBOM <code>adacovex:dep_scope</code> propert"
       & "y (<code>test</code>)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and in the dashboard dependency badges, scope filter, legend, and rings."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "The Alire-side <code>[[test-depends-on]]</code> sections and test project fi"
       & "les are"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the other source of <code>test</code> scope; see the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a href=""sbom.html#test-dependencies"">SBOM reference</a>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""unix-philosophy""><a class=""header"" href=""#unix-philosophy"">Unix Phil"
       & "osophy</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex follows the Unix philosophy of doing one thing well:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Single-purpose pipeline</strong>: Each step (scanning, proof par"
       & "sing, test parsing, DAL assessment, rendering) is a focused, composable unit"
       & ".</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Text-based interfaces</strong>: Input and output are plain text "
       & "(Ada source, <code>.out</code> files, Markdown reports, ANSI terminal output"
       & ").</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>No library dependencies</strong>: Only the GNAT runtime is used."
       & " No external"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "libraries or frameworks. Alire is the packaging/delivery mechanism but adds"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "no runtime dependency. adacovex declares no library or tool dependencies"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(gnatprove is resolved at run time by the <code>prove</code> subcommand).</l"
       & "i>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Composable tools</strong>: The <code>prove</code> subcommand run"
       & "s GNATprove and then falls through to the standard assessment pipeline. The "
       & "<code>sbom</code> subcommand generates a proof-aware SBOM independently.</li"
       & ">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Exit codes</strong>: <code>0</code> for success (DAL achieved), "
       & "<code>1</code> for compliance failure. This enables straightforward CI integ"
       & "ration.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Minimal user code</strong>: users write as little code as possib"
       & "le while getting"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "maximum value. The tool accepts third-party and generated code as it is. It "
       & "recognises common docstring conventions (Ada <code>--  @param</code>, Google"
       & " <code>Args:</code>/<code>Returns:</code>, Sphinx <code>:param:</code>/<code"
       & ">:returns:</code>). It recognises common test-result formats (TAP, Automake,"
       & " Surefire, Unity).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>It lowers foreign type names (<code>int32_t</code>, <code>size_t</code>, "
       & "and more) onto bounded Ada types. Nothing needs to be rewritten to be assess"
       & "ed.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""zero-library-dependency-design""><a class=""header"" href=""#zero-librar"
       & "y-dependency-design"">Zero-Library-Dependency Design</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex declares no library dependencies beyond the GNAT runtime. All da"
       & "ta structures use either:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>GNAT runtime containers (<code>Ada.Containers.Vectors</code> for unbound"
       & "ed collections)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Fixed-size string buffers (<code>Max_Line = 262144</code>, <code>Max_Pat"
       & "h = 4096</code>, etc.) for bounded I/O</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>Max_Path</code> and <code>Max_Line</code> scale with the auto-detec"
       & "ted host word size"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>System.Word_Size</code>), keeping the classic 4096 / 262144 values on"
       & " 64-bit"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "hosts while using proportionally smaller limits on narrower machines. The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "semantic limits (<code>Max_Id_Str</code>, <code>Max_Desc_Str</code>, <code>M"
       & "ax_Filename</code>) are not"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "storage-size dependent and remain fixed.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>Max_Line</code> is deliberately generous (256 KiB on 64-bit) so tha"
       & "t single-line declarations from heavily code-generated projects parse cleanl"
       & "y. When a physical line <em>does</em> exceed the buffer, adacovex <strong>ne"
       & "ver truncates it and then processes it</strong>. Truncation can silently pro"
       & "duce a partial (and wrong) result. Instead the parser drains the remainder, "
       & "reports the file and line to standard error, and fails that parse explicitly"
       & ".</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The source scanner counts the skipped file in <code>Skipped_Ct</code>, wh"
       & "ich forces the DAL assessment to <code>Unmet</code> and the exit code to <co"
       & "de>1</code> (no compliance claim can be made for unread code). The same expl"
       & "icit-failure contract applies to every parser: HLR/LLR markdown, GNATprove o"
       & "utput (text and JSON), test results, and Alire manifest / lockfile / GPR dep"
       & "endency graphs. An exact buffer-length line is not an overflow (it parses no"
       & "rmally), and paths exceeding <code>Max_Path</code> are likewise reported and"
       & " skipped rather than crashing.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>Overflow contract (two tiers).</strong> Path and line buffers <em"
       & ">fail loudly</em>. An"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "overlong physical line is drained and reported (<code>line exceeds Max_Line "
       & "buffer</code>). The file is not parsed. <code>Skipped_Ct</code> increments. "
       & "DAL becomes <code>Unmet</code>. An overlong path is reported and the file/su"
       & "btree is skipped.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>No partial results ever flow downstream. Semantic text fields (subprogram"
       & " names, HLR/LLR IDs, descriptions, docstring tag names/values, CLI strings) "
       & "are</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><em>clamped</em> to their fixed buffer with the length field (<code>Name_"
       & "Len</code>, <code>Id_Len</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>D_Len</code>, "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(166)
       & ") recording the recorded prefix, so adversarial or generated"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "input can never raise <code>Constraint_Error</code>. Clamping keeps the scan"
       & " correct."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "The full token is still consumed so following tokens are not misparsed.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>Why no chunking / LEB128.</strong> adacovex audits in memory. Cou"
       & "nts (packages,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "subprograms, HLR tags, tests, SBOM components) are unbounded vectors. Each s"
       & "canned unit is processed line-at-a-time into fixed per-item buffers. A singl"
       & "e Ada declaration does not admit streaming/chunked parsing. Truncating a dec"
       & "laration is worse than a loud failure.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Chunking can gain nothing. LEB128 (variable-length integer encoding) is a"
       & " serialization concern and does not apply to an in-memory CLI audit. The des"
       & "ign therefore scales to arbitrarily large codebases by dynamic allocation, b"
       & "ounded per-item buffers, and explicit overflow handling, without streaming e"
       & "ncodings.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The bounded-buffer constants are tabulated in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>docs/api-docs/adacovex-types.md</code> (<code>Max_Line</code>, <code>M"
       & "ax_Path</code>, <code>Max_Desc_Str</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Max_Filename</code>, <code>Max_Id_Str</code>).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>This ensures adacovex can be built and run on any system with a GNAT tool"
       & "chain,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "without requiring any additional package installation beyond Alire for"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "toolchain management.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""spark-formal-verification""><a class=""header"" href=""#spark-formal-ver"
       & "ification"">SPARK Formal Verification</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex itself is SPARK-proven at Platinum level (all VCs proved,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "AoRTE-free). The tool analyses GNATprove output (<code>gnatprove.out</code>)"
       & " to assess"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "SPARK assurance levels (Stone through Platinum) for target projects.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The tool does not perform verification itself. It parses and reports on p"
       & "roof"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "results produced by GNATprove. This keeps the tool"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s scope narrow and aligns"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "with the Unix philosophy of composing specialised tools.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""proof-scope-and-justification-policy""><a class=""header"" href=""#proof"
       & "-scope-and-justification-policy"">Proof scope and justification policy</a></h"
       & "3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Proof scope is the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s own units.</strong> adacovex proves the Ada/SPARK"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "code it is run against, never third-party dependencies. GNATprove units that"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "are skipped (for example standard-library or vendor code that GNATprove"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "itself does not analyse) are tracked via <code>Units_Skipped</code> and repo"
       & "rted in the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "ANSI and Markdown reports. They are out of proof scope by design, not a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "proof failure.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Justifications are an accepted discharge mechanism.</strong> A <"
       & "code>Total</code> row"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Justified</code> count (GNATprove <code>pragma Annotate</code> justifi"
       & "cations for decidedly"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "unprovable checks, such as non-functional foreign-language calls) is counted"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "neither as proved nor as unproved: <code>Proved = Total - Justified - Unprov"
       & "ed</code>."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Justified VCs do <strong>not</strong> downgrade the SPARK level. Only unprov"
       & "ed VCs do."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "This is pinned by unit tests.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Gold is the minimum compliance baseline. Platinum is the ideal.<"
       & "/strong>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Min_SPARK_For</code> thresholds (A=Gold, B=Silver, C=Bronze, D/E=Stone"
       & ") are the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "gate for DAL compliance. Platinum is achieved and reported when every"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "functional contract is proved, but it is a best-effort target, not a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "compliance requirement at any DAL level.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""ir-synthesiser""><a class=""header"" href=""#ir-synthesiser"">IR Synthesi"
       & "ser</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code>src/ir/</code> layer starts an intermediate representation for"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cross-compilation assessments, so the tool can reason about types as they"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "exist on a target rather than only as they appear in Ada source:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>Adacovex.Target_Profiles</code> defines bounded machine-integer ty"
       & "pes"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>IR_Int8</code>..<code>IR_Int64</code>, <code>IR_UInt8</code>..<code>I"
       & "R_UInt64</code>) with <code>Size</code> clauses and a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Target_Config</code> record (host/target/pointer word sizes). The type"
       & "s are"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "SPARK-proved: <code>Checked_Add32</code> / <code>Checked_Add64</code> show o"
       & "verflow is detected,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "not undefined.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>Adacovex.IR_Synthesiser</code> lowers foreign type names (<code>in"
       & "t8_t</code>, <code>size_t</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>usize</code>, <code>ptrdiff_t</code>, "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(166)
       & ") onto the bounded IR types and synthesizes"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "package declarations from a comma/whitespace-separated type list.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>Adacovex.IR_Bounds</code> is a gnatprove fixture deriving synthesi"
       & "zed-style"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>int32_t</code> / <code>int64_t</code> types and proving their <code>Ad"
       & "d32</code> / <code>Add64</code> overflow"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "checks, so absence of integer overflow on the lowered types is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "machine-checked.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""do-178c-dal-compliance""><a class=""header"" href=""#do-178c-dal-complia"
       & "nce"">DO-178C DAL Compliance</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The DAL assessment evaluates four criteria:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>All HLRs defined in <code>docs/compliance/HLR.md</code> are traced by <c"
       & "ode>-- HLR-XXXX</code> tags in source</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>No orphan tags (every in-source HLR maps to a defined HLR)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>All tests passing (zero failures in <code>test_result.md</code>)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Minimum SPARK proof level met (varies by DAL level)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>DAL-C is the default target level. Higher levels (A, B) require stricter "
       & "proof levels (Gold, Silver respectively).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""source-scanning""><a class=""header"" href=""#source-scanning"">Source Sc"
       & "anning</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The scanner walks the target directory tree, skipping always-excluded dir"
       & "ectories (<code>.git</code>, <code>obj</code>, <code>tests</code>, <code>con"
       & "fig</code>, <code>.adacovex</code>). For each <code>.ads</code> file found, "
       & "it extracts:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Package name from filename</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Subprogram declarations (<code>procedure</code>, <code>function</code>, "
       & "<code>generic procedure</code>, <code>generic function</code>, and <code>ove"
       & "rriding</code> / <code>not overriding</code> variants)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Docstring annotations (<code>--  </code> prefix with optional <code>@par"
       & "am</code>, <code>@return</code>, <code>@field</code>, <code>@formal</code> t"
       & "ags, plus Google <code>Args:</code>/<code>Returns:</code> blocks and Sphinx "
       & "<code>:param:</code>/<code>:returns:</code> fields)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>HLR traceability tags (<code>-- HLR-XXXX</code>)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>In strict mode (default), the scanner also applies docstring patches from"
       & " <code>.adacovex/patches/</code> to document vendored/third-party code witho"
       & "ut modifying the originals.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""patch-system""><a class=""header"" href=""#patch-system"">Patch System</a"
       & "></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code>.adacovex/patches/</code> directory overlays docstring informat"
       & "ion onto"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "third-party or vendored code that cannot be modified directly, so strict mod"
       & "e"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "can still reach 100% docstring coverage without touching the originals.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""why-patches-exist""><a class=""header"" href=""#why-patches-exist"">Why p"
       & "atches exist</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>In strict mode (default), all directories except <code>.git</code>, <code"
       & ">obj</code>, <code>tests</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>config</code>, and <code>.adacovex</code> are scanned. Vendored depend"
       & "encies (for example a copy of"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "vt100 in <code>demo/deps/vt100/</code>) are scanned, and their undocumented "
       & "subprograms"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "count against docstring coverage. Patches document them in place.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""patch-file-format""><a class=""header"" href=""#patch-file-format"">Patch"
       & " file format</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A patch file is a valid Ada <code>.ads</code> file containing only the su"
       & "bprogram"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "declarations to document, each preceded by a docstring:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code class=""language-ada"">--  Package-level comment (optional, not use"
       & "d by patch engine)."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "package VT100 is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   --  Summary of the procedure."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   --  @param Name  Description."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   procedure Some_Procedure (Name : in Some_Type);"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   --  Another procedure with no params."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   procedure No_Param_Proc;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "end VT100;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Rules:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>File name must match the original <code>.ads</code> (for example <code>v"
       & "t100.ads</code>).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Subprogram names must match the originals exactly.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Only subprograms with preceding docstrings (<code>--  </code> lines) are"
       & " merged.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Overloaded subprograms: one patch entry per overload. Each patches the n"
       & "ext"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "undocumented original with the same name.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>The scanner merges <code>Has_Docstring</code>, <code>Doc_Param_Ct</code>"
       & ", and <code>Doc_Return</code> into"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the matching originals.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""patch-file-location""><a class=""header"" href=""#patch-file-location"">P"
       & "atch file location</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code>&lt;target-project&gt;/.adacovex/patches/&lt;relative-path&gt;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>&lt;relative-path&gt;</code> is the path from the target root to th"
       & "e <code>.ads</code> file. Example:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "to patch <code>Ada_CRDT/demo/deps/vt100/vt100.ads</code>, create"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Ada_CRDT/.adacovex/patches/demo/deps/vt100/vt100.ads</code>. The <code"
       & ">.adacovex</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "directory is always excluded from source scanning.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""proof-patches-spark-contracts-over-vendored-dependencies""><a class="""
       & "header"" href=""#proof-patches-spark-contracts-over-vendored-dependencies"">Pro"
       & "of patches: SPARK contracts over vendored dependencies</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The same <code>.adacovex/patches/&lt;relative-path&gt;</code> file can ca"
       & "rry <strong>SPARK proof aspects</strong> in addition to docstrings, so vendo"
       & "red dependencies participate in the SPARK proof without modifying their sour"
       & "ces. A patch file that includes any of <code>SPARK_Mode</code>, <code>Pre =&"
       & "gt;</code>, <code>Post =&gt;</code>, or <code>Global =&gt;</code> (detected "
       & "by <code>Adacovex. Prove_Patch. Has_Proof</code>) is a <em>proof patch</em>."
       & "</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A patch with only docstrings remains a docstring overlay and never engage"
       & "s the proof machinery. This section is the design. For the user-facing guide"
       & " "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " how proving works, writing SPARK contracts, and the <code>.ads</code>/<code"
       & ">.adb</code> patch files with worked examples and pitfalls "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " see <a href=""proving.html"">Proving and writing proofs</a>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code class=""language-ada"">package VT100 with SPARK_Mode =&gt; On is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   --  Scroll a region of the screen up."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   --  @param From  Starting line of scroll region."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   --  @param To    Ending line of scroll region."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   procedure Scroll_Screen (From : in Natural; To : in Natural)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "     with Pre =&gt; From &lt;= To;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "end VT100;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code>prove</code> subcommand merges proof patches before running gna"
       & "tprove:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>Count_Proof_Patches</code> scans <code>&lt;target&gt;/.adacovex/pa"
       & "tches/</code> (<code>.ads</code> and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>.adb</code> patch files). A target with no proof patches is proved aga"
       & "inst"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "its own tree exactly as before.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>Build_Patched_Copy</code> copies the target tree (excluding <code>"
       & ".git</code>, <code>obj</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and <code>.adacovex</code>) into <code>&lt;target&gt;/obj/adacovex-proof/</c"
       & "ode> and overwrites each proof-patched source with its merged form "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " package-level aspects spliced onto the package declaration line (for a <cod"
       & "e>package body ... is</code> declaration too), and each aspect-carrying subp"
       & "rogram declaration replaced by the patch"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s declaration block. The merge matches on name <strong>and</strong> normalis"
       & "ed parameter profile (<code>Param_Profile</code>), so an overloaded subprogr"
       & "am patches its exact signature and never a same-named sibling. The default <"
       & "code>in</code> mode is equivalent to a bare mode. <code>in out</code> and <c"
       & "ode>out</code> are distinct. A spec declaration terminates at its <code>;</c"
       & "ode>, a body declaration at its <code>is</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " so a patched body declaration is replaced without touching the body proper."
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The original vendored sources are never touched.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ol start=""3"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>gnatprove runs against the copy"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s root project (<code>&lt;copy&gt;/&lt;basename&gt;.gpr</code>)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and the resulting <code>gnatprove.out</code> is copied back to"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>&lt;target&gt;/obj/gnatprove/gnatprove.out</code> for the assessment p"
       & "ipeline. The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "copy lives under the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <code>obj/</code>, so it is excluded from scanning,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "manifest graphs, and the prove input hash.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Proof-patch contents are folded into the prove result-cache key, so a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "patch edit invalidates the cached proof and forces a re-prove.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""the-two-patch-shapes""><a class=""header"" href=""#the-two-patch-shapes"""
       & ">The two patch shapes</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A <strong>spec patch</strong> (<code>.ads</code> in the patch directory) "
       & "re-declares the vendored"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "spec with contracts, exactly as the VT100 example above. gnatprove analyses"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "a unit"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s body only when the <em>body itself</em> opts in (<code>SPARK_Mode =&gt; On"
       & "</code> on"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the package body or a subprogram body), so a SPARK-clean vendored body also"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "needs a <strong>body patch</strong> (<code>.adb</code> in the patch director"
       & "y) that declares the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "intended mode. The body patch mirrors the body"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s declarations with stub"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "bodies that the merge ignores "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the original body proper is preserved:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code class=""language-ada"">--  .adacovex/patches/demo/deps/vecmath/vecm"
       & "ath.adb"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "package body Vecmath with SPARK_Mode =&gt; On is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   function Clamp (Value : in Integer; Lo : in Integer; Hi : in Integer)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "     return Integer with SPARK_Mode =&gt; On is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   begin"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "      null;  --  stub: replaced by the original body's implementation"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   end Clamp;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "end Vecmath;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A worked example end to end: a vendored <code>Vecmath.Clamp</code> whose "
       & "original"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "spec and body carry no contracts, with the spec patch above declaring"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>SPARK_Mode =&gt; On</code> plus <code>Pre =&gt; Lo &lt;= Hi, Post =&gt"
       & "; Clamp'Result in Lo .. Hi</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and the body patch opting the body into the proof. The merged copy is what"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "gnatprove sees "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>package body Vecmath with SPARK_Mode =&gt; On is</code> with the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "original <code>if Value &lt; Lo ... return Value</code> implementation intac"
       & "t "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " and the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "contracts prove: 2 VCs (the <code>Clamp</code> postcondition and its termina"
       & "tion"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "check), 0 unproved.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Where the vendored body is SPARK-clean and opted in via a body patch,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "gnatprove proves the patched contracts. Where it is not (for example bodies"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "that call <code>Ada.Text_IO</code>, which is <code>SPARK_Mode Off</code>), g"
       & "natprove skips the I/O"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "bodies by design and reports the unit out of proof scope "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " a proof patch"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "never drags the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s proof level down. The Ada_CRDT dogfood target"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "proves the mechanism end to end: its"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>.adacovex/patches/demo/deps/vt100/vt100.ads</code> declares <code>SPAR"
       & "K_Mode =&gt; On</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "on the vendored package and pins the <code>Scroll_Screen</code> scroll-regio"
       & "n"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "contract (its bodies are Text_IO-bound, so gnatprove skips them by design),"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and <code>make run-ada-crdt</code> / Ada_CRDT"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <code>make prove</code> run through the patched"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "copy, preserving the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s proof.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""output-formats""><a class=""header"" href=""#output-formats"">Output Form"
       & "ats</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex supports multiple output formats:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>ANSI terminal report</strong>: Colour-coded summary for interacti"
       & "ve use."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Colour is suppressed under CI, <code>NO_COLOR</code>, or <code>TERM=dumb</co"
       & "de>, so CI logs"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "stay plain (see <code>Adacovex.Ansi</code> and its pure decision function"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Colour_Allowed</code>)</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>SVG badges</strong>: <code>spark.svg</code>, <code>tests.svg</cod"
       & "e>, <code>docs.svg</code>, plus <code>do178c.svg</code> /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>iso26262.svg</code> / <code>iec62304.svg</code> compliance badges (<co"
       & "de>--standard=all</code> emits all"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "three) for CI badges</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>Markdown reports</strong>: <code>VERIFICATION.md</code> and <code"
       & ">TRACE.md</code> for compliance documentation</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
