       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""result-caching""><a class=""header"" href=""#result-caching"">Result cach"
       & "ing</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex persists parsed analysis results on disk so unchanged inputs are"
       & " not re-scanned, re-parsed, or re-proved. Source scans, GNATprove summaries,"
       & " test summaries, HLR.md/LLR.md requirement parses, the resolved SBOM depende"
       & "ncy graph, and the differential-mode scans are each keyed by a namespace pre"
       & "fix plus the SHA-256 of the artifact(s) they were derived from. For example:"
       & " <code>""scan:"" | ""prove:"" | ""tests:"" | ""hlr:"" | ""llr:"" | ""graph:"" + digest</"
       & "code>. Re-parsing a byte-identical artifact yields a cache hit regardless of"
       & " the target directory or command line.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>An unchanged manifest/lockfile/.gpr set serves the cached dependency grap"
       & "h. Unchanged HLR.md/LLR.md serve the cached requirement parses. <code>--comp"
       & "are-base</code> / <code>--coverage-delta</code> reuse cached source scans fo"
       & "r the current tree.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Schema namespace</strong>: the default cache root is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>~/.adacovex/cache/&lt;version&gt;/&lt;Cache_Schema&gt;</code>. <code>C"
       & "ache_Schema</code> (in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>src/core/adacovex-cache.ads</code>) is bumped whenever the serialized "
       & "layout of a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cached record or the scanner/parser semantics change, so blobs written by an"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "incompatible build are never served as if valid. System-tool version probes"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "are <em>not</em> under the result cache: they live in <code>~/.adacovex/prob"
       & "es/</code> (a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "stable machine-level store; wiping the result cache must not re-probe every"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tool).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Graph key</strong>: the dependency-graph key hashes the Alire ma"
       & "nifests, the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>alire.lock</code>, every <code>.gpr</code>, the vendored trees, and th"
       & "e root language mix."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "It also hashes the supported-language project manifests that can own a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "vendored directory (<code>package.json</code>, <code>Cargo.toml</code>, <cod"
       & "e>Cargo.lock</code>, <code>go.mod</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>composer.json</code>, <code>Gemfile</code>, <code>pom.xml</code>, <cod"
       & "e>pyproject.toml</code>, <code>Package.swift</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and the npm lockfiles), so an edit to a test-labelled section or lockfile"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "invalidates the cached graph and the scope classification is recomputed.</li"
       & ">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Eviction</strong>: <code>Put_Cached</code> evicts oldest-first b"
       & "y modification time when more"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "than <code>--cache-max</code> entries (default <code>4096</code>) accumulate"
       & ". <code>Eviction_Count</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tracks removals and is reported in the ANSI cache line.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Overflow safety</strong>: <code>Serialize</code> returns an empt"
       & "y blob when a package is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "larger than <code>Max_Cache_Blob</code>. Callers skip storing it and <code>D"
       & "eserialize</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "rejects empty/oversized input, so truncated data can never be served as a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "hit.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong><code>--target</code> normalization</strong>: <code>--target</co"
       & "de> is normalised (<code>.</code>/<code>..</code> collapsed to"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "a canonical absolute path) before scanning, keeping the <code>File_Path</cod"
       & "e> values in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cached <code>Package_Info</code> consistent across invocations that spell th"
       & "e same"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "directory differently.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>CI</strong>: the GitHub action persists <code>~/.adacovex/cache<"
       & "/code> between workflow runs"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>result-cache</code> input, default true).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>--no-cache</code> bypasses it entirely (useful when artifacts chang"
       & "e without their"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "content hash changing, or to measure rescan cost) and <code>--cache-dir</cod"
       & "e> relocates"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "it. The ANSI report shows a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>result cache: X hit(s), Y miss(es), Z evicted</code> line per run.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""testing""><a class=""header"" href=""#testing"">Testing</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex uses a native zero-dependency test framework (<code>Adacovex.Tes"
       & "t_Support</code>) with 1173 tests across 16 categories. No external test fra"
       & "mework (AUnit, and more) is required. Test results are written to <code>docs"
       & "/test_result.md</code> in a parseable Markdown table format.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""complexity-check""><a class=""header"" href=""#complexity-check"">Complex"
       & "ity check</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code>complexity</code> subcommand walks the whole target and scores "
       & "many languages"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(C, C++, C#, Go, Java, JavaScript, TypeScript, Python, Ruby, PHP, Rust,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Shell, Kotlin, and the YAML/JSON/TOML/XML/Markdown/reStructuredText"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "families) alongside Ada.  Per-subprogram analysis stays Ada-specific; the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "other languages contribute file-level lines of code and decision counts."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>--excludes=EXT,EXT</code> skips listed file extensions and is rejected"
       & " unless the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>complexity</code> subcommand is given, so it can never run on its own."
       & "  <code>make complexity-check</code> gates the tree through the same thresho"
       & "lds.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""timezone-resolution""><a class=""header"" href=""#timezone-resolution"">T"
       & "imezone resolution</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex honours the operating system"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s timezone by default.  The resolved"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "offset comes from <code>Ada.Calendar.Time_Zones.UTC_Time_Offset</code>, the "
       & "standard"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Ada runtime, which reads the <code>TZ</code> variable and the system timezon"
       & "e through"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the C library, so the default is always the operator"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s wall clock"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(DST-aware).  <code>status</code> reports the effective timezone, the curren"
       & "t date and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "time in it, and how many dated release changelogs the target carries under"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>docs/changelogs</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>--tz</code> / <code>--timezone</code> override the display zone for"
       & " one invocation.  The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "value is either a well-known IANA name (for example <code>Asia/Singapore</co"
       & "de>) or a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "fixed <code>UTC</code>/<code>GMT</code> offset (<code>UTC+8</code>, <code>GM"
       & "T+8</code>, <code>UTC+08</code>, <code>GMT+08</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>UTC+08:30</code>).  adacovex ships no timezone database, so a named zo"
       & "ne"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "resolves from a built-in table of common IANA names and their standard-time"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "offsets.  A zone that may observe daylight saving time (marked in the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "table), or one the table lacks, is probed against the platform tzdata"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>zdump</code> validates the name, <code>date +%z</code> reads the curr"
       & "ent offset, both"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "through one shell command) for the DST-correct offset; the table offset is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the fallback when the probe is unavailable.  The date/time rendering"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "compensates for GNAT"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s local-time calendar accessors, so the displayed wall"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "clock is correct in every zone.  <code>HLR-TZ</code> covers this behaviour.<"
       & "/p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""build-and-documentation-gates""><a class=""header"" href=""#build-and-do"
       & "cumentation-gates"">Build and documentation gates</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Two cheap Python gates keep the dashboard and the hand-written docs in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "step with the code, and both run inside <code>make check</code>:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>tools/csslint.py</code> (<code>make csslint-check</code>) enforces"
       & " the dashboard spacing"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "convention: every <code>margin</code>, <code>padding</code>, and <code>gap</"
       & "code> pixel length is a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "multiple of 4px.  It also runs inside <code>make build</code>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>tools/check-docs.py</code> (<code>make docs-check</code>) fails wh"
       & "en any paragraph in the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "user docs, README, or human changelogs exceeds four sentences, and it"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "rejects em dashes and Latin abbreviations (<code>i.e.</code>, <code>e.g.</co"
       & "de>, <code>etc.</code>)."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>tools/para-split.py</code> rewraps over-long paragraphs to comply.</li"
       & ">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The generated <code>docs/api-docs</code> pages are excluded from the para"
       & "graph rule;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "its source docstrings carry the same rule.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""supported-platforms""><a class=""header"" href=""#supported-platforms"">S"
       & "upported Platforms</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex supports the same platforms Alire itself supports. Because Alire"
       & " is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the packaging and delivery mechanism, adacovex inherits Alire"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "supported-platform matrix. The crate builds via <code>alr build</code>. It i"
       & "s distributed"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "through the Alire community index (<code>alr install covex</code>). The rele"
       & "ase workflow"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "builds it with the Alire toolchain:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Binary distribution</strong>: Linux x86-64, Windows x86-64, and "
       & "macOS x86-64"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(the platforms for which Alire publishes binary releases and GNAT FSF"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "toolchains, including cross compilers for ARM, RISC-V, and AVR).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>From source</strong>: any platform with a GNAT FSF 9.2+ compiler"
       & " on which Alire"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "can be built (Alire lists FreeBSD and OpenBSD among buildable hosts).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>GitHub release bundles</strong>: built on GitHub"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s Linux runners and distributed"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "as <code>adacovex-vX.Y.Z.tar.gz</code> for every tag.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The GitHub Actions composite action pins <code>gnat-version</code> (defau"
       & "lt <code>16.1.0</code>) via"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>alire-project/setup-alire</code>, and CI runs on <code>ubuntu-latest</"
       & "code>, so the CI-verified"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "platform is Linux x86-64. The tool itself is written in portable Ada 2012 us"
       & "ing"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "only the GNAT runtime, so no adacovex code is platform-specific beyond what "
       & "the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "GNAT runtime and Alire toolchain provide.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""delivery-and-versioning""><a class=""header"" href=""#delivery-and-versi"
       & "oning"">Delivery and Versioning</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex follows one version across every delivery channel, and each chan"
       & "nel is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "version-locked to the same release:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Single source of truth</strong>: the <code>version</code> field "
       & "in <code>alire.toml</code> /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>alire-dev.toml</code> is the single source, resolved by installation m"
       & "ethod. <code>tools/gen-version.py</code> regenerates <code>src/adacovex_vers"
       & "ion_info.ads</code> at build time (and <code>make bump-version</code>). It r"
       & "eads the first available of <code>ADACOVEX_VERSION</code> (release builds), "
       & "<code>alire-dev.toml</code> (source checkouts), or <code>alire.toml</code> ("
       & "dependency-managed installs). For dependency-managed installs, the published"
       & " crate builds from its release manifest, so the toml associated with the cov"
       & "ex binary for dependency management carries the version. <code>Adacovex. Ver"
       & "sion</code> in <code>src/adacovex.ads</code> re-exports the version.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>As a result, <code>--version</code>, the man page, the SBOM tool version,"
       & " and the result-cache namespace all derive from the manifest and can never d"
       & "rift. Release builds bundle the release tag instead via the <code>ADACOVEX_V"
       & "ERSION</code> environment variable (release workflow / <code>make release</c"
       & "ode>).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>CI is tied to the release version</strong>: the GitHub Actions c"
       & "omposite action"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>action.yml</code>) is version-matched to the adacovex binary. The rel"
       & "ease workflow bundles <code>adacovex-vX. Y. Z.tar.gz</code> and `adacovex-ac"
       & "tion-vX.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Y. Z.tar.gz<code>for every</code>vX. Y. Z<code> tag, and the action downl"
       & "oads the binary for the tag it is referenced by (</code>@vX.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Y. Z<code> runs that exact version). Floating tags (</code>vMAJOR<code>, "
       & "</code>vMAJOR. MINOR<code>, </code>latest<code>) are force-pushed at release"
       & " time so </code>@latest<code>/</code>@v1<code>/</code>@v1.3` always resolve "
       & "to the newest matching release.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>CI platform/compiler</strong>: CI validates the self-assessment "
       & "(build, prove,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tests) with the pinned <code>gnat-version</code> on <code>ubuntu-latest</cod"
       & "e>, so the CI-proven"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "combination is the released binary built against that exact toolchain.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Attestation</strong>: every release bundle is attested with"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>actions/attest</code> (OIDC), and the release notes link the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "signed attestation.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""build-time-linker-output-sframe""><a class=""header"" href=""#build-time"
       & "-linker-output-sframe"">Build-time linker output (SFrame)</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The Alire GNAT toolchain"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s bundled <code>ld</code> (2.44) emits a benign message"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>error in ...(.sframe); no .sframe will be created</code>) when it rea"
       & "ds the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>.sframe</code> section that newer system binutils wrote into the glibc"
       & " startup"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "objects. The link still succeeds. <code>make build</code> filters only this "
       & "one message;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "all compiler and gnatprove warnings remain fully visible, so nothing real is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "ever suppressed.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""read-only""><a class=""header"" href=""#read-only"">Read Only</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex itself is read-only. It merely scans your codebase for target do"
       & "cstrings and proofs.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>It does not make edits in place or on your behalf.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""flexible""><a class=""header"" href=""#flexible"">Flexible</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex lets you write proofs and decide where proofs are pointless (for"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "example code that has to involve manual memory management). You just have to"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "justify your rationale. The tool is not rigid. It does not expect 100% provi"
       & "ng"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "for all use cases.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>You write the proofs yourself, so there is no magic or hidden abstraction"
       & "s here.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""pipeline-execution-order""><a class=""header"" href=""#pipeline-executio"
       & "n-order"">Pipeline (execution order)</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>When adacovex runs, it executes these steps in sequence:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code>0. Parse CLI args           -&gt; CLI_Config record (prove / sbom"
       & " / diff / man / complexity / normal)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "0a. Early-exit modes        -&gt; --help / --version / man / status / comple"
       & "xity exit before the pipeline"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "1. Determine ANSI color     -&gt; NO_COLOR check"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "2. (prove mode) Run GNATprove -&gt; fresh obj/gnatprove/gnatprove.out"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "3. Scan source files        -&gt; Package_Vectors.Vector (subprograms, HLR t"
       & "ags, docstrings)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "4. Apply docstring patches  -&gt; Merge .adacovex/patches/ (strict mode only"
       & ")"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "5. Compute doc metrics      -&gt; Docstring_Metrics (coverage %)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "6. Parse GNATprove output   -&gt; Proof_Summary (VC counts, SPARK level)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "7. Parse test results       -&gt; Test_Summary (pass/fail counts)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "8. Assess DAL compliance    -&gt; DAL_Assessment (Achieved / Unmet + reasons"
       & ")"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "9. Render ANSI summary      -&gt; stdout (terminal report)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "10. Emit SVG badges          -&gt; &lt;svg-dir&gt;/*.svg (if enabled)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "11. Emit Markdown reports    -&gt; &lt;md-dir&gt;/VERIFICATION.md + TRACE.md"
       & " (if enabled)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "12. Emit automatic SBOM      -&gt; &lt;target&gt;/sbom.json | sbom.spdx.json"
       & " | docs/compliance/SBOM.md (unless --no-sbom)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "13. Start HTTP server        -&gt; :&lt;port&gt; (if --serve; serves the das"
       & "hboard,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                              the JSON API, the SVG badges, and the bundled"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                              offline manual at /docs)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "14. Set exit code            -&gt; 0 if Achieved, 1 if Unmet"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Differential modes (<code>--compare-base</code> / <code>--coverage-delta<"
       & "/code>) run before the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "pipeline and snapshot a base revision via <code>Adacovex.VCS</code> (git <co"
       & "de>worktree add</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "hg <code>archive</code>, svn <code>export</code>, fossil <code>open</code> o"
       & "n a copied DB, or a git worktree"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "against the jj store), assess base and current tree, report the delta, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "exit. <code>man</code> installs the generated man page (<code>Adacovex.Rende"
       & "rers.Man</code>) into"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the local man database (<code>~/.local/share/man</code>, Linux/WSL) and refr"
       & "eshes it with"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>mandb</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""swapping-the-gnat-compiler-llvm-backend""><a class=""header"" href=""#sw"
       & "apping-the-gnat-compiler-llvm-backend"">Swapping the GNAT compiler (LLVM back"
       & "end)</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex and Alire both default to the GCC-based <strong>GNAT</strong> (<"
       & "code>gnat_native</code>)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "compiler. No action is needed. Only swap if you specifically want an"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "LLVM-backend GNAT (for example GNAT LLVM) for your target project "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " for"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "example to exercise dissimilar redundancy via diverse code generation.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>GNAT LLVM is <strong>not</strong> yet packaged as a standard Alire toolch"
       & "ain crate, so two"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "paths exist:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>Alire-managed compiler (preferred when available).</strong> If a "
       & "GNAT LLVM binary"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "release becomes available in the Alire index, declare it in your"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>alire.toml</code> / <code>alire-dev.toml</code>:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code class=""language-toml"">[[depends-on]]"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "gnat_llvm = ""*"""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>alr</code> then selects it automatically for that project"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s builds. You can also"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "pick a default compiler for all projects with"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>alr toolchain --select --disable-assistant</code> and choosing the LLV"
       & "M GNAT.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>System-installed GNAT LLVM.</strong> Install GNAT LLVM on <code>$"
       & "PATH</code>, then force the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Ada toolchain in the root <code>.gpr</code> so <code>gprbuild</code> does no"
       & "t fall back to the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "GCC GNAT:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code class=""language-gpr"">for Toolchain_Name (""Ada"") use ""GNAT_LLVM"";"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>You can confirm which compiler built a given <code>.ali</code> file by it"
       & "s first line"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>GNAT</code> vs <code>GNAT-LLVM</code>).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Notes:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>GNAT LLVM and GCC GNAT are not guaranteed ABI-compatible. Compile all Ad"
       & "a in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "a project with the same compiler.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>GNAT LLVM"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <code>-fstack-check</code> support is partial and some features"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>Scalar_Storage_Order</code>, <code>Convention C++</code>) differ from"
       & " GCC GNAT.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>SPARK proof results are compiler-independent, so <code>covex prove</code"
       & "> and the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "DAL assessment are unaffected by the choice.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
