       & "y"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>tools/gen-version.py</code>). <code>make fmt</code> runs gnatformat ov"
       & "er every unit in the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "project "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " including the generated ones "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " and gnatformat rewraps the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "string-concatenation lines differently than the generator emits them. A"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>prove -&gt; fmt -&gt; doc</code> chain therefore produced a different "
       & "byte state for"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the template on every alternating run, depending on whether build/fmt ran"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "last. <code>make fmt</code> now re-runs both generators after gnatformat, so"
       & " the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "generated files always end in their canonical committed form "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " verified"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "deterministic across repeated <code>build -&gt; fmt -&gt; doc</code> chains."
       & "</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c3-dedicated-documentation-pages-and-a-slimmer-cli-reference""><a cla"
       & "ss=""header"" href=""#c3-dedicated-documentation-pages-and-a-slimmer-cli-refere"
       & "nce"">C3: dedicated documentation pages and a slimmer CLI reference</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The docs were reorganized around one page per feature so the CLI referenc"
       & "e"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "stays a quick reference instead of accumulating every flag"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s full detail:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>New <a href=""../dashboard.html"">Web dashboard + JSON API</a></st"
       & "rong> page "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " endpoints,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dashboard cards, the <code>/api/metrics</code> JSON schema, and the theme-re"
       & "solution"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "order (<code>?theme=</code> &gt; <code>--theme=</code> &gt; saved <code>loca"
       & "lStorage</code> &gt; system).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>New <a href=""../sbom.html"">SBOM</a></strong> page "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " usage, standard-awareness, component"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "properties, and <code>SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH</code> determinism.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>New <a href=""../vcs.html"">VCS support</a></strong> page "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the per-VCS snapshot mechanisms and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the <code>--compare-base</code> / <code>--coverage-delta</code> contracts.</"
       & "li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>New <a href=""../target-projects.html"">Target projects</a></stron"
       & "g> page "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the target-project"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "requirements (sources, <code>gnatprove.out</code> discovery order, test-summ"
       & "ary file"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "names, HLR.md, missing-data behaviour) moved out of the README.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong><code>docs/cli-reference.md</code> slimmed</strong> to the flag "
       & "table plus a concise note"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "per flag, linking to the dedicated pages; the result-caching design moved"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "to <a href=""../architecture.html#result-caching""><code>../architecture.md#re"
       & "sult-caching</code></a>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>README condensed and its Quick start rewritten</strong>: the Qui"
       & "ck start now"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "shows the end-user flow (install -&gt; assess -&gt; <code>status</code> -&gt"
       & "; <code>--serve</code>)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "instead of contributor build targets, the documentation table moved to the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "top (right after Quick start), the duplicated standards paragraph was"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "removed, and sections that duplicate dedicated pages (platforms,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "toolchain resolution, VCS, AI disclosure, dashboard) now point at them.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c4-contributor-guide-link-checker-and-a-tighter-readme""><a class=""he"
       & "ader"" href=""#c4-contributor-guide-link-checker-and-a-tighter-readme"">C4: con"
       & "tributor guide, link checker, and a tighter README</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>New <a href=""../developer-guide.html"">Contributor guide</a></str"
       & "ong> page "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " a human-readable"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tour of the codebase (repository layout, pipeline, where each kind of"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "change lives, testing and SPARK discipline, common workflows) to"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "supplement CONTRIBUTING.md, linked from it, the README docs table, and the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "AGENTS.md documentation block.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>New <code>make link-check</code> gate</strong> (<code>tools/chec"
       & "k-links.py</code>) "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " verifies every"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "markdown link in the repo resolves (file existence plus GitHub-style"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "heading anchors, code fences excluded), wired into <code>make check</code> a"
       & "s a cheap"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "static gate. It immediately found a pre-existing broken link in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>docs/platforms.md</code> (a <code>README.md</code> reference missing t"
       & "he <code>../</code> prefix),"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "now fixed.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>README trimmed further</strong> (318 -&gt; 229 lines over this r"
       & "elease): the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "platform/toolchain/VCS sections merged into one compact section, the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "docstring example folded into a pointer, the DAL table moved out (the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "standards table + links remain), and the example list cut to the six most"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "common invocations.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""fixes""><a class=""header"" href=""#fixes"">Fixes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h1-release-workflow-linked-only-the-current-versions-changelog""><a c"
       & "lass=""header"" href=""#h1-release-workflow-linked-only-the-current-versions-ch"
       & "angelog"">H1: release workflow linked only the current version"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s changelog</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code>Create GitHub Release</code> step in <code>.github/workflows/re"
       & "lease.yml</code> filters"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>docs/changelogs/adacovex-*.md</code> to the versions between the previ"
       & "ous release"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tag and the released version. The upper-bound filter compared the maximum of"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the changelog version and the released version against the changelog version"
       & ASCII.LF
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " inverted "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " so every changelog below the released version was skipped and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the release notes listed only the current version"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s changelog. The comparison"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "now keeps every available changelog strictly above the previous release tag"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and at or below the released version, so a release that spans multiple"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "versions links all of them (derived from the entries actually present in the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tree).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h2-cached-scans-leaked-another-trees-absolute-path-differential-mode"
       & "s""><a class=""header"" href=""#h2-cached-scans-leaked-another-trees-absolute-pa"
       & "th-differential-modes"">H2: cached scans leaked another tree"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s absolute path (differential modes)</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>--compare-base</code> / <code>--coverage-delta</code> scan entries "
       & "are cached per file by"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "content hash (<code>""scan:"" + sha256</code>), so a byte-identical file in a "
       & "different"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "directory "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " e.g. the base snapshot under <code>/tmp/adacovex-diff-&lt;pid&gt;</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " used"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "to hit the entry cached from whichever tree was scanned first and inherit"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "that tree"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s absolute <code>File_Path</code>. Relative-path consumers then silently"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "broke: <code>Apply_Patches</code> could not match <code>.adacovex/patches/</"
       & "code> entries"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>Relative_Path</code> returned "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & "), so docstring coverage dropped on cached runs"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(observed as 88% vs the true 100% when running <code>make coverage-gate</cod"
       & "e> against"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Ada_CRDT, flipping with cache state). <code>Scan_Project_Cached</code> now r"
       & "ewrites the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>File_Path</code> of every cache-hit package to the file currently bein"
       & "g scanned,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "so patch application, HLR traceability, and report paths always reflect the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "scanned tree. The scanner test suite gained a regression check (Test 22:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "scan identical content in two directories and verify each result keeps its"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "own path).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""test-suite""><a class=""header"" href=""#test-suite"">Test Suite</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>666 tests (was 659), across 12 categories. The HTML/Markdown renderers"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "category gained 4 regression checks for the dashboard card block (no HTML"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "comment wrapping, live card markup present, badge images rendered, SPARK"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "proof card present), and the Source scanner category gained 3 checks for the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cached-scan path fix (Test 22: both cached scans parse, the second tree keep"
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "its own <code>File_Path</code>, the first keeps its own).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""proof-results""><a class=""header"" href=""#proof-results"">Proof Results"
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Platinum, 408/408 VCs proved across 45 analysed units (unchanged from"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "1.13.0): the cache-path fix lives in the non-SPARK <code>parsers-source</cod"
       & "e> body and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the regression tests are not proved, so no new proof obligations. Proven"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "with <code>make prove</code> under gnatprove 16.1.0 (<code>--steps=10000</co"
       & "de>).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""traceability""><a class=""header"" href=""#traceability"">Traceability</a"
       & "></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>No new HLRs. The dashboard rendering fix stays covered by the existing"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>HLR-RENDER-HTML</code> (<code>src/renderers/adacovex-renderers-html.ad"
       & "s</code>/<code>.adb</code>) tag;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the template bundle (<code>resources/dashboard.html</code> +"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>tools/gen-dashboard.py</code>) is generated data that adds no traceabi"
       & "lity. The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cached-scan fix stays covered by the existing <code>HLR-SCAN</code> tag"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>src/parsers/adacovex-parsers-source.ads</code>/<code>.adb</code>); th"
       & "e documentation"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "reorganization, the link checker, and the release-workflow changelog-listing"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "fix touch no HLR-bearing code, so no new or changed HLR traceability tags ar"
       & "e"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "required.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
