       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""adacovex-1210""><a class=""header"" href=""#adac"
       & "ovex-1210"">adacovex 1.21.0</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Date: <em>2026-08-23</em></p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Version bumped 1.20.0 -&gt; 1.21.0.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""changes""><a class=""header"" href=""#changes"">Changes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c1-fix-raw-css-rendered-as-text-in---serve-dashboard""><a class=""head"
       & "er"" href=""#c1-fix-raw-css-rendered-as-text-in---serve-dashboard"">C1: Fix raw"
       & " CSS rendered as text in <code>--serve</code> dashboard</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The dashboard page shell (<code>resources/dashboard.html</code>) had a du"
       & "plicated"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>&lt;/style&gt;</code> tag: the custom dashboard CSS was closed, the ve"
       & "ndored"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>charts.min.css</code> was then inlined <em>outside</em> any <code>&lt;"
       & "style&gt;</code> block, and a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "second <code>&lt;/style&gt;</code> closed the head.  Browsers rendered the e"
       & "ntire vendored"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "CSS as literal text at the top of the page.  The template is now a single"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>&lt;style&gt;</code> block (custom CSS + vendored Charts.css + a singl"
       & "e <code>&lt;/style&gt;</code>)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "regenerated via <code>tools/gen-dashboard.py</code>, so the page is self-con"
       & "tained and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "valid HTML again.  No visual change beyond the bug being gone.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c2-dependency-tree-text-spacing-scope-filtering-and-overview-collati"
       & "on""><a class=""header"" href=""#c2-dependency-tree-text-spacing-scope-filtering"
       & "-and-overview-collation"">C2: Dependency tree text spacing, scope filtering, "
       & "and overview collation</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The tree"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s typography is tightened: <code>line-height</code> 1.5 -&gt; 1.65, node mar"
       & "gins 4px -&gt; 6px, leaf padding 6x8 -&gt; 8x12, gaps 8px -&gt; 10px, and a "
       & "hover <code>border-color: var(--accent)</code> transition. Every <code>&lt;l"
       & "i class=""dep-node""&gt;</code> now carries <code>data-scope</code> (<code>bas"
       & "e</code> / <code>dev</code> / <code>transitive</code> / <code>vendored</code"
       & ">) and <code>data-name</code>, and the toolbar gains four scope checkboxes ("
       & "base, dev, transitive, vendored "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " all checked by default) plus <code>Expand all</code> / <code>Collapse all</"
       & "code>. A new <code>filterByScope()</code> JS function composes the name filt"
       & "er and the scope filters so <code>dev</code> and <code>vendored</code> deps "
       & "can be hidden without losing the hierarchy (and re-renders the nomnoml diagr"
       & "am when visible). The <code>dep-filter</code> input is now visually consiste"
       & "nt with the global search box (<code>padding:7px 12px; border-radius:8px; fo"
       & "nt-size:.88rem</code>).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <strong>Overview</strong> tab is also more useful: after the Source O"
       & "verview / Quick Stats grid it now shows a collation <code>chart-grid</code> "
       & "with three mini visuals (SPARK donut, Tests pie, Docs bar) so the key pies/b"
       & "ars are visible without leaving the overview. The same <code>data-scope</cod"
       & "e> attribute drives the scope pie in C3.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c3-charts--pie-bar-line-area-and-scope-aware-extras-where-suitable"">"
       & "<a class=""header"" href=""#c3-charts--pie-bar-line-area-and-scope-aware-extras"
       & "-where-suitable"">C3: Charts "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " pie, bar, line, area and scope-aware extras where suitable</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>Renderers.HTML.Render_Charts</code> now has a graph-aware overload"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>(Doc, Proof, Tests, Graph)</code> (the old 3-arg form remains as a wra"
       & "pper) and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "emits four new visuals in the <strong>Charts</strong> tab (now 8 cards total"
       & "):</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Tests Pass/Fail</strong> pie "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " passed vs failed slice (previously only the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "per-category bar existed, so a single failing test was easy to miss);</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Dependencies by Scope</strong> pie "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " counts of base / dev / transitive /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "vendored components from the resolved graph (skipped when the graph is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "empty);</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Proof (line)</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>charts-css line</code> variant of the proof categories,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "same data as the column chart but as a line, for trend-appropriate"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "comparison;</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Docs Area</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>charts-css area</code> variant of the doc coverage bar.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Existing charts are kept (SPARK donut now proved vs unproved, proof"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "categories column, test categories bar normalised to the max, doc coverage"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "bar) and now correctly use <code>0..1</code> <code>--size</code> fractions. "
       & " The chart grid stays"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr))</code> inside the tab panel.  The"
       & " <strong>Overview</strong>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tab also gains a collation row with three mini charts (SPARK donut, Tests"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "pie, Docs bar) for a quick summary without leaving the overview.  See"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>docs/dashboard.md#metrics-charts</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c4-dependency-hierarchy-alternative-view-with-vendored-nomnoml-and-g"
       & "raphre""><a class=""header"" href=""#c4-dependency-hierarchy-alternative-view-wi"
       & "th-vendored-nomnoml-and-graphre"">C4: Dependency hierarchy alternative view w"
       & "ith vendored nomnoml and graphre</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <strong>Dependencies</strong> tab gains a second view: <strong>Tree</"
       & "strong> (default) vs"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<strong>Diagram (nomnoml)</strong>.  The diagram is rendered with vendored"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a href=""https://github.com/skanaar/nomnoml"">nomnoml 1.7.0</a> (MIT, <code>r"
       & "esources/nomnoml.js</code>, 71 KB) plus its layout engine <a href=""https://g"
       & "ithub.com/cytoscape/graphre"">graphre 0.1.3</a> (MIT, <code>resources/graphre"
       & ".js</code>, 38 KB, inlined before nomnoml as <code>global.graphre</code>). W"
       & "ithout graphre, <code>nomnoml.draw</code> throws <code>graphlib is undefined"
       & "</code> (the UMD wrapper <code>require('graphre')</code> expects <code>globa"
       & "l.graphre</code>). Both are inlined into the single-file dashboard template "
       & "so the diagram works offline. <code>ADACOVEX_GRAPH</code> (injected as <code"
       & ">__GRAPH_JSON__</code> by the Ada renderer) is converted to nomnoml source ("
       & "<code>[parent]--&gt;[child]</code> edges, <code>#direction: right</code>, pl"
       & "us a legend note) and drawn via <code>nomnoml.draw(canvas, src)</code>. The "
       & "view switch is persisted in <code>localStorage</code> (<code>adacovex-dep-vi"
       & "ew</code>) and hash-routed, with <strong>Re-render</strong> and <strong>Down"
       & "load PNG</strong> buttons.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Scope checkboxes filter both views (tree hides nodes via <code>data-scope"
       & "</code>, diagram re-renders from the filtered set after <code>filterByScope("
       & ")</code>). Control characters (<code>\x01</code>) in the vendored graphre bu"
       & "ndle are sanitized to <code>\x01</code> escapes so the Ada template remains "
       & "pure ASCII and <code>make ascii-check</code> passes. Credits and license upd"
       & "ated in <code>docs/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c5-vendor-flexsearch-for-dashboard-search-indexing-and-responsive-la"
       & "yout""><a class=""header"" href=""#c5-vendor-flexsearch-for-dashboard-search-ind"
       & "exing-and-responsive-layout"">C5: Vendor FlexSearch for dashboard search inde"
       & "xing and responsive layout</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The dashboard header gains a global search box (packages, HLRs, deps) pow"
       & "ered by vendored <a href=""https://github.com/nextapps-de/flexsearch"">FlexSea"
       & "rch 0.7.31</a> (Apache-2.0, <code>resources/flexsearch.js</code>, 16 KB, inl"
       & "ined before the theme/tab script). At page load the index is hydrated robust"
       & "ly for both FlexSearch 0.7 (<code>FlexSearch. Index</code>) and 0.8 (<code>F"
       & "lexSearch</code> as constructor) APIs: <code>FlexSearch. Index({tokenize:'fo"
       & "rward'})</code> with a <code>try</code> fallback, populated from <code>ADACO"
       & "VEX_GRAPH.dependencies</code> and from rendered <code>data-name</code> attri"
       & "butes.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Queries are served from the index (20-hit limit) with a DOM fallback, and"
       & " hits appear in a <code>search-hits</code> dropdown (absolute, <code>max-hei"
       & "ght:240px</code>, <code>z-index:10</code>) that is keyboard-focusable and ju"
       & "mps to the Dependencies tab while seeding <code>dep-filter</code>. The heade"
       & "r is now responsive: <code>flex:1 1 200px</code> search box with <code>@medi"
       & "a(max-width:640px)</code> stacking, and the <code>dep-filter</code> input in"
       & " the Dependencies toolbar is unified to the same <code>padding:7px 12px; bor"
       & "der-radius:8px; font-size:.88rem</code> as the global box (previously <code>"
       & "8px 10px / .9rem</code> vs <code>.88rem</code>). See <code>docs/dashboard.md"
       & "</code> and <code>docs/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c6-man-pages-are-now-single-source-of-truth-from-source""><a class=""h"
       & "eader"" href=""#c6-man-pages-are-now-single-source-of-truth-from-source"">C6: M"
       & "an pages are now single source of truth from source</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>Adacovex. Renderers. Man</code> no longer hard-codes the <code>. SH"
       & " OPTIONS</code> list. <code>Render_Page</code> now derives the option list a"
       & "t runtime from `Adacovex.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Config. Flag_List<code>(the same</code>Known_Flags<code>that drives</code"
       & ">"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "help<code>and shell completion), iterating the space-separated flag table an"
       & "d emitting a</code>. TP<code>entry per flag via a central</code>Desc_For<cod"
       & "e>map. Adding a flag to</code>Known_Flags<code>automatically adds a man entr"
       & "y (with a fallback generic line) even before a bespoke description is added,"
       & " so the man page,</code>"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "help`, and completion can never drift.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A future <code>tools/gen-man.py</code> generator (parity with <code>gen-d"
       & "ashboard.py</code> / <code>gen-version.py</code>) is documented as the next "
       & "step, but the runtime derivation already makes <code>Flag_List</code> the si"
       & "ngle source. The <code>man --check</code> / <code>man --dir</code> / <code>m"
       & "an --force</code> flow and the installed page header (<code>adacovex vX. Y. "
       & "Z</code>) are unchanged.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c7-check-for-vendored-dependencies-including-js-assets""><a class=""he"
       & "ader"" href=""#c7-check-for-vendored-dependencies-including-js-assets"">C7: Che"
       & "ck for vendored dependencies including JS assets</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>Discover_Vendored_Components</code> in <code>parsers-manifest.adb</"
       & "code> now scans"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>resources/</code> (and <code>vendor/</code> / <code>assets/</code> if "
       & "present) for <code>*.js</code> / <code>*.css</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "assets in addition to <code>.adacovex/patches/*.ads</code>.  Each <code>char"
       & "ts.min.css</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>nomnoml.js</code>, <code>graphre.js</code>, and <code>flexsearch.js</c"
       & "ode> is added as a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Scope_Vendored</code> <code>pkg:generic/&lt;name&gt;</code> dependency"
       & " of the root, so"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>adacovex --target=.</code> (and <code>--emit-metrics</code> / <code>/a"
       & "pi/deps</code>) now lists the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "vendored JS/CSS that the dashboard inlines.  The dashboard"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s scope pie and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "its filter checkboxes therefore show vendored vs dev vs transitive vs base"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "correctly, and <code>make check</code> can gate on vendored presence.  The r"
       & "esult-cache"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "schema is bumped <code>s3</code> -&gt; <code>s4</code> so stale graphs witho"
       & "ut vendored assets are"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "never served.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""fixes""><a class=""header"" href=""#fixes"">Fixes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h1-dashboard-served-valid-html-again-and-nomnoml-no-longer-throws""><"
       & "a class=""header"" href=""#h1-dashboard-served-valid-html-again-and-nomnoml-no-"
       & "longer-throws"">H1: Dashboard served valid HTML again and nomnoml no longer t"
       & "hrows</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Covered by C1: the duplicated <code>&lt;/style&gt;</code> that caused the"
       & " vendored CSS to be"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "rendered as text is removed.  <code>make ascii-check</code> and <code>tools/"
       & "gen-dashboard.py --check</code> both pass; the served page at <code>http://1"
       & "27.0.0.1:8080/</code> now shows"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "styled cards, not raw CSS.  Covered by C4: vendored <code>graphre.js</code> "
       & "is now"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "inlined before <code>nomnoml.js</code> so <code>nomnoml.draw</code> no longe"
       & "r throws"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>graphlib is undefined</code> (<code>global.graphre</code> is defined b"
       & "y the UMD wrapper)."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Control characters (<code>\x01</code>) in the graphre bundle are sanitized t"
       & "o <code>\x01</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "escapes so the Ada template remains pure ASCII and <code>alr build</code> no"
       & " longer"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "errors with <code>control character not allowed in string</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""test-suite""><a class=""header"" href=""#test-suite"">Test Suite</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>886 tests passing (unchanged) across 14 categories.  No new test categori"
       & "es"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "added in this release; the existing HTML rendering, man page, and server"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "routing expectations continue to pin the dashboard shell and the <code>/api/"
       & "deps</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "route.  A follow-up will add renderer tests for the new chart pies and the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>data-scope</code> attribute.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""proof-results""><a class=""header"" href=""#proof-results"">Proof Results"
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Platinum, 720/720 VCs proved across 49 analysed units (unchanged from"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "1.20.0): the chart pies, dep-tree scope attributes, nomnoml/flexsearch"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "inlining (tooling-bundled JS), and the dynamic man page all live in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "default-off bodies or are Python/JS tooling "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " no new SPARK obligations.  0"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "unproved, 0 justified.  Re-verified with <code>adacovex prove --target=. --f"
       & "orce</code> under gnatprove 16.1.0 (<code>--steps=10000</code>).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""traceability""><a class=""header"" href=""#traceability"">Traceability</a"
       & "></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>No new HLRs.  Coverage:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-DASH</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " C1 raw-CSS fix, C2 tree spacing, C3 scope/test pies, C4"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "nomnoml diagram, C5 FlexSearch indexing (renderer, dashboard docs,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "third-party notices);</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-CLI</code> / <code>HLR-DOC</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " C6 man page single source (man renderer,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "config flag list);</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-SBOM</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " dependency graph already covers scope filtering (no new"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "SBOM surface).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>See <code>docs/dashboard.md</code>, <code>docs/cli-reference.md</code>, <"
       & "code>docs/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
