       & "ibute('aria-expanded', sidebar === 'visible');"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                    document.getElementById('mdbook-sidebar').setAttribute('"
       & "aria-hidden', sidebar !== 'visible');"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                    Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('#mdbook-sidebar a'"
       & ")).forEach(function(link) {"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        link.setAttribute('tabIndex', sidebar === 'visible' "
       & "? 0 : -1);"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                    });"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                </script>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                <div id=""mdbook-content"" class=""content"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                    <main>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""adacovex-1220""><a class=""header"" href=""#adac"
       & "ovex-1220"">adacovex 1.22.0</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Date: <em>2026-08-24</em></p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Version bumped 1.21.0 -&gt; 1.22.0.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""changes""><a class=""header"" href=""#changes"">Changes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c1-charts-page-has-six-distinct-chart-types-and-pies-render-correctl"
       & "y""><a class=""header"" href=""#c1-charts-page-has-six-distinct-chart-types-and-"
       & "pies-render-correctly"">C1: Charts page has six distinct chart types and pies"
       & " render correctly</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <strong>Charts</strong> tab now shows six cards, each a different typ"
       & "e: SPARK proof"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "donut, proof check types column, test results by category bar, docstring"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "coverage radial gauge, tests pass/fail pie, and the dependencies-by-scope"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "polar ring.  The duplicated proof line/area variants are gone and the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "docstring coverage visual is back on the Charts tab as a half-circle radial"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "gauge.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The long-standing "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "pie &lt;U+2260&gt; pie"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " bug is fixed at the root: Charts.css"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>--start</code>/<code>--end</code> are unitless <code>0..1</code> turn "
       & "fractions, but every pie/donut"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "slice was fed <code>0..100</code> percentages, so each slice rendered as a f"
       & "ull circle"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(and stacked opaque over the previous one).  All pie values now go through a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Frac</code> helper that clamps to <code>0..1</code>, and the donut hol"
       & "e is a pure-CSS"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>.charts-css.pie.donut::after</code> circle instead of an invalid <code"
       & ">donut</code> class.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c2-overview-at-a-glance---robustness-radar-with-a-tier-rating""><a cl"
       & "ass=""header"" href=""#c2-overview-at-a-glance---robustness-radar-with-a-tier-r"
       & "ating"">C2: Overview at a glance - robustness radar with a tier rating</a></h"
       & "3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The Overview tab now leads with a <strong>Robustness</strong> radar spide"
       & "r and a tier"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "rating (S / A / B / C / D) computed as the average of five <code>0..100</cod"
       & "e> axes:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Docstrings (coverage), Proof (VCs proved), Tests (pass rate), Compliance"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(gate achieved), and Deps (non-vendored share of the graph).  The tier chip"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "is colour-coded per theme, the legend lists each axis with its percentage,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and the thresholds (S &gt;= 90, A &gt;= 80, B &gt;= 65, C &gt;= 50, D &lt; 5"
       & "0) plus axis"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "definitions are documented in <code>docs/dashboard.md</code> and shown in th"
       & "e card.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The per-check-type <strong>SPARK radar</strong> moved from the Charts tab"
       & " to the Overview"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(miniature), the tests visual is now a donut, and the doc-coverage gauge"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "completes the collation.  All overview visuals are inline SVG/CSS with"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "integer math (no floating point in the renderer) and follow the active"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "light/dark theme.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c3-dashboard-footer-with-version-licensing-and-credits""><a class=""he"
       & "ader"" href=""#c3-dashboard-footer-with-version-licensing-and-credits"">C3: Das"
       & "hboard footer with version, licensing and credits</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The single-line footer is now a semantic <code>&lt;footer class=""footer""&"
       & "gt;</code> grid with"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "three sections: copyright + license + repository + the injected"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>v1.22.0</code> version, the third-party credits summary (Charts.css, n"
       & "omnoml, graphre, FlexSearch)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "linking to <code>docs/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md</code>, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the API endpoints (<code>/api/metrics</code>, <code>/api/deps</code>, <code>"
       & "/badge/*.svg</code>).  The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "version is injected next to <code>__THEME__</code>/<code>__GRAPH_JSON__</cod"
       & "e> by the Ada"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "renderer from <code>Adacovex.Version</code>, so the footer always matches th"
       & "e binary.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c4-nomnoml-diagram-top-to-bottom-and-theme-aware""><a class=""header"" "
       & "href=""#c4-nomnoml-diagram-top-to-bottom-and-theme-aware"">C4: nomnoml diagram"
       & " top-to-bottom and theme-aware</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The dependency diagram now lays out with <code>#direction: down</code> (a"
       & " vertical"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tree that stays within the page width on wide dep graphs) and reads the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "page"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s CSS custom properties (<code>--card</code>, <code>--border</code>, <code>-"
       & "-fg</code>) at draw time,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "re-rendering on theme change so the box/arrow colours always match.  The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "canvas is sized to its container and deep graphs scroll inside"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>.nomnoml-wrap</code> instead of overflowing the layout.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c5-dependency-tree-spacing-and-theme-aware-scope-badges""><a class=""h"
       & "eader"" href=""#c5-dependency-tree-spacing-and-theme-aware-scope-badges"">C5: D"
       & "ependency tree spacing and theme-aware scope badges</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Node text now carries explicit spacing in the markup (no more"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>covex1.21.0transitive...</code> when CSS is slow or copying), and the "
       & "scope badges"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "use <code>--scope-*</code> CSS variables with <code>color-mix</code> backgro"
       & "unds: dark-theme-safe"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "purple for <code>dev</code>, muted for <code>transitive</code>, vendored in "
       & "the danger colour,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "base in the accent colour.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c6-scope-checkboxes-styled-with-inline-svg-pictograms""><a class=""hea"
       & "der"" href=""#c6-scope-checkboxes-styled-with-inline-svg-pictograms"">C6: Scope"
       & " checkboxes styled with inline SVG pictograms</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The four scope checkboxes are custom-styled accessible checkboxes (hidden"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "native input + styled <code>.box</code> with a checkmark SVG) and each has a"
       & " small"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "inline SVG pictogram "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " info circle for base, wrench for dev, layers for"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "transitive, warning triangle for vendored "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " used sparingly next to the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "text labels (<code>aria-hidden</code>, focus-visible rings preserved).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c7-language-agnostic-vendored-dependency-discovery-with-sbom-languag"
       & "es""><a class=""header"" href=""#c7-language-agnostic-vendored-dependency-discov"
       & "ery-with-sbom-languages"">C7: Language-agnostic vendored dependency discovery"
       & " with SBOM languages</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The dependency graph now discovers vendored components beyond Alire/GPR:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>node_modules</code> (npm, shallow: one component per top-level <code>p"
       & "ackage.json</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>pkg:npm/...@version</code>), <code>vendor</code>, <code>third_party</c"
       & "ode>, <code>deps</code>, <code>submodules</code>, etc."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "carrying <code>Cargo.toml</code>/<code>Cargo.lock</code> (pkg:cargo), <code>"
       & "go.mod</code> (pkg:golang),"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>pyproject.toml</code>/<code>requirements*.txt</code> (pkg:pypi), <code"
       & ">composer.json</code> (pkg:composer),"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Gemfile</code> (pkg:gem), and plain source libraries.  A directory wit"
       & "hout a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "manifest becomes ONE component whose language is the top-3 summary of its"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "source-extension distribution (e.g. <code>Go; Python; JavaScript</code>) "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " loose files"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "under a vendor root never become components.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Every SBOM component now carries <code>language</code> in CycloneDX (and "
       & "the Markdown"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "table), inferred from the file extension or manifest, with mobile"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "fallbacks.  The graph cache key hashes vendored trees and lockfiles too"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>Vendored_Hash</code>), so adding/removing vendored code invalidates t"
       & "he cached"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "graph.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c8-dashboard-resources-modularised-and-minified-at-build-time""><a cl"
       & "ass=""header"" href=""#c8-dashboard-resources-modularised-and-minified-at-build"
       & "-time"">C8: Dashboard resources modularised and minified at build time</a></h"
       & "3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The single 190 KB <code>resources/dashboard.html</code> (CSS, four script"
       & " bundles and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "page markup all interleaved) is now a <strong>page skeleton</strong> plus on"
       & "e file per"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "concern: <code>resources/dashboard.css</code> (author styles), <code>resourc"
       & "es/dashboard.js</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(tabs, theme, searches, filters, dep-details popup) and the vendored"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>charts.min.css</code> / <code>graphre.js</code> / <code>nomnoml.js</co"
       & "de> / <code>flexsearch.js</code>."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>tools/gen-dashboard.py</code> inlines the modules into <code>dashboard"
       & ".html</code> at build"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "time via <code>__STYLE_CUSTOM__</code> / <code>__STYLE_CHARTS__</code> / <co"
       & "de>__JS_*</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "placeholders and <strong>minifies the author CSS/JS</strong> (comments and w"
       & "hitespace"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "stripped; vendored bundles are already minified and inlined byte-for-byte,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "license headers preserved).  <code>gen-dashboard.py --check</code> (wired in"
       & "to"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>make check</code>) fails when the committed generated spec drifts.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c9-per-dependency-detail-panel-with-registry-links""><a class=""header"
       & """ href=""#c9-per-dependency-detail-panel-with-registry-links"">C9: Per-depende"
       & "ncy detail panel with registry links</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Dependency names in the tree are now clickable and open an inline"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "detail panel: name, version, scope, licence, PURL, parent, and a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "registry link derived from the PURL (<code>pkg:github</code> -&gt; GitHub re"
       & "po,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>pkg:npm</code> -&gt; npmjs, <code>pkg:cargo</code> -&gt; crates.io, <c"
       & "ode>pkg:pypi</code> -&gt; PyPI,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>pkg:golang</code> -&gt; pkg.go.dev, <code>pkg:alire</code> -&gt; alire"
       & ".ada.dev, otherwise a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "GitHub search).  Licence and PURL text in the tree is colour-coded"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>--lic</code> amber, <code>--purl</code> muted monospace) so vendored/"
       & "uncommon licences"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "stand out; <code>lang</code> is exposed in <code>/api/deps</code> JSON per c"
       & "omponent.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c10-mini-visualisation-atop-every-tab-separate-but-similar-searches"""
       & "><a class=""header"" href=""#c10-mini-visualisation-atop-every-tab-separate-but"
       & "-similar-searches"">C10: Mini-visualisation atop every tab; separate but simi"
       & "lar searches</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Each tab now leads with a small visual: Proof gets a VCs-proved/total"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "column, Tests a pass/fail donut, Compliance an achievement radial gauge, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Dependencies a scope-distribution stacked bar with legend.  The header"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<strong>global search</strong> (FlexSearch index over packages/HLRs/deps) an"
       & "d the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Dependencies tab <strong>tree filter</strong> (plain DOM filter over the ren"
       & "dered tree)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "are separate mechanisms sharing one styling class, so they look consistent"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "but only a clicked global hit seeds the tree filter.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c11-sbom-language-detection-documented""><a class=""header"" href=""#c11"
       & "-sbom-language-detection-documented"">C11: SBOM language detection documented"
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>docs/sbom.md</code> gains a Language detection section: manifest-de"
       & "clared"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "ecosystems map to their canonical language (npm -&gt; JavaScript, cargo -&gt"
       & ";"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Rust, go.mod -&gt; Go, "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(166)
       & "), Alire/GPR -&gt; Ada, and everything else (vendored"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "trees, resources, loose file drops) infers the top-3 languages from actual"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "source-extension distribution.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""fixes""><a class=""header"" href=""#fixes"">Fixes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h1-pie-charts-rendered-as-full-circles-covex1210transitive-spacing"">"
       & "<a class=""header"" href=""#h1-pie-charts-rendered-as-full-circles-covex1210tra"
       & "nsitive-spacing"">H1: Pie charts rendered as full circles; "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "covex1.21.0transitive"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " spacing</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Both reported regressions from 1.21.0 are fixed:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>pie-type charts (overview collation, Charts tab, dependencies scope)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "were fed 0..100 values into unitless 0..1 properties, drawing each"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "slice as a full circle; now correct with a real donut hole.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>the dependency tree"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s name/version/scope badges collapsed together"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "when CSS copy-paste or slow load lost <code>gap</code>; markup now carries"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "explicit textual spacing and <code>line-break</code> safety.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""test-suite""><a class=""header"" href=""#test-suite"">Test Suite</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>900 tests passing (886 -&gt; 900) across 14 categories.  New <code>SBOM g"
       & "enerator</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "checks pin the language-agnostic vendored discovery: npm packages under"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>node_modules</code> register as <code>pkg:npm/...@version</code> (shal"
       & "low), a mixed-language"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>vendor/</code> directory becomes one component whose <code>Language</c"
       & "ode> lists the top-3"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "source-extension languages, and loose files under a vendor root never become"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "components.  The dashboard renderer test that pinned a stale template"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "heading now pins the Credits tab content instead (the template was"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "reorganised in this release).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""proof-results""><a class=""header"" href=""#proof-results"">Proof Results"
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Platinum, 720/720 VCs proved (unchanged from 1.21.0): the radar, radial"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "gauge, tier, and removal digs all live in default-off renderer bodies or are"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "pure CSS in the inlined dashboard template, and the vendored-discovery code"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "sits in the parser"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s I/O/container-heavy default-off body "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " not new SPARK"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "obligations.  0 unproved, 0 justified.  Re-verified with"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>adacovex prove --target=. --force</code> under gnatprove 16.1.0.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""traceability""><a class=""header"" href=""#traceability"">Traceability</a"
       & "></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>No new HLRs.  Coverage:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-DASH</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " C1 chart variety/pie, C2 robustness radar + tier"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "rating, C3 footer, C4 nomnoml, C5 spacing/badges, C6 checkbox icons,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "C8 resource modularisation + minify, C9 dep detail panel, C10 per-tab"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "minis + search separation;</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-MANIFEST</code> / <code>HLR-SBOM</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " C7 language-agnostic vendored discovery"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and SBOM language fields.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-DOC</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>Comp</code>/tier documentation in <code>docs/dashboard.md</code>;</li"
       & ">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-SERVER</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>__VERSION__</code> footer injection; Credits tab;</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-SBOM</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " C11 language-detection documentation.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>See <code>docs/dashboard.md</code>, <code>docs/sbom.md</code>, <code>docs"
       & "/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                    </main>"
