       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""adacovex-1260""><a class=""header"" href=""#adac"
       & "ovex-1260"">adacovex 1.26.0</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Date: <em>2026-08-24</em></p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Version bumped 1.25.0 -&gt; 1.26.0.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""changes""><a class=""header"" href=""#changes"">Changes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c1-perf-bench-target-wired-to-makefile""><a class=""header"" href=""#c1-"
       & "perf-bench-target-wired-to-makefile"">C1: perf-bench target wired to Makefile"
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>tools/perf-bench.py</code> is now exposed as <code>make perf-bench<"
       & "/code>, providing a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dedicated perf/strace profiling target alongside the existing <code>bench</c"
       & "ode>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "hyperfine target.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c2-spark_mode-off-restricted-to-documented-exceptions""><a class=""hea"
       & "der"" href=""#c2-spark_mode-off-restricted-to-documented-exceptions"">C2: SPARK"
       & "_Mode Off restricted to documented exceptions</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Verified that <code>SPARK_Mode (Off)</code> and <code>SPARK_Mode =&gt; Of"
       & "f</code> appear only in the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "three documented exception packages: <code>adacovex-complexity</code> (non-f"
       & "ormal"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Ada.Containers), <code>adacovex-types</code> (Subprogram_Vectors container),"
       & " and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>adacovex-cpus.Get_Temp_Directory</code> (Ada.Environment_Variables).</"
       & "p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c3-dedicated-credits-file""><a class=""header"" href=""#c3-dedicated-cre"
       & "dits-file"">C3: Dedicated credits file</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Added <code>docs/CREDITS.md</code> as the dedicated acknowledgements file"
       & ". It lists"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "adacovex credits and points to <code>docs/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md</code> for "
       & "full"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "third-party license details.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c4-requirements-table""><a class=""header"" href=""#c4-requirements-tabl"
       & "e"">C4: Requirements table</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Added <code>docs/requirements.md</code> with a table that categorises dep"
       & "endencies as"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Core, Development, or Good to have. Alire-managed dependencies are listed"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "under their Alire crate names.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c5-docs-rewritten-in-asd-ste100""><a class=""header"" href=""#c5-docs-re"
       & "written-in-asd-ste100"">C5: Docs rewritten in ASD-STE100</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>User documentation now follows ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English ru"
       & "les:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "short sentences, active voice, one instruction per sentence, consistent"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "terminology, and no AI-slop hedging. See"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "https://github.com/AminBlg/SimpleEnglish for the skill reference.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c6-simpleenglish-skill-reference-in-agentsmd""><a class=""header"" href"
       & "=""#c6-simpleenglish-skill-reference-in-agentsmd"">C6: SimpleEnglish skill ref"
       & "erence in AGENTS.md</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>AGENTS.md now references the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a href=""https://github.com/AminBlg/SimpleEnglish"">AminBlg/SimpleEnglish</a>"
       & " skill for"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "technical writing guidance.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c7-british-english-in-inline-source-comments""><a class=""header"" href"
       & "=""#c7-british-english-in-inline-source-comments"">C7: British English in inli"
       & "ne source comments</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>British English now also covers inline (non-docstring) source comments"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "across the Ada sources.  This completes the spelling pass: docstrings"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "were already converted, and the remaining American spellings (analyse,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "colour, normalise, synthesise, licence, honour, centre, and friends)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "were updated to match the AGENTS.md technical-writing convention.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c8-hardened-ascii-and-link-checks-skills-directory-excluded""><a clas"
       & "s=""header"" href=""#c8-hardened-ascii-and-link-checks-skills-directory-exclude"
       & "d"">C8: Hardened ASCII and link checks; skills directory excluded</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code>ascii-check</code> makefile target was rewritten to be less bri"
       & "ttle: it now"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "runs a single recursive grep with explicit include and exclude patterns"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "instead of a nested find loop over extensions, and it no longer relies on"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tab escapes inside bracket expressions.  The vendored <code>skills/</code> d"
       & "irectory"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "is excluded from the ASCII check (its skill files legitimately carry"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "non-ASCII punctuation such as em-dashes).  The link checker now also"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "skips <code>skills/</code>, so vendored third-party content is never gated b"
       & "y our"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "repo checks.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
