       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""adacovex-1270""><a class=""header"" href=""#adac"
       & "ovex-1270"">adacovex 1.27.0</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Date: <em>2026-08-24</em></p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Version bumped 1.26.0 -&gt; 1.27.0.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""changes""><a class=""header"" href=""#changes"">Changes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c1-prove-run-no-longer-emits-gnat-temp-files""><a class=""header"" href"
       & "=""#c1-prove-run-no-longer-emits-gnat-temp-files"">C1: Prove run no longer emi"
       & "ts GNAT-TEMP files</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code>--suppress-warnings</code> output capture used <code>GNAT. OS_L"
       & "ib. Create_Temp_File</code>, which writes a <code>GNAT-TEMP-XXXXX. TMP</code"
       & "> file into the current directory.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>An interrupted run left that file in the project tree, and the <code>.git"
       & "ignore</code> entry <code>*.tmp</code> is case-sensitive, so the <code>. TMP"
       & "</code> suffix showed up in <code>git status</code>. The capture file now li"
       & "ves in the system temp directory (`Adacovex. CPUs.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Get_Temp_Directory<code>) under a PID-suffixed name, following the existi"
       & "ng VCS snapshot convention. A defensive </code>.gitignore<code>entry for</co"
       & "de><em>. TMP<code>and</code>GNAT-TEMP-</em>` was added as well.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c2-ste100-technical-names-dictionary""><a class=""header"" href=""#c2-st"
       & "e100-technical-names-dictionary"">C2: STE100 Technical Names dictionary</a></"
       & "h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Added <code>docs/ste100-technical-names.md</code>, the controlled list of"
       & " Technical"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Names (non-STE words) for the adacovex domain, per ASD-STE100 Section 1"
       & ASCII.LF
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "Words"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & ". The dictionary organises entries into the four STE categories"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(Hardware and System Entities, Ada Language Constructs, Domain and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Mathematical Terms, Code Identifier Names). Every entry carries the five"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "required fields: approved word, part of speech, approved meaning,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "non-approved alternatives, and an example sentence.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c3-ste100-rewrite-audit-of-docs-and-api-reference""><a class=""header"""
       & " href=""#c3-ste100-rewrite-audit-of-docs-and-api-reference"">C3: STE100 rewrit"
       & "e audit of docs and API reference</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Audited the STE100-rewritten user documentation and the generated API"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "reference for dropped jargon. All important technical terms survived the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "rewrite (Alire, gnatprove, GNAT, manifest, SBOM, CycloneDX, SPDX, DAL,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "ASIL, HLR, LLR, verification conditions, pragma, aspect, contract,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "subprogram, and friends). One garbled sentence in <code>docs/architecture.md"
       & "</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "was corrected.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c4-documentation-index-pages-for-docs-and-every-docs-subdirectory""><"
       & "a class=""header"" href=""#c4-documentation-index-pages-for-docs-and-every-docs"
       & "-subdirectory"">C4: Documentation index pages for docs and every docs subdire"
       & "ctory</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Added <code>docs/index.md</code> (the top-level documentation landing pag"
       & "e) and index pages for the subdirectories that lacked one: <code>docs/proof/"
       & "index.md</code> (proof records), <code>docs/compliance/index.md</code> (VERI"
       & "FICATION.md, TRACE.md, and the HLR/LLR indexes), and <code>docs/badges/index"
       & ".md</code> (the SVG badge set). Every index states that the documentation us"
       & "es British English and ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English and points at"
       & " the <code>docs/ste100-technical-names.md</code> dictionary. The generated A"
       & "PI reference index (<code>docs/api-docs/index.md</code>) now opens with a "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "How to read this reference"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " section written for end users, contributors, and maintainers; it links the "
       & "CLI reference, the standards pages, the contributing guide, the architecture"
       & " notes, the proof ledger, the changelogs, and the STE100 dictionary. The API"
       & "-docs reader guide lives in <code>tools/rst2md.py</code> so <code>make doc</"
       & "code> regenerates it instead of overwriting a hand-edited file.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code>tools/doc-links.map</code> and the AGENTS.md documentation bloc"
       & "k now list the new index pages.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c5-sbom-system-tool-scan-rewritten-as-a-single-pass-word-scan""><a cl"
       & "ass=""header"" href=""#c5-sbom-system-tool-scan-rewritten-as-a-single-pass-word"
       & "-scan"">C5: SBOM system-tool scan rewritten as a single-pass word scan</a></h"
       & "3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>Discover_System_Dev_Deps</code> matched every line against every sy"
       & "stem tool with a per-tool substring loop (60 tools x line length). It domina"
       & "tes the whole warm assessment pipeline: profiling showed 76% of warm-path CP"
       & "U in <code>Line_Refers_To</code> / <code>Match_At</code>. The replacement wa"
       & "lks each line once, extracts maximal <code>[a-z0-9_-]</code> words, and comp"
       & "ares each word against the tool table by length first. Match semantics are i"
       & "dentical and the cmp is per-word, so <code>make</code> still matches in <cod"
       & "e>make build</code>, <code>Makefile</code> still does not match (capital M),"
       & " and <code>python</code> still does not match in <code>python3</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Warm self-assessment dropped from ~1021 ms to ~63 ms (16x) on the benchma"
       & "rk machine.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c6-tool-output-directories-excluded-from-both-tree-walks""><a class="""
       & "header"" href=""#c6-tool-output-directories-excluded-from-both-tree-walks"">C6:"
       & " Tool-output directories excluded from both tree walks</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The SBOM dev-dependency walk and the source scan walked every directory"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "except the blacklist. A <code>gnatprove/</code> output directory (thousands "
       & "of"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "files after a proof run) and <code>__pycache__</code>, <code>node_modules</c"
       & "ode>, <code>.headroom</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and <code>.lccst</code> directories were therefore enumerated and cleaned on"
       & " every"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "run. All five names are now skipped by both walks; the remaining syscall"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "noise on warm runs is glibc hwcaps startup probing, not adacovex code.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c7-cache-eviction-batched""><a class=""header"" href=""#c7-cache-evictio"
       & "n-batched"">C7: Cache eviction batched</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>Put_Cached</code> ran <code>Evict_If_Needed</code> after every stor"
       & "e; <code>Evict_If_Needed</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "walks the whole cache tree (<code>readdir</code> + <code>stat</code> per ent"
       & "ry). A cold run"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "that stores one blob per source file therefore walked the cache once per"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "file. Eviction now runs every 32 stores, so a bounded overshoot of at"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "most 31 entries is the steady state and a cold run walks the tree once or"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "twice. This is part of the cold-run improvement (~1.4 s to ~0.55 s).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c8-cpusget_temp_directory-and-spark-mode-off-exceptions""><a class=""h"
       & "eader"" href=""#c8-cpusget_temp_directory-and-spark-mode-off-exceptions"">C8: <"
       & "code>CPUs.Get_Temp_Directory</code> and SPARK Mode Off exceptions</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>1.26.0 restricted <code>SPARK_Mode (Off)</code> to three documented excep"
       & "tions. Each"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "was re-verified against gnatprove 16.1.0 with minimal scratch units:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>A <code>SPARK_Mode =&gt; On</code> unit instantiating non-formal"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Ada. Containers. Vectors</code> is rejected by flow analysis: it says "
       & "the instantiation is "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "not allowed in SPARK (due to entity declared with SPARK_Mode Off)"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & ". The `Adacovex.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Types. Implementation<code>and</code>Adacovex. Complexity<code>container "
       & "packages are therefore the two irreducible exceptions, and the Makefile</cod"
       & "e>spark-off-check` gate now allows exactly those two.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>Ada.Environment_Variables</code> reads were never SPARK-blocked. A"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>SPARK_Mode =&gt; On</code> function calling <code>Exists</code> / <cod"
       & "e>Value</code> proves clean,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "with <code>[assumed-global-null]</code> warnings because the runtime has no"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Global contracts. <code>CPUs.Get_Temp_Directory</code> therefore returned to"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>SPARK_Mode =&gt; On</code> with <code>Global =&gt; null</code> (spec a"
       & "nd body), and its"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "docstring in <code>docs/</code> was corrected. The full proof now reports 72"
       & "4"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "VCs, 0 unproved, 0 justified (Platinum), with the ledger listing the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "six <code>[assumed-global-null]</code> warnings.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The evidence and the skipped-units audit are recorded in"
