       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""adacovex-1280""><a class=""header"" href=""#adac"
       & "ovex-1280"">adacovex 1.28.0</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Date: <em>2026-08-25</em></p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Version bumped 1.27.0 -&gt; 1.28.0.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""changes""><a class=""header"" href=""#changes"">Changes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c1-perfmd-updated-with-measured-numbers-and-optimisation-history""><a"
       & " class=""header"" href=""#c1-perfmd-updated-with-measured-numbers-and-optimisat"
       & "ion-history"">C1: perf.md updated with measured numbers and optimisation hist"
       & "ory</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>docs/perf.md</code> now records the 1.28.0 benchmark figures (cold "
       & "~0.6 s, warm"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "~40 ms on the self-assessment, 9.0 MiB binary / 3.6 MiB stripped), the new"
       & ASCII.LF
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "when the numbers regress"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " workflow, and the full optimisation history in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "reverse-chronological order so each future round can see which assumption"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "drove the previous change.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c2-stamp-fast-path-hashing-for-the-scan-cache""><a class=""header"" hre"
       & "f=""#c2-stamp-fast-path-hashing-for-the-scan-cache"">C2: Stamp fast-path hashi"
       & "ng for the scan cache</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The warm-path CPU profile showed GNAT. SHA256 at ~48%: every <code>.ads</"
       & "code> file was fully re-read and re-hashed on every run just to compute its "
       & "cache key, even when the content was unchanged. <code>Adacovex. Cache. Hash_"
       & "File</code> now keeps an in-memory path -&gt; (size, digest) stamp map and s"
       & "erves the recorded digest without opening the file when the size still match"
       & "es.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The fast path is per-process (the map is not persisted), so an edited fil"
       & "e always re-hashes: its size differs or the map is empty. The same map means"
       & " the SBOM tree-walk hashing reuses the digests the source scan computed in t"
       & "he same run, collapsing two hash passes into one read plus one size check. W"
       & "arm user time dropped by roughly a third on the self-target.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c3-sbom-system-tool-referenced-set-cache""><a class=""header"" href=""#c"
       & "3-sbom-system-tool-referenced-set-cache"">C3: SBOM system-tool referenced-set"
       & " cache</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>Discover_System_Dev_Deps</code> walked the whole project tree and w"
       & "ord-scanned every dev-facing file on every run to collect the system-tool de"
       & "v dependencies for the SBOM. A profile showed that word scan at ~62% of warm"
       & " CPU. The referenced-tool set is now cached on disk under a key that covers "
       & "every input the scan reads: the content hash of exactly the files the scan r"
       & "eads (same <code>Should_Scan</code> predicate and directory exclusions as th"
       & "e main walk), the curated tool-table names (in case the table changes within"
       & " a release), and a namespace salt. An unchanged project serves the set from "
       & "one small cache blob and skips the tree walk and every file read; any edit t"
       & "o a scanned file changes the key and forces a re-scan.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Cold runs pay one extra tree walk (about 8% of cold); warm runs skip the "
       & "entire SBOM scan, taking the warm self-assessment from ~58 ms to ~39 ms. A u"
       & "nit test round-trips the cache: a second discovery on the same fixture and c"
       & "ache dir agrees exactly with the first, including tools that are absent from"
       & " PATH.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c4-formal-containers-experiment-confirms-the-two-spark_mode-off-exce"
       & "ptions""><a class=""header"" href=""#c4-formal-containers-experiment-confirms-th"
       & "e-two-spark_mode-off-exceptions"">C4: Formal-containers experiment confirms t"
       & "he two SPARK_Mode Off exceptions</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code>Adacovex.Complexity</code> package was probed as a candidate fo"
       & "r moving to"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "SPARK-approved (formal) containers so its <code>SPARK_Mode (Off)</code> coul"
       & "d be"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "removed. Scratch units under gnatprove 16.1.0 show this is not viable:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>The GNAT 16.2.1 runtime formal containers"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>Ada. Containers. Formal_Vectors</code> and friends) are <code>pragma "
       & "Compile_Time_Error</code> stubs; the implementations moved to the SPARK libr"
       & "ary shipped inside the gnatprove toolchain (`SPARK. Containers.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Formal.*`).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Adopting them would make the crate depend at build time on the SPARK"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "library, breaking the zero-dependency contract: gnatprove is resolved at"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "run time by the <code>prove</code> subcommand, but the containers would be a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "compile-time dependency.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>The <code>Complexity</code> aggregates embed vector components; the form"
       & "al"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "containers"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & " limited private <code>Vector</code> cannot be a record component, so a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cursor-iteration data-flow rewrite would be required on top of the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "library change.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Verdict recorded in <code>docs/proof/16.1.0-ledger.md</code>: <code>Adaco"
       & "vex. Complexity</code> and <code>Adacovex. Types. Implementation</code> rema"
       & "in the only two <code>SPARK_Mode (Off)</code> packages, both for the same re"
       & "ason (non-formal `Ada.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Containers<code>instantiations), and</code>spark-off-check` allows exactl"
       & "y these two.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c5-makefile-parsing-moved-to-pure-python-tools""><a class=""header"" hr"
       & "ef=""#c5-makefile-parsing-moved-to-pure-python-tools"">C5: Makefile parsing mo"
       & "ved to pure-Python tools</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Several <code>make</code> targets formatted or parsed text with shell one"
       & "-liners that"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "broke under some shells (<code>awk</code>"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "backslash not last character on line"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & ASCII.LF
       & "inside the <code>bench</code> size report) and used GNU-only filters (<code>"
       & "grep -P</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>sed -i</code>, <code>sort -V</code>) that do not exist on BSD/macOS. T"
       & "he parsing and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "formatting moved to pure-stdlib Python scripts so the targets behave the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "same on every platform:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>tools/bench-size.py</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>make bench</code>"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s binary-size report (stats the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "files itself; no more <code>stat -c</code> + awk quoting).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>tools/ascii-check.py</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the ASCII gate (no <code>grep -P</code>; tab and LF are"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "allowed, CR still fails, so CRLF line endings are caught).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>tools/spark-off-check.py</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the <code>SPARK_Mode (Off)</code> gate.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>tools/versions.py</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " version read / <code>set-version</code> / version-aware"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "filter (replaces <code>sed</code>/<code>sort -V</code> in <code>release</cod"
       & "e>, <code>test-publish</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>coverage-gate</code>).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>tools/bump-version.py</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the whole <code>make bump-version</code> recipe"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(manifest rewrites, release-file/index scaffolding, changelog"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "scaffolding, description sync).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>tools/filter-sframe.py</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the build-log SFrame-notice filter"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>make build</code>).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>tools/rst2md.py --prune-test-pages</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " drops test-page links from the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "API-docs index (replaces two <code>sed -i</code> calls in <code>make doc</co"
       & "de>).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The recipes that remain in the Makefile are plain POSIX pipelines"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>head</code>, <code>tail</code>, <code>grep -E</code>, <code>cmp</code"
       & ">, <code>ls</code>); there is no GNU-only filter or"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "inline awk left.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c6-system-tool-probes-moved-to-a-stable-machine-level-store""><a clas"
       & "s=""header"" href=""#c6-system-tool-probes-moved-to-a-stable-machine-level-stor"
       & "e"">C6: system-tool probes moved to a stable machine-level store</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The cold-path profile showed the SBOM system-tool version probes (each a "
       & "subprocess; node/hg/mandb boot an interpreter) dominating cold runs. They we"
       & "re cached under the result cache, so wiping the cache or pointing <code>--ca"
       & "che-dir</code> elsewhere re-probed every tool. They now live in <code>~/.ada"
       & "covex/probes/</code> (7-day TTL) outside the result cache, and the reference"
       & "d-tools cache blob stores each tool"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s probe result so a cache hit rebuilds the SBOM tool edges without PATH look"
       & "ups, probe reads, or spawns. Cold on a warm-probe machine dropped from ~658 "
       & "ms to ~86 ms (7.7x); warm from ~39.8 ms to ~34.6 ms.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The blob layout is names-<code>|</code>-version-pairs and <code>Cache_Sch"
       & "ema</code> was bumped to s6 so names-only blobs from the earlier layout are "
       & "never served as complete.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c7-dashboard-dependency-graph-versions-direct-links-real-packages""><"
       & "a class=""header"" href=""#c7-dashboard-dependency-graph-versions-direct-links-"
       & "real-packages"">C7: Dashboard dependency graph: versions, direct links, real "
       & "packages</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The dashboard dependency graph (and the SBOM that shares it) no longer"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "lists things that are not packages, and every listed package carries a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "version and a direct registry link:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>The four vendored dashboard libraries (FlexSearch, nomnoml, graphre,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Charts.css) are now versioned (<code>0.7.31</code> / <code>1.7.0</code> / <c"
       & "ode>0.1.3</code> / <code>1.2.0</code>)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "with <code>pkg:npm</code> PURLs.  adacovex"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s own dashboard sources"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>resources/dashboard.*</code>) are not a package and never become"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "components.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>node_modules</code> scanning resolves scoped packages"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>node_modules/@scope/pkg</code> becomes <code>@scope/pkg@&lt;version&g"
       & "t;</code> from its"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>package.json</code>, so the e2e fixture yields <code>@playwright/test@"
       & "1.62.1</code>)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and skips pnpm"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s virtual store and shim dirs (<code>.pnpm</code>, <code>.bin</code>)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "entirely.  <code>.pnpm</code> is not a dependency; the <code>pnpm</code> bin"
       & "ary is, and stays"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the dev tool.  The SBOM and the dashboard now render the same list.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>The dep-details Link row builds direct GitHub / GitLab / Bitbucket /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "npm / crates.io / PyPI / pkg.go.dev / Alire links from the PURL"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(scoped npm names included) and no longer falls back to a GitHub"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "search URL for unknown ecosystems.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c8-proof-categories-match-gnatproves-summary-table""><a class=""header"
       & """ href=""#c8-proof-categories-match-gnatproves-summary-table"">C8: Proof categ"
       & "ories match gnatprove"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s summary table</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>gnatprove 16 reports flow analysis as "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "Data Dependencies"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " (checked) plus"
       & ASCII.LF
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "Flow Dependencies"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " (proved implicitly), and the dashboard"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s Flow row"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "read only the Flow Dependencies row "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " showing 0/0 on the self-target"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "while gnatprove showed 56 checked data-dependency VCs.  The parser now"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "sums both rows into the Flow category and computes every category"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "proved count as Total - Justified - Unproved (Termination previously"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "showed 73/94 instead of 94/94).  The Proof tab table and the Charts"
       & ASCII.LF
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "Proof Check Types"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " column gained a Termination row, so the per-category"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "numbers sum exactly to gnatprove"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s Total (56 + 5 + 407 + 107 + 55 +"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "94 = 724).  <code>Cache_Schema</code> bumped <code>s6</code> -&gt; <code>s7<"
       & "/code> (parser semantics).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c10-makefile-orchestration-moved-to-dedicated-python-tools""><a class"
       & "=""header"" href=""#c10-makefile-orchestration-moved-to-dedicated-python-tools"""
       & ">C10: Makefile orchestration moved to dedicated Python tools</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Beyond the pure parsing ports in C5, every multi-step <code>make</code> r"
       & "ecipe now"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "delegates to a dedicated stdlib-Python script, so the Makefile is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "declarative and each flow is individually testable:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>tools/build.py</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the build flow (<code>gen-version</code> + <code>gen-dashboard</code> +"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>alr build</code> with the SFrame log filter + the <code>covex</code> s"
       & "ymlink).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>tools/dev-cmd.py</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the alire-dev.toml swap behind <code>make doc</code> /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>make fmt</code>, restored unconditionally (including on Ctrl-C / SIGTE"
       & "RM)."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "The swap uses a fresh-mtime copy: <code>alr exec</code> re-synchronises the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "workspace only when <code>alire.toml</code> is strictly newer than"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>alire/alire.lock</code>, so a metadata-preserving copy silently skippe"
       & "d the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "sync and gnatdoc / gnatformat never reached the exec PATH.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>tools/bench.py</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the cold/warm hyperfine (or measured) benchmark"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "plus the stripped-binary-size report.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>tools/coverage-gate.py</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the release-tag docstring delta in a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "temporary worktree, removed even when the assessment fails.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>tools/run.py</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the single owner of the <code>prove</code> / <code>run-self</code> / <code>"
       & "sbom</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "/ <code>run-ada-crdt</code> invocation shape (SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH + acceptance"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "gates); <code>run.py assess-args</code> feeds the release flow, so the gate "
       & "flags"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "live in exactly one place.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>tools/release.py</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the whole release flow (prove, build, validate,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "coverage gate, changelogs, bundling, attestation, manifest bumps,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tag/push), with <code>make release DRY_RUN=1</code> running everything excep"
       & "t the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "irreversible commit/tag/push.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>tools/tests.py</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " a stdlib-<code>unittest</code> suite over the tools"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & " pure"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "logic (26 tests), wired into <code>make check</code> as the <code>tools-chec"
       & "k</code> gate.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The ASCII gate now skips the gitignored generated Playwright output"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>tests/e2e/playwright-report/</code>, <code>tests/e2e/test-results/</c"
       & "ode>), which"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "previously tripped the gate after a local <code>make e2e</code> run.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c11-gnatprove-run-is-warning-free""><a class=""header"" href=""#c11-gnat"
       & "prove-run-is-warning-free"">C11: gnatprove run is warning-free</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The six <code>[assumed-global-null]</code> warnings from"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>CPUs.Get_Temp_Directory</code>"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <code>Ada.Environment_Variables</code> reads are"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "silenced in the source: the function scopes a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>pragma Warnings (Off, ""no Global contract available"")</code> around it"
       & "self"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(re-enabled immediately after), which gnatprove honours by message"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "prefix.  The proof surface is unchanged "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " still 724/724 VCs, 0"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "unproved, 0 justified.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c9-dashboard-chart-filter-diagram-and-credits-fixes""><a class=""heade"
       & "r"" href=""#c9-dashboard-chart-filter-diagram-and-credits-fixes"">C9: Dashboard"
       & " chart, filter, diagram and credits fixes</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Pie/donut data numbers are upright: Charts.css rotates each slice"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "value by its midpoint angle, so a full proved ring (0..1 turn)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "rendered the "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "724 VCs"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " number rotated 180 degrees.  Overridden to"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>transform: none</code>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>The test-category bar chart is sized to its category count (<code>--rows"
       & "</code>),"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "so a 14-category suite no longer clips its last rows; column charts"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "with more than eight categories rotate their labels vertically instead"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "of overlapping.  The Overview tests donut no longer overflows its card.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>The dep name filter and scope checkboxes actually work: the filter"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "used <code>Map</code> bracket access (<code>info[n]</code>), which threw on "
       & "every keystroke"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and aborted the run, so typing a name or unchecking a scope changed"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "nothing.  Fixed to <code>info.get(n)</code>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>The nomnoml diagram now derives every colour (fill, background,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "stroke, line, font, note) from the active theme"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s CSS custom"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "properties and re-renders when the theme changes, so light and dark"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "no longer produce identical (default-yellow) diagrams.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>The Credits tab fills the Playwright version from the resolved graph"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>@playwright/test@1.62.1</code>) instead of showing a static "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "dev"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & ".</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""fixes""><a class=""header"" href=""#fixes"">Fixes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h1-cold-cache-runs-no-longer-re-probe-the-whole-toolchain""><a class="
       & """header"" href=""#h1-cold-cache-runs-no-longer-re-probe-the-whole-toolchain"">H"
       & "1: Cold-cache runs no longer re-probe the whole toolchain</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Before 1.28.0-era cache wipes, a wiped <code>--cache-dir</code> re-probed"
       & " every"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "referenced tool. After these changes a fresh result cache on a machine"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "with warm probes skips every spawn. First-run-on-machine cost unchanged.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h2-make-e2e-runs-the-dashboard-suite-again""><a class=""header"" href="""
       & "#h2-make-e2e-runs-the-dashboard-suite-again"">H2: <code>make e2e</code> runs "
       & "the dashboard suite again</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The Playwright web-server wiring referenced a script that does not"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "exist (<code>tools/start-dashboard-server.py</code>), and the launcher compu"
       & "ted the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "repository root one level too deep "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " both fixed.  The suite now runs"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "serially (a single-process dashboard server cannot serve a fully"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "parallel browser swarm), and the stale layout expectations were updated"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "for the current dashboard (card counts, scope badges, chart count,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "credits links), plus new coverage for the dep name filter and the scope"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "checkboxes fixed in C9.  15 e2e tests pass.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""test-suite""><a class=""header"" href=""#test-suite"">Test Suite</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>973 tests passing across 14 categories (5 new: the tools-set cache"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "round-trip in the SBOM suite; the probe-store change keeps the same"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "count).  The GNATprove parser tests cover both summary layouts (legacy"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "3-column and modern 6-column rows).  15 Playwright dashboard layout"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tests pass via <code>make e2e</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""proof-results""><a class=""header"" href=""#proof-results"">Proof Results"
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Platinum, 724/724 VCs proved under gnatprove 16.1.0. 0 unproved, 0"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "justified. <code>CPUs.Get_Temp_Directory</code> scopes a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>pragma Warnings (Off, ""no Global contract available"")</code> around it"
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Ada.Environment_Variables</code> reads (the GNAT runtime carries no Gl"
       & "obal"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "contracts for them), so the run is warning-free.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""traceability""><a class=""header"" href=""#traceability"">Traceability</a"
       & "></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>No new HLRs. Coverage:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-CACHE</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " C2 stamp fast-path hashing, C3 tools-set cache,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "C6 probe-store change, C8 Cache_Schema s7 bump.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-SBOM</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " C3 tools-set cache keyed on the scanned file set"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "storing probe results (C6), C7 dependency-graph package fixes.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-ARCH</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " C1 perf.md documentation, C4 formal-containers"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "verdict, C5 Python-tooling port.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>RENDER-HTML</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " C8 proof-category consistency, C9 dashboard"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "chart/filter/diagram/credits fixes, H2 e2e suite.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>See <code>docs/perf.md</code>, <code>docs/proof/16.1.0-ledger.md</code>.<"
       & "/p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                    </main>"
