       & "                    <main>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""adacovex-1300""><a class=""header"" href=""#adac"
       & "ovex-1300"">adacovex 1.30.0</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Date: <em>2026-08-26</em></p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Version bumped 1.29.0 -&gt; 1.30.0.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""changes""><a class=""header"" href=""#changes"">Changes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c1-system-dependencies-get-a-first-class-system-scope""><a class=""hea"
       & "der"" href=""#c1-system-dependencies-get-a-first-class-system-scope"">C1: Syste"
       & "m dependencies get a first-class <code>system</code> scope</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The dependency graph now models system tools (<code>python3</code>, <code"
       & ">git</code>, <code>gnatprove</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and more) as a dedicated <code>system</code> scope, distinct from <code>base"
       & "</code>, <code>dev</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>transitive</code>, and <code>vendored</code>. The dashboard gives the "
       & "scope its own filter"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "checkbox, badge colour, and legend entry; the SBOM lists it under <code>syst"
       & "em</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "scope; and the <code>/api/deps</code> JSON reports <code>scope: ""system""</co"
       & "de>. A system"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dependency"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s detail panel still notes that no external link or licence is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "provisioned "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " only the resolved version is shown. Both the dashboard and the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "SBOM run the same <code>Discover_System_Dev_Deps</code> discovery, so they s"
       & "how the same"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "system dependencies.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c2-flexible-ecosystem-licence-resolution""><a class=""header"" href=""#c"
       & "2-flexible-ecosystem-licence-resolution"">C2: Flexible ecosystem licence reso"
       & "lution</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>Read_Vendor_Manifest</code> reads the <code>license</code> field fr"
       & "om each vendored package"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "manifest (<code>package.json</code> for npm/pnpm, <code>Cargo.toml</code> fo"
       & "r cargo,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>pyproject.toml</code>/<code>composer.json</code> for pypi/composer) an"
       & "d carries it onto the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "SBOM component and the dashboard detail panel. When the local manifest carri"
       & "es"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "no licence, the new <code>Resolve_Ecosystem_Metadata</code> resolver falls b"
       & "ack to the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "package registry. The resolver dispatches on the ecosystem (the PURL type)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "through a single static table, so adding a language is one row rather than a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "new code path:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>npm</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>npm view &lt;pkg&gt; license</code>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>pnpm</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>pnpm show &lt;pkg&gt; license</code>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>cargo</strong> (Rust) "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>cargo search &lt;pkg&gt;</code>, with the SPDX id read from the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>(license: ...)</code> token in the output.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>go</strong> and other ecosystems with no portable, reliable regi"
       & "stry query keep"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "an empty licence; the vendored manifest scanner still reads any in-repo"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "licence file.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The fallback runs only when the offline read finds nothing, so a vendored"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "package that ships a licence never touches the network.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The bundled third-party libraries that the dashboard vendors (Charts.css,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "FlexSearch, nomnoml, graphre) now report their known upstream licence (MIT o"
       & "r"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Apache-2.0) from a built-in table. The Credits tab and the SBOM therefore li"
       & "st"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "them with a licence rather than a blank.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c3-dependency-detail-panel-is-the-single-richer-source-dry""><a class"
       & "=""header"" href=""#c3-dependency-detail-panel-is-the-single-richer-source-dry"""
       & ">C3: Dependency detail panel is the single, richer source (DRY)</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The dependency detail panel is now the one place that shows a dependency"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "full detail. It adds the <code>Language</code> and <code>Description</code> "
       & "fields (already present"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "in <code>/api/deps</code>) and a per-dependency system-tool note, so the Tre"
       & "e and Diagram"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "views open the same, complete panel instead of each carrying a partial copy."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "The <code>/api/deps</code> JSON gains a <code>description</code> field to su"
       & "pport this.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c4-e2e-tooling-reorganised""><a class=""header"" href=""#c4-e2e-tooling-"
       & "reorganised"">C4: e2e tooling reorganised</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The ad-hoc <code>repro*.mjs</code> scripts at the root of <code>tests/e2e"
       & "/</code> moved into"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>tests/e2e/repro/</code> so the suite root holds only the Playwright co"
       & "nfig, the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "spec, and the server bootstrap. The spec gains assertions for the split-view"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "toggle and the system-dependency badge.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c5-no-source-file-may-exceed-10-of-the-codebase""><a class=""header"" h"
       & "ref=""#c5-no-source-file-may-exceed-10-of-the-codebase"">C5: No source file ma"
       & "y exceed 10% of the codebase</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The complexity gate now rejects any source file that exceeds 10% of the t"
       & "otal"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "codebase size (the <code>Max_File_Pct</code> gate in <code>adacovex_main.adb"
       & "</code>), so a single"
       & ASCII.LF
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "god object"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " can no longer dominate the tree. The gate counts only real"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "subprogram-bearing code "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " comments, blanks, and inline specs are excluded "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and fails loudly with the offending file and its share; <code>make complexit"
       & "y-check</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "exits non-zero when the cap is breached.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c6-complexity-report-reads-like-tokei""><a class=""header"" href=""#c6-c"
       & "omplexity-report-reads-like-tokei"">C6: Complexity report reads like tokei</a"
       & "></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>adacovex complexity</code> now prints a tokei-style summary (total "
       & "files, lines,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "code, comments, blanks, and the codebase loc percentage) followed by a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "per-file table. Each per-file row reports <code>Lines=</code>, <code>Code=</"
       & "code>, <code>Comments=</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Blanks=</code>, the loc percentage, and the cyclomatic complexity <cod"
       & "e>cx=</code>, with a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "legend line <code>Per-file (Lines / Code / Comments / Blanks / loc % / cx):<"
       & "/code>."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Over-long comment blocks and dash-only separator lines are classified as"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "comments, not code, so the counts match a plain <code>wc</code>-style read.<"
       & "/p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c7-registry-lookups-fetch-version-website-and-licence-in-one-call""><"
       & "a class=""header"" href=""#c7-registry-lookups-fetch-version-website-and-licenc"
       & "e-in-one-call"">C7: Registry lookups fetch version, website, and licence in o"
       & "ne call</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>Resolve_Ecosystem_Metadata</code> now resolves the version, website"
       & ", and licence"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "for a vendored package from the registry CLI (previously licence-only), and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>alr show</code> is folded into the same dispatch table so the three fi"
       & "elds come from"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "one place for every ecosystem. The npm and pnpm rows issue a single"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>view &lt;pkg&gt; version license homepage --json</code> call and parse"
       & " the JSON, so they"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "boot node once per component instead of once per field "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " a 3x reduction in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "subprocess starts that removes the main responsiveness cost the dependency"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "graph build paid on vendored JavaScript trees (and, by extension, on"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>make prove</code>, which builds the graph before gnatprove).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c8-bundled-dashboard-assets-resolve-their-licence-live""><a class=""he"
       & "ader"" href=""#c8-bundled-dashboard-assets-resolve-their-licence-live"">C8: Bun"
       & "dled dashboard assets resolve their licence live</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The four vendored dashboard libraries (Charts.css, FlexSearch, nomnoml,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "graphre) no longer carry a hard-coded licence in the SBOM builder.  When a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "loose vendored copy is scanned, the builder resolves the licence (and websit"
       & "e)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "from the package registry through <code>Resolve_Ecosystem_Metadata</code>, p"
       & "referring"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>pnpm show &lt;pkg&gt; license</code> and falling back to <code>npm</co"
       & "de>, <code>yarn</code>, then <code>bun</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "same preference chain used for every JavaScript component.  The SBOM and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Credits tab therefore track the real upstream licence instead of a built-in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "copy that could drift.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c9-registry-metadata-is-cached-per-project-so-warm-runs-skip-node""><"
       & "a class=""header"" href=""#c9-registry-metadata-is-cached-per-project-so-warm-r"
       & "uns-skip-node"">C9: Registry metadata is cached per project, so warm runs ski"
       & "p node</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>Resolve_Ecosystem_Metadata</code> now caches each package"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s licence, version, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "website in a per-project store under the project"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s result cache (the same"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>--cache-dir</code> the scan uses, so a project that sets its own cache"
       & " gets an"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "isolated meta store), keyed by the target directory as well as the ecosystem"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and package name, with the same 7-day TTL as the system-tool probe cache.  T"
       & "he"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "content-addressed result cache does not cover these registry calls (each one"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "boots node for npm/pnpm), so a "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "warm"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " <code>adacovex</code> run still paid for them "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "residual slowness on <code>make prove</code> after the result cache had alre"
       & "ady been"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "served.  The meta cache removes that cost: the first run resolves and caches"
       & ","
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and every later run (warm result cache or not) serves the answer from disk w"
       & "ith"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "zero subprocess spawns.  Keying by the target also means two projects that"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "share a cache directory never serve each other"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s resolved licence or version.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""fixes""><a class=""header"" href=""#fixes"">Fixes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h1-dependency-split-view-detail-panel-works-from-tree-and-diagram""><"
       & "a class=""header"" href=""#h1-dependency-split-view-detail-panel-works-from-tre"
       & "e-and-diagram"">H1: Dependency split-view detail panel works from Tree and Di"
       & "agram</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>1.29.0 claimed the split layout but the activating class was applied to t"
       & "he"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "wrong element (<code>#tab-deps</code> instead of <code>.dep-split</code>), s"
       & "o the flex split never"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "engaged and clicking a dependency showed nothing. The class now toggles on t"
       & "he"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>.dep-split</code> container, so selecting a dependency from either the"
       & " Tree or the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Diagram view docks the view on the left and opens the detail card on the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "right. By default (no selection) the view fills the container; the split"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "appears only on selection.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h2-spark-proof-radar-flow-label-no-longer-clipped""><a class=""header"""
       & " href=""#h2-spark-proof-radar-flow-label-no-longer-clipped"">H2: SPARK proof r"
       & "adar "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "Flow"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " label no longer clipped</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The radar SVGs used a <code>0 0 220 220</code> viewBox, which clipped the"
       & " top axis label"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "("
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "Flow"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " on the proof radar, "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "Docs"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " on the robustness radar) at the SVG edge."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "The viewBox now starts at <code>y = -14</code>, giving the top label headroo"
       & "m so all five"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "axis labels render.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h3-doc-coverage-caption-no-longer-overlaps-the-donut""><a class=""head"
       & "er"" href=""#h3-doc-coverage-caption-no-longer-overlaps-the-donut"">H3: Doc-cov"
       & "erage caption no longer overlaps the donut</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The doc-coverage card built its caption with a split HTML <code>style</co"
       & "de> attribute"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "that dropped <code>text-align:center;margin:6px 0 0</code>, so the "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "X% documented"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & ASCII.LF
       & "caption sat flush against the donut. The attribute is now a single, correct"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>style</code> string; the same malformed-attribute pattern on the Overv"
       & "iew badges"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "caption is fixed likewise.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h4-nomnoml-diagram-legend-removed-and-node-clicks-easier""><a class="""
       & "header"" href=""#h4-nomnoml-diagram-legend-removed-and-node-clicks-easier"">H4:"
       & " nomnoml diagram legend removed and node clicks easier</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The diagram"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <code>[&lt;note&gt; Legend: ...]</code> box is gone (the scope badges and "
       & "legend"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "already live in the Tree view). The canvas click hit-test now adds a small"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "slack around each box and, when boxes overlap, picks the smallest enclosing"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "box, so the tight text boxes are easy to hit and clicks near a boundary open"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the right dependency.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h5-dependency-graph-build-no-longer-spawns-three-registry-calls-per-"
       & "npmpnpm-component""><a class=""header"" href=""#h5-dependency-graph-build-no-lon"
       & "ger-spawns-three-registry-calls-per-npmpnpm-component"">H5: Dependency graph "
       & "build no longer spawns three registry calls per npm/pnpm component</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>1.30.0"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s licence fallback (C2) spawned one <code>npm view</code>/<code>pnpm show</c"
       & "ode> per field,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "so each vendored JavaScript component started three node processes. The grap"
       & "h"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "build now resolves the three fields from one <code>--json</code> call (C7), "
       & "cutting the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "node boots per component by 3x and removing the stall that made <code>make p"
       & "rove</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and self-assessment feel slow even with the result cache warm.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""test-suite""><a class=""header"" href=""#test-suite"">Test Suite</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>973 tests passing across 14 categories (unchanged: the dependency enrichm"
       & "ent"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and the licence resolution integrate with the existing graph builder without"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "changing the fixture counts).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""proof-results""><a class=""header"" href=""#proof-results"">Proof Results"
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Platinum, 724/724 VCs proved under gnatprove 16.1.0 (unchanged). The new"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Resolve_Ecosystem_Metadata</code> and the dependency enrichment run on"
       & "ly at"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "graph-build time and are outside the proof surface (the manifest parser body"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "is not in <code>SPARK_Mode On</code>).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""traceability""><a class=""header"" href=""#traceability"">Traceability</a"
       & "></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-SBOM</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " C1 system dependencies in the dashboard, C2 ecosystem and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "bundled-asset licence resolution, C7 version/website/licence resolution in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "one JSON call, C8 live bundled-asset licence via pnpm (then npm/yarn/bun),"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "C9 machine-level registry metadata cache; the SBOM spec carries the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "resolved licence for vendored packages.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>RENDER-HTML</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " C3 detail panel DRY, C4 e2e assertions, H1 split view,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "H2 radar label, H3 doc-coverage caption, H4 nomnoml legend/clicks.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-ARCH</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " C4 e2e tooling reorganisation, C5 10% file-size cap,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "C6 tokei-style complexity report, H5 single-call registry resolution,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "C9 registry metadata machine cache.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-COMPLEXITY</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " C5 file-size cap, C6 tokei report.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>See <code>docs/dashboard.md</code>, <code>docs/sbom.md</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
