       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""adacovex-1340""><a class=""header"" href=""#adac"
       & "ovex-1340"">adacovex 1.34.0</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Date: <em>2026-08-29</em></p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Version bumped 1.33.0 -&gt; 1.34.0.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""changes""><a class=""header"" href=""#changes"">Changes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c1-overview-paired-cards-now-fill-50-50""><a class=""header"" href=""#c1"
       & "-overview-paired-cards-now-fill-50-50"">C1: Overview paired cards now fill 50"
       & "-50</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <strong>Doc Coverage</strong> and <strong>Dependency Scope</strong> c"
       & "ards on the Overview tab sit in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "a <code>.chart-pair</code> grid, but that pair was itself a single item insi"
       & "de the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "overview <code>.chart-grid</code> (auto-fit, min 280px per cell), so the two"
       & " cards were"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "squeezed into one narrow column instead of each taking half the content widt"
       & "h."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "The pair now spans every grid track (<code>grid-column: 1 / -1</code>), so t"
       & "he two cards"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "fill 50-50 of the Overview content container exactly like <strong>Source Ove"
       & "rview</strong>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and <strong>Quick Stats</strong> do, and still stack on narrow screens.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c2-search-finds-page-sections-not-just-tabs""><a class=""header"" href="
       & """#c2-search-finds-page-sections-not-just-tabs"">C2: Search finds page section"
       & "s, not just tabs</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The header search indexed each tab as one blob of words, so a query only "
       & "ever"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "jumped to a whole tab and multi-word page text such as "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "orphan tags"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " or a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "section heading rarely matched.  The index is now built from the rendered DO"
       & "M"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "at the granularity of a section:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>every <code>.card</code> / <code>.chart-card</code> (labelled by its hea"
       & "ding);</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>every compliance-table row, so "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "orphan tags"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " lands on the exact row;</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>every dependency node and every HLR-tagged element;</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>plus one catch-all entry per tab.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Queries are tokenised and every token must match (AND semantics), so mult"
       & "i-word"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "page content and section headings resolve.  Selecting a hit switches to the "
       & "tab"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<strong>and</strong> scrolls to the matched section, briefly flashing it to "
       & "show where the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "match is, instead of only switching tabs.  Dependency names, versions, scope"
       & "s,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "licences and PURLs stay indexed, so the box still filters the dependency tre"
       & "e.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c3-system-tool-probe-cache-self-invalidates""><a class=""header"" href="
       & """#c3-system-tool-probe-cache-self-invalidates"">C3: System-tool probe cache s"
       & "elf-invalidates</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The referenced-tools cache key now folds in every curated tool"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "version-probe flag and the probe fallback chain.  Editing how a tool"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s version"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "is read (for example the <code>go</code> subcommand or the <code>--version, "
       & "-v, version</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "fallbacks) busts the cache automatically.  The 1.33-era control relied on a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "manually bumped <code>|tools-v3|</code> salt; forgetting the bump silently s"
       & "erved stale"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "probe results within a release.  No hand-maintained salt is needed now.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c4-gnatdoc-and-gnatformat-documented-as-alire-dev-dependencies""><a c"
       & "lass=""header"" href=""#c4-gnatdoc-and-gnatformat-documented-as-alire-dev-depen"
       & "dencies"">C4: gnatdoc and gnatformat documented as Alire dev dependencies</a>"
       & "</h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>gnatdoc_bin</code> and <code>gnatformat_bin</code> were already dev"
       & " dependencies declared in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>alire-dev.toml</code> (run via <code>alr exec</code> for the <code>mak"
       & "e doc</code> and <code>make fmt</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "targets), but the README"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <em>Requirements</em> list only mentioned <code>gnatpp</code> /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>gnatdoc</code> as optional tools.  The list now states that <strong>gn"
       & "atdoc_bin</strong> and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<strong>gnatformat_bin</strong> are managed by Alire as dev dependencies, so"
       & " the published"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "crate still installs and builds with no toolchain beyond the GNAT compiler.<"
       & "/p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""fixes""><a class=""header"" href=""#fixes"">Fixes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h1-proof-check-types-bars-now-scale-with-value""><a class=""header"" hr"
       & "ef=""#h1-proof-check-types-bars-now-scale-with-value"">H1: Proof Check Types b"
       & "ars now scale with value</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>1.33 rolled out proof-category bars with a per-row track-width style, but"
       & " the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "CSS <code>.hbar-track { flex: 1 }</code> overrode that inline width, so ever"
       & "y proof bar"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "stretched to the full row and showed only the proved <em>rate</em> (100% gre"
       & "en),"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "never the magnitude "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " unlike the test-category bars, which scale because their"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "fill is measured against the largest category.  The proof fills are now also"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "measured against the largest category: the green fill is Proved/Max and the "
       & "red"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "remainder is (Checks-Proved)/Max inside a full-width track, with the grey tr"
       & "ack"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "showing the scale gap "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " so a 407-VC category reads as a longer bar than a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "56-VC one, precisely like the test chart.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h2-links-render-in-the-accent-colour""><a class=""header"" href=""#h2-li"
       & "nks-render-in-the-accent-colour"">H2: Links render in the accent colour</a></"
       & "h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Links outside the Credits and footer areas "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the dependency-detail source"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "link, the <code>/api/deps</code> / <code>/api/metrics</code> references, and"
       & " the nomnoml note "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " fell"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "back to the browser"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s default blue/purple, while the Credits and footer links"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "used <code>--accent</code>.  A global <code>a { color: var(--accent) }</code"
       & "> rule now styles every"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "link uniformly (the Credits/footer rules become redundant but harmless), so "
       & "the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "detail panel, dependency views and search results match the rest of the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dashboard in both themes.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""test-suite""><a class=""header"" href=""#test-suite"">Test Suite</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Native suite grows to 1066 tests (14 categories).  The HTML/Markdown rend"
       & "erer"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "suite gains two assertions: the proof-check-type bar scales against the larg"
       & "est"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "category (Flow"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s green fill is a quarter of the full-width track when Flow is 2"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "of 8 runtime checks, and the largest category fills it), and the partial-pro"
       & "of"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "red remainder is sized by the maximum category.  The existing donut,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "chart-pair and hoverable scope-ring checks still pass unchanged.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""proof-results""><a class=""header"" href=""#proof-results"">Proof Results"
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Platinum, 723/723 VCs proved across 50 analysed units (unchanged at 1.34."
       & "0 "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the renderer and manifest-parser bodies are not in SPARK_Mode On, so the bar"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "scaling and cache-key changes add no new VCs).  Invocation: <code>adacovex p"
       & "rove</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>--steps=10000</code>, gnatprove 16.1.0).  0 unproved, 0 justified.</p"
       & ">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""traceability""><a class=""header"" href=""#traceability"">Traceability</a"
       & "></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>No new HLRs.  Coverage:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>RENDER-HTML</code> / <code>HLR-DASH</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " C1 paired-card width, C2 section search,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "H1 proof-bar scaling, H2 uniform link colour.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>MANIFEST</code> / <code>HLR-SBOM</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " C3 self-invalidating system-tool probe cache.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-ARCH</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " C4 doc changes (gnatdoc_bin / gnatformat_bin declared as Alire"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dev dependencies in <code>alire-dev.toml</code> and run via <code>alr exec</"
       & "code> for <code>make doc</code> /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>make fmt</code>).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>See <code>docs/dashboard.md</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
