       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""adacovex-1350""><a class=""header"" href=""#adac"
       & "ovex-1350"">adacovex 1.35.0</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Date: <em>2026-08-29</em></p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Version bumped 1.34.0 -&gt; 1.35.0.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""changes""><a class=""header"" href=""#changes"">Changes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c1-configurable-dashboard-worker-count""><a class=""header"" href=""#c1-"
       & "configurable-dashboard-worker-count"">C1: Configurable dashboard worker count"
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>--serve-workers=N</code> sets the HTTP server task-pool size for <c"
       & "ode>--serve</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(default 4).  Raise it to serve more concurrent dashboard requests; lower it"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "to use less memory.  The value is rejected unless <code>--serve</code> is al"
       & "so given, so"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "a silent no-op is impossible.  The bound is <code>Positive</code>; the pool "
       & "still caps at"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "its internal maximum.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c2-css-4px-spacing-gate-and-build-time-minification""><a class=""heade"
       & "r"" href=""#c2-css-4px-spacing-gate-and-build-time-minification"">C2: CSS 4px s"
       & "pacing gate and build-time minification</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>tools/csslint.py</code> enforces the dashboard spacing convention: "
       & "every"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>margin</code>, <code>padding</code> and <code>gap</code> pixel length "
       & "must be a multiple of 4px.  It runs"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "as a cheap static gate inside <code>make build</code> and <code>make check</"
       & "code>.  The authored"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "CSS and JavaScript are minified at build time by <code>tools/gen-dashboard.p"
       & "y</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(comments stripped, whitespace collapsed) before they are bundled into the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "served dashboard.  The vendored graph libraries are already minified and are"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "inlined byte-for-byte.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c3-four-sentence-paragraph-gate-for-hand-written-docs""><a class=""hea"
       & "der"" href=""#c3-four-sentence-paragraph-gate-for-hand-written-docs"">C3: Four-"
       & "sentence paragraph gate for hand-written docs</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>tools/check-docs.py</code> (wired as <code>make docs-check</code>) "
       & "fails when any paragraph"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "in the user documentation, README, or human changelogs exceeds four"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "sentences.  It also rejects em dashes and Latin abbreviations (<code>i.e.</c"
       & "ode>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>e.g.</code>, <code>etc.</code>) to keep the prose under Simplified Tec"
       & "hnical English."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>tools/para-split.py</code> rewraps over-long paragraphs to comply.  Th"
       & "e generated"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>docs/api-docs</code> pages are excluded; their source docstrings carry"
       & " the same"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "rule.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c4-timezone-support-with-os-aware-default""><a class=""header"" href=""#"
       & "c4-timezone-support-with-os-aware-default"">C4: Timezone support with OS-awar"
       & "e default</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>--tz</code> / <code>--timezone</code> override the display zone for"
       & " <code>status</code> reports."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Accepted forms are an IANA name (<code>Asia/Singapore</code>) or a fixed"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>UTC</code>/<code>GMT</code> offset (<code>UTC+8</code>, <code>GMT+8</c"
       & "ode>, <code>UTC+08</code>, <code>GMT+08</code>, <code>UTC+08:30</code>).  Wi"
       & "th"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "no override, adacovex now honours the operating system"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s wall-clock zone"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "through <code>Ada.Calendar.Time_Zones.UTC_Time_Offset</code> (which reads th"
       & "e <code>TZ</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "variable and the system timezone) and shows it as <code>UTC+/-HH:MM</code>. "
       & " A named"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "zone resolves from a built-in table of common IANA names; a zone that may"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "observe daylight saving time, or one the table lacks, is probed against the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "platform tzdata (<code>zdump</code> + <code>date +%z</code>) for the DST-cor"
       & "rect current offset,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "with the table as the fallback when the probe is unavailable.  <code>status<"
       & "/code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>status --export</code> and <code>status --metrics</code> report the re"
       & "solved zone, the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "current date and time, and the count of dated release changelogs under the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "target.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c5-complexity-check-extended-to-non-ada-source""><a class=""header"" hr"
       & "ef=""#c5-complexity-check-extended-to-non-ada-source"">C5: Complexity check ex"
       & "tended to non-Ada source</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>complexity</code> now walks the whole target and scores many langua"
       & "ges (C/C++,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "C#, Go, Java, JavaScript, TypeScript, Python, Ruby, PHP, Rust, Shell,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Kotlin, and the YAML/JSON/TOML/XML/Markdown/Markdown families) alongside"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Ada.  <code>--excludes=EXT,EXT</code> skips listed file extensions and is re"
       & "jected"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "unless the <code>complexity</code> subcommand is given, so it can never run "
       & "on its own."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Per-subprogram analysis stays Ada-specific; other languages contribute"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "file-level lines of code and decision counts.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c6-ansi-colour-on-the-terminal-report""><a class=""header"" href=""#c6-a"
       & "nsi-colour-on-the-terminal-report"">C6: ANSI colour on the terminal report</a"
       & "></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>Adacovex.Ansi</code> colours the terminal output (red for failures,"
       & " green for"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "passes, bold for headings).  Colour is disabled automatically inside CI"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(the <code>CI</code> variable), under <code>NO_COLOR</code>, or with <code>T"
       & "ERM=dumb</code>, so CI logs stay"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "plain and machine-readable.  The complexity report and the main header use"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "it.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c7-agentsmd-keeps-documentation-current""><a class=""header"" href=""#c7"
       & "-agentsmd-keeps-documentation-current"">C7: AGENTS.md keeps documentation cur"
       & "rent</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A new note in <code>AGENTS.md</code> states that every change must update"
       & " the relevant"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "user documentation, the Ada docstrings that feed <code>docs/api-docs</code>,"
       & " and the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "changelog, and must re-run the sync gates (<code>docs-check</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>action-parity-check</code>, <code>agents-tree</code>, <code>doc-links<"
       & "/code>, <code>link-check</code>).  This makes"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the expectation explicit that LLM-assisted edits keep docs in step with code"
       & ".</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""fixes""><a class=""header"" href=""#fixes"">Fixes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h1-status-default-zone-now-follows-the-operating-system""><a class=""h"
       & "eader"" href=""#h1-status-default-zone-now-follows-the-operating-system"">H1: S"
       & "tatus default zone now follows the operating system</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The previous timezone default ignored the system zone and fell back to UT"
       & "C"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "unless a <code>TZ</code> variable or a Debian <code>/etc/timezone</code> fil"
       & "e named a zone."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Timezones.Default</code> now resolves the offset from"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Ada.Calendar.Time_Zones.UTC_Time_Offset</code>, so the reported time m"
       & "atches the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "operator"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s configured wall clock.  The date/time rendering also compensates"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "for GNAT"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s local-time calendar accessors, so the displayed wall clock is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "correct in every zone (including negative offsets, which the original"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "implementation rejected outright).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h2-timezone-and-ansi-packages-stay-spark-clean""><a class=""header"" hr"
       & "ef=""#h2-timezone-and-ansi-packages-stay-spark-clean"">H2: Timezone and ANSI p"
       & "ackages stay SPARK-clean</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>Adacovex.Timezones</code> dropped its <code>Ada.Text_IO</code> read"
       & " of <code>/etc/timezone</code> and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Adacovex.Ansi</code> scoped its environment-variable reads, so both re"
       & "main"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>SPARK_Mode On</code> with only the env-var Global-contract warning sup"
       & "pressed"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(matching <code>CPUs.Get_Temp_Directory</code>).  <code>make prove</code> th"
       & "erefore keeps its"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Platinum, zero-unproved status.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""test-suite""><a class=""header"" href=""#test-suite"">Test Suite</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The native suite grows from 1066 to 1157 tests (16 categories).  The CLI"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "config suite gains 16 flag-gating assertions (<code>--excludes</code> requir"
       & "es"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>complexity</code>, <code>--serve-workers</code> requires <code>--serve"
       & "</code> and a positive value,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>--tz</code>/<code>--timezone</code> validates its value and stores it)"
       & ".</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A new Timezone + ANSI suite (63 assertions) covers timezone parsing and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "formatting (named IANA zones, <code>UTC</code>/<code>GMT</code> offsets, mal"
       & "formed values,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Now_Text</code>, the OS default, and the platform probe) and ANSI colo"
       & "ur"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "coverage (<code>Colour_Allowed</code> under CI / NO_COLOR / TERM=dumb, plus "
       & "the SGR"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "wrappers).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A new Complexity check suite (12 assertions) covers the multi-language"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "scan and <code>--excludes</code> filtering.  The totals are resynced via"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>make test-count</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""proof-results""><a class=""header"" href=""#proof-results"">Proof Results"
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Platinum, 0 unproved, 0 justified.  The timezone and ANSI refactors keep"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "every analysed unit <code>SPARK_Mode On</code> (the only non-SPARK construct"
       & "s are the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "env-var reads, whose Global-contract absence is suppressed), so the VC total"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "is resynced via <code>make proof-status</code> and stays at the Platinum bar"
       & "."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Invocation: <code>adacovex prove</code> (<code>--steps=10000</code>, gnatpro"
       & "ve 16.1.0).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""traceability""><a class=""header"" href=""#traceability"">Traceability</a"
       & "></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-CLI</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " C1 <code>--serve-workers</code>, C5 <code>complexity --excludes</code>, C6 "
       & "ANSI"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "colour, C7 AGENTS.md note.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-TZ</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " C4 timezone support and status detail, H1 OS-default fix.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-ANSI</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " C6 terminal colour.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-COMPLEXITY</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " C5 multi-language complexity and excludes.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-DASH</code> / <code>HLR-ARCH</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " C2 CSS 4px gate and build-time minification.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>See <code>docs/cli-reference.md</code>, <code>docs/dashboard.md</code>, a"
       & "nd <code>docs/platforms.md</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
