       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""adacovex-1360""><a class=""header"" href=""#adac"
       & "ovex-1360"">adacovex 1.36.0</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Date: <em>2026-08-29</em></p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Version bumped 1.35.0 -&gt; 1.36.0.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""fixes""><a class=""header"" href=""#fixes"">Fixes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h1-bundled-dashboard-javascript-survives-minification""><a class=""hea"
       & "der"" href=""#h1-bundled-dashboard-javascript-survives-minification"">H1: Bundl"
       & "ed dashboard JavaScript survives minification</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The dashboard builder minified the authored JavaScript with a comment"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "stripper that did not understand regular-expression literals. A slash pair"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "inside a regular expression, for example the <code>//</code> in <code>/^http"
       & "s?:\/\//i</code>, was"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "read as a line comment. The stripper then deleted the rest of that line.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The deleted text was the dependency link check in <code>details.js</code>"
       & ":</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code>if (d.website &amp;&amp; /^https?:\/\//i.test(String(d.website)))"
       & " {"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The minifier rewrote it to <code>if (d.website &amp;&amp; /^https?:\/</co"
       & "de>, an unterminated"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "statement that broke the dependency detail panel. The fault lived in the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "generated <code>src/adacovex-dashboard_template.ads</code>, so every built b"
       & "inary"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "carried the broken page. Releases on GitHub and the Alire crate were both"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "affected, because the dashboard is bundled into the binary as one string"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "constant.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>tools/gen-dashboard.py</code> now scans a regular expression litera"
       & "l to its"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "closing slash before it strips comments. The previous significant token"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "decides whether a slash opens a regular expression or a division, so"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "embedded <code>//</code> and <code>/*</code> text stays intact. The vendored"
       & " graph libraries are"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "still inlined byte for byte and are not minified. The regenerated template"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "passes <code>tools/gen-dashboard.py --check</code> and every inlined script "
       & "passes a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "JavaScript syntax check.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h2-dashboard-proof-guidance-uses-the-adacovex-cli""><a class=""header"""
       & " href=""#h2-dashboard-proof-guidance-uses-the-adacovex-cli"">H2: Dashboard pro"
       & "of guidance uses the adacovex CLI</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The Proof tab told users to run <code>make prove</code> after each change"
       & ". The dashboard"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and command help are user-facing output; developer-only make targets do not"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "belong there. The text now reads <code>adacovex prove</code>, matching the a"
       & "ctual"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "user-facing subcommand.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h3-dashboard-credits-show-actual-third-party-versions""><a class=""hea"
       & "der"" href=""#h3-dashboard-credits-show-actual-third-party-versions"">H3: Dashb"
       & "oard credits show actual third-party versions</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The Credits tab listed Playwright as <code>test / Apache-2.0</code> and C"
       & "harts.css as"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>inspiration / MIT</code>. Both now carry their actual vendored version"
       & "s: Playwright"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>1.62.1 / Apache-2.0</code> and Charts.css <code>1.2.0 / MIT</code> (cr"
       & "edited for inspiration,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "as the dashboard charts are hand-rolled CSS/SVG).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h4-fast-hover-tooltips-for-dependency-scope-and-tree""><a class=""head"
       & "er"" href=""#h4-fast-hover-tooltips-for-dependency-scope-and-tree"">H4: Fast ho"
       & "ver tooltips for dependency scope and tree</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The dependency tree and the nomnoml diagram used the native SVG <code>&lt"
       & ";title&gt;</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tooltip, which browsers delay by one to two seconds. A custom <code>DepToolt"
       & "ip</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "now appears immediately on <code>mouseover</code> and follows the cursor. Th"
       & "e polar"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "scope ring already used a native <code>&lt;title&gt;</code>; the same fast t"
       & "ooltip is wired"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "to its segments.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h5-system-tool-discovery-skips-source-files""><a class=""header"" href="
       & """#h5-system-tool-discovery-skips-source-files"">H5: System-tool discovery ski"
       & "ps source files</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>Discover_System_Dev_Deps</code> scanned every file whose extension "
       & "looked like code"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>ads</code>, <code>adb</code>, <code>c</code>, <code>cpp</code>, <code"
       & ">rs</code>, <code>go</code>, <code>js</code>, <code>ts</code>, "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(166)
       & "). That produced false"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "positives: Ada source contains the word <code>ada</code>, Rust source contai"
       & "ns <code>go</code>, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "C source contains <code>make</code>. The scanner now reads only build-facing"
       & " files"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(Makefile variants, shell scripts, GNAT project files, CI workflows, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "build manifests). Prose and source text are never scanned for tool names.</p"
       & ">"
       & ASCII.LF
