       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""adacovex-1370""><a class=""header"" href=""#adac"
       & "ovex-1370"">adacovex 1.37.0</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Date: <em>2026-08-30</em></p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Version bumped 1.36.0 -&gt; 1.37.0.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""changes""><a class=""header"" href=""#changes"">Changes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c1-api-playground-tab""><a class=""header"" href=""#c1-api-playground-ta"
       & "b"">C1: API playground tab</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The dashboard now has an <strong>API</strong> tab that works as an intera"
       & "ctive REST"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "client. Every endpoint the <code>--serve</code> server dispatches on is list"
       & "ed as a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "clickable button, grouped by purpose (Metrics, Dependencies, Badges,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Documentation). A filter input searches the endpoints as you type, matching"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the path, description, and group name.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Clicking an endpoint issues a live <code>fetch</code> against the serving"
       & " origin and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "previews the response. JSON endpoints are pretty-printed and syntax"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "highlighted with the vendored yace tokenizer, with object keys coloured"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "separately from string values. SVG badge endpoints show the live image above"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the raw markup. A toolbar offers <strong>Copy</strong> and <strong>Download<"
       & "/strong> for the raw"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "response body, so the playground doubles as a lightweight HTTP client withou"
       & "t"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "leaving the browser.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The first endpoint (<code>/api/metrics</code>) runs automatically, so the"
       & " tab always"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "opens with a live preview. The endpoint list is not hardcoded in client"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "JavaScript: the playground fetches it from the new <code>GET /api/endpoints<"
       & "/code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "endpoint, the single catalog the server declares. Each request is made live"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "against the instance, so what you preview is exactly what <code>curl</code> "
       & "returns.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c2-charts-tab-is-a-strict-superset-of-the-overview-charts""><a class="
       & """header"" href=""#c2-charts-tab-is-a-strict-superset-of-the-overview-charts"">C"
       & "2: Charts tab is a strict superset of the Overview charts</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <strong>Charts</strong> tab now leads with the same two radars that h"
       & "eadline the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Overview: the <strong>Robustness</strong> five-axis radar with its S/A/B/C/D"
       & " tier rating,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and the <strong>SPARK proof-by-check-type</strong> radar. Both are shared wi"
       & "th the Overview"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(one source of truth in the renderer), so every Overview chart appears on th"
       & "e"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Charts tab and the two tabs cannot drift apart. The Charts tab now renders"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "eight cards.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c3-vendored-yace-for-json-syntax-highlighting""><a class=""header"" hre"
       & "f=""#c3-vendored-yace-for-json-syntax-highlighting"">C3: Vendored yace for JSO"
       & "N syntax highlighting</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex vendors the <code>code()</code> tokenizer highlighter from"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a href=""https://github.com/petersolopov/yace"">petersolopov/yace</a> (MIT, v"
       & "1.1.0) as"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>resources/js/yace.js</code>, exposed as <code>window.YaceTok</code>. T"
       & "he API playground uses"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "it to syntax-highlight the prettified JSON responses of the <code>/api/*</co"
       & "de>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "endpoints. The tokenizer is adapted from ESM/TypeScript to a single"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "plain-script binding so the dashboard needs no build step; the tokenizer"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "logic is unchanged. The dashboard supplies the token colours via theme-aware"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "CSS. yace is credited on the Credits tab and in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c4---serve-semantics-clarified-and---serve-workers-documented-as-a-r"
       & "elated-flag""><a class=""header"" href=""#c4---serve-semantics-clarified-and---s"
       & "erve-workers-documented-as-a-related-flag"">C4: <code>--serve</code> semantic"
       & "s clarified and <code>--serve-workers</code> documented as a related flag</a"
       & "></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code>--serve</code> flag description now states clearly that it is a"
       & " switch: passing"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>--serve</code> is the only way to start the HTTP dashboard server, and"
       & " omitting it"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(the default, <code>off</code>) renders and exits without serving. There is "
       & "no"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>--no-serve</code>, because the flag already controls it. The man page "
       & "and the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Related CLI flags table in <code>docs/dashboard.md</code> now list <code>--s"
       & "erve-workers</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "alongside <code>--port</code> and <code>--theme</code> as a related <code>--"
       & "serve</code> flag, with its own"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "description (default 4, capped at 256, only meaningful with <code>--serve</c"
       & "ode>). The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dashboard docs also note that the server strips query strings and fragments"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "before routing, so <code>/?theme=light</code> works.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c5-more-actionable-information""><a class=""header"" href=""#c5-more-act"
       & "ionable-information"">C5: More actionable information</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The API playground gives users an actionable way to inspect the live"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "assessment data: preview every endpoint, copy the exact JSON for scripting,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and download the raw response. Combined with the strict-superset Charts tab,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the dashboard now surfaces the same health data in more explorable and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "machine-consumable forms.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""fixes""><a class=""header"" href=""#fixes"">Fixes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h1-themelightdarksystem-on-the-dashboard-url-returned-404""><a class="
       & """header"" href=""#h1-themelightdarksystem-on-the-dashboard-url-returned-404"">H"
       & "1: <code>?theme=light|dark|system</code> on the dashboard URL returned 404</"
       & "a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The HTTP server routed on the raw request path, including the query strin"
       & "g"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and fragment. A browser requesting <code>http://localhost:8080/?theme=light<"
       & "/code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "produced a path of <code>/?theme=light</code>, which did not match any route"
       & " and served"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>404 Not Found</code> instead of the themed dashboard. The server now s"
       & "trips the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "query string and fragment before routing (<code>Strip_Query</code>), so <cod"
       & "e>/?theme=light</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>/api/metrics?x=1</code> and <code>/api/deps#top</code> reach the same "
       & "handlers as <code>/</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>/api/metrics</code> and <code>/api/deps</code>. The <code>?theme=</cod"
       & "e> value is applied client-side as"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "before; the fix makes the request reach the dashboard in the first place.</p"
       & ">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h2-footer-no-longer-lists-a-redundant-tabs-hint""><a class=""header"" h"
       & "ref=""#h2-footer-no-longer-lists-a-redundant-tabs-hint"">H2: Footer no longer "
       & "lists a redundant tabs hint</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The dashboard footer carried a <code>Tabs: #proof/#deps</code> hint. Ever"
       & "y tab is already"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "hash-addressable, so the hint only named two of seven tabs and added nothing"
       & "."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "The footer now shows the embed query hint and the JSON API links, and adds a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "link to the new API playground. External docs stopped referencing the remove"
       & "d"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>#proof</code>/<code>#deps</code> convenience.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""test-suite""><a class=""header"" href=""#test-suite"">Test Suite</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The native suite grows from 1157 to 1169 tests (16 categories). The serve"
       & "r"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "routing category adds 12 checks covering <code>Strip_Query</code> (the theme"
       & "d root URL,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "query strings and fragments on the JSON API and badge endpoints, the empty"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "path, and unchanged paths with no query) and the new <code>/api/endpoints</c"
       & "ode> catalog"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "route. All 1169 tests pass.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""proof-results""><a class=""header"" href=""#proof-results"">Proof Results"
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Platinum, 0 unproved, 0 justified, 723 VCs unchanged under gnatprove 16.1"
       & ".0."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "The dashboard, serve-path, and manifest scanner changes are build-time or"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "I/O-bound code that adds no analysed Ada, so the VC total stays at the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Platinum bar. The <code>Strip_Query</code> server helper is a new spec-decla"
       & "red SPARK"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "subprogram and is proved alongside the rest of the server spec.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""traceability""><a class=""header"" href=""#traceability"">Traceability</a"
       & "></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-DASH</code> / <code>HLR-SERVER</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " C1 API playground tab, C2 Charts superset, C3"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "vendored yace, H1 query-string/fragment route stripping, H2 footer cleanup.<"
       & "/li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-CLI</code> / <code>HLR-DOC</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " C4 <code>--serve</code> semantics and the <code>--serve-workers</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "related-flag documentation in the man page and dashboard docs.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
