       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""adacovex-1380""><a class=""header"" href=""#adac"
       & "ovex-1380"">adacovex 1.38.0</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Date: <em>2026-08-30</em></p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Version bumped 1.37.0 -&gt; 1.38.0.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""changes""><a class=""header"" href=""#changes"">Changes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c1-manual-is-now-an-mdbook-project-with-a-read-the-docs-site""><a cla"
       & "ss=""header"" href=""#c1-manual-is-now-an-mdbook-project-with-a-read-the-docs-s"
       & "ite"">C1: Manual is now an mdBook project with a Read the Docs site</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The user documentation under <code>docs/</code> is now a proper <strong>m"
       & "dBook</strong> project:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>docs/book.toml</code> (with <code>src = "".""</code>) and a root <code>d"
       & "ocs/SUMMARY.md</code> table of"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "contents. Read the Docs builds the public manual from it (<code>.readthedocs"
       & ".yaml</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>mdbook build docs</code>), so the deployed site, the repository pages,"
       & " and the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "bundled offline manual all share one source of truth. The generated <code>do"
       & "cs/book/</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "build output is now <strong>committed with the source</strong> (the <code>.g"
       & "itignore</code> entry was"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dropped), so <code>make book</code> keeps it in sync and the built site trav"
       & "els with the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "repository. <code>make book-serve</code> serves the manual locally at"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>http://localhost:8000</code>; <code>make docs-serve</code> keeps servi"
       & "ng the raw Markdown.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c2-bundled-offline-manual-served-at-docs""><a class=""header"" href=""#c"
       & "2-bundled-offline-manual-served-at-docs"">C2: Bundled offline manual served a"
       & "t /docs</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code>--serve</code> server now serves a <strong>bundled offline manu"
       & "al</strong> at <code>/docs</code> (both"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "spellings, with and without the trailing slash, reach the same page)."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>tools/gen-docs.py</code> runs <code>mdbook build</code> over <code>doc"
       & "s/</code> at build time, inlines"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the generated <code>print.html</code> into one self-contained ASCII page, an"
       & "d bundles it"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "into the binary as <code>src/adacovex-docs_template.ads</code> (regenerated "
       & "by"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>make book</code>, which is also part of <code>make build</code>). Styl"
       & "esheets are inlined and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "external fonts and interactive scripts are dropped, so the page reads fully"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "offline with no network or extra assets. The dashboard footer <strong>Manual"
       & "</strong> link"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and the API playground"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <code>/docs</code> endpoint both open it, so a user on a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "machine without a network connection can still consult the manual.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c3-api-playground-endpoints-are-clickable-links""><a class=""header"" h"
       & "ref=""#c3-api-playground-endpoints-are-clickable-links"">C3: API playground en"
       & "dpoints are clickable links</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The API playground endpoint buttons now carry a real link on the endpoint"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "path: clicking the path opens the raw URL in a new tab, while clicking the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "rest of the button still runs the endpoint live in the playground. JSON"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "responses that reference endpoint paths (for example the <code>/api/...</cod"
       & "e> and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>/badge/...</code> values in <code>/api/endpoints</code>) get those pat"
       & "hs linkified too, so a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "user can jump straight from a URL in the payload to the live endpoint. The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "endpoint catalog now lists <code>/docs</code> as an <code>html</code> endpoi"
       & "nt.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c4-yace-token-colours-follow-the-pinned-theme""><a class=""header"" hre"
       & "f=""#c4-yace-token-colours-follow-the-pinned-theme"">C4: yace token colours fo"
       & "llow the pinned theme</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The vendored yace highlighter"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s token colours are driven by the dashboard"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>--tok-*</code> CSS variables. The variables had a light default and a "
       & "dark"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)</code> block, but no explicit ligh"
       & "t override,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "so a user who pinned the light theme on a dark OS still saw dark token"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "colours. The CSS now defines the token colours explicitly per theme"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>:root</code>, <code>[data-theme=""light""]</code>, <code>[data-theme=""d"
       & "ark""]</code>), so the highlighted"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "JSON always matches the active dashboard theme, not the OS.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c5-complexity-check-skips-the-mdbook-build-output""><a class=""header"""
       & " href=""#c5-complexity-check-skips-the-mdbook-build-output"">C5: complexity-ch"
       & "eck skips the mdBook build output</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code>complexity</code> subcommand"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s directory walk now skips <code>book</code> directories,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "so the committed mdBook build output (<code>docs/book/</code>) is excluded f"
       & "rom the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "source-quality scan. The build output contains minified single-line"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "JavaScript (the search index alone is a 1.4 MB line, far beyond the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Max_Line</code> buffer), which printed a spurious "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "line exceeds Max_Line buffer"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & ASCII.LF
       & "error on every scan and, in constrained environments, could push the scan"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "into heap exhaustion. The gate now scans assessed source only, matching the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "existing <code>obj</code> / <code>bin</code> / <code>dist</code> / <code>bui"
       & "ld</code> exclusions.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c7-book-links-check-gate-keeps-the-committed-manual-in-sync""><a clas"
       & "s=""header"" href=""#c7-book-links-check-gate-keeps-the-committed-manual-in-syn"
       & "c"">C7: book-links-check gate keeps the committed manual in sync</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A new <code>make book-links-check</code> gate (wired into <code>make chec"
       & "k</code>, via"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>tools/check-book-links.py</code>) stops the committed mdBook build out"
       & "put"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>docs/book/</code>) from drifting from the <code>docs/</code> source. "
       & " It rebuilds the book"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "from a temp copy of <code>docs/</code> and fails when the committed output d"
       & "iffers"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "byte for byte.  It also verifies that every link inside the bundled offline"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "manual resolves against the bundled assets or the deliberately-not-bundled"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "prefixes shared with <code>tools/gen-docs.py</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The manual is now <strong>complete</strong>: every page under <code>docs/"
       & "</code> (the 64"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "API-reference pages, the 39 changelogs, the compliance outputs, the proof"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "ledger, the test report, credits, and third-party notices) is a book"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "chapter, so the index pages no longer link to pages the book never builds"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(previously 131 broken links in the built site).  Links from the manual to"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "repo-root files (<code>README.md</code>, <code>CONTRIBUTING.md</code>, <code"
       & ">AGENTS.md</code>) now point at"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the repository URLs instead of <code>../</code> paths that cannot resolve in"
       & "side the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "book.  The tools unit tests grow from 41 to 48.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c6-dashboard-preview-screenshots-refreshed-and-api-tab-added""><a cla"
       & "ss=""header"" href=""#c6-dashboard-preview-screenshots-refreshed-and-api-tab-ad"
       & "ded"">C6: Dashboard preview screenshots refreshed and API tab added</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The Charts tab preview (<code>docs/media/dashboard_preview_charts.png</co"
       & "de>) is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "regenerated from the live dashboard, and a new API tab preview"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>docs/media/dashboard_preview_api.png</code>) is captured and added to"
       & " the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dashboard walk-through in <code>docs/dashboard.md</code>. The walk-through n"
       & "ow covers"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "all eight tabs in header order, and the Charts tab description is corrected"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "from "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "six cards"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " to the real eight (the two shared radars, proof and test"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "donuts, proof and test bars, the docstring radial gauge, and the dependency"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "scope polar ring). The screenshots are captured with a Playwright script"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>tests/e2e/capture-previews.mjs</code>) against the live <code>--serve"
       & "</code> dashboard.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""fixes""><a class=""header"" href=""#fixes"">Fixes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h1-vendored-yacejs-now-appears-in-the-sbom""><a class=""header"" href="""
       & "#h1-vendored-yacejs-now-appears-in-the-sbom"">H1: Vendored yace.js now appear"
       & "s in the SBOM</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The vendored JavaScript bundles (<code>graphre.js</code>, <code>nomnoml.j"
       & "s</code>, <code>flexsearch.js</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>yace.js</code>) sat at the <code>resources/</code> root, but the vendo"
       & "red <code>yace.js</code> lived"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "under <code>resources/js/</code> with the authored dashboard modules. The SB"
       & "OM asset"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "scanner treats <code>resources/js/</code> as authored dashboard code and ski"
       & "pped it, so"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "yace never became a dependency component. <code>yace.js</code> now sits at t"
       & "he"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>resources/</code> root with the other vendored libraries, the layout c"
       & "learly"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "separates dependency JavaScript from dashboard JavaScript, and the SBOM list"
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "yace (MIT, v1.1.0, <code>pkg:generic/yace</code>) alongside the other bundle"
       & "d libraries.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h3-docs-subpages-are-served-again""><a class=""header"" href=""#h3-docs-"
       & "subpages-are-served-again"">H3: /docs subpages are served again</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code>Docs_Subpath</code> slicing assumed the request path started at"
       & " index 1, but"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Get_Path</code> returns a slice of the request line, so every <code>/d"
       & "ocs/&lt;subpath&gt;</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "kept a leading slash and returned 404 "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " only <code>/docs</code> and <code>/docs/</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "resolved.  The six-character prefix is now stripped from the slice"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s actual"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "first index, so every page, stylesheet, and badge of the bundled manual"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "serves (an e2e test pins the exact, nested, and extensionless subpaths plus"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "a missing-page 404).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h4-bundled-manual-no-longer-overflows-the-gnatprove-frontend""><a cla"
       & "ss=""header"" href=""#h4-bundled-manual-no-longer-overflows-the-gnatprove-front"
       & "end"">H4: Bundled manual no longer overflows the gnatprove frontend</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The complete-book offline manual is a 4 MB asset set, and <code>gen-docs."
       & "py</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "emitted it as one giant <code>&amp;</code>-concatenation chain (300k+ string"
       & " literals)."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "GNAT"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s frontend parses that tree fine, but gnatprove"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s flow analysis blew"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "its stack (<code>Storage_Error stack overflow</code> at <code>adacovex-docs_"
       & "template.ads</code>),"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "aborting <code>make prove</code> and therefore <code>make check</code> and e"
       & "very release."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Experiments showed the limit is the constant size itself (a single string"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "constant over ~1 MB overflows whatever its structure), so the generated"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "spec now holds one <code>aliased constant String</code> per asset "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " 152 bodies, each"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "well under the limit, never concatenated into one value "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " with an"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Asset_Bodies</code> access-to-constant table and an <code>Asset_Index<"
       & "/code> subtype so"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Content (Idx)</code> needs no unchecked bounds reasoning. The served b"
       & "ytes are"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "unchanged (each asset constant carries the identical content), the server"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "routes through the same <code>Find</code>/<code>Content</code> API, and the "
       & "bundle-links check"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "still passes.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h2-dashboard-footer-links-updated""><a class=""header"" href=""#h2-dashb"
       & "oard-footer-links-updated"">H2: Dashboard footer links updated</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The footer"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s API links now include the bundled manual:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>API: /api/metrics /api/deps Manual API playground</code>, with the Man"
       & "ual link"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "opening <code>/docs</code> in a new tab. The <code>adacovex help serve</code"
       & "> text and the dashboard docs list the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>/docs</code> endpoint alongside the JSON API and badge endpoints.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""test-suite""><a class=""header"" href=""#test-suite"">Test Suite</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The native suite grows from 1169 to 1173 tests. The server routing catego"
       & "ry"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "adds four checks for the <code>/docs</code> and <code>/docs/</code> routes a"
       & "nd two near-miss paths"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>/docs2</code>, <code>/manual</code>) that must stay 404s. All 1173 te"
       & "sts pass.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""proof-results""><a class=""header"" href=""#proof-results"">Proof Results"
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Platinum, 0 unproved, 0 justified, 725 VCs (725 proved) under gnatprove"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "16.1.0 "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the total reported by <code>adacovex prove</code> and mirrored in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>/api/metrics</code>, the 16.1.0 proof ledger, and the self-assessment "
       & "docs. The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "manual-bundling, dashboard, and SBOM changes are build-time or I/O-bound"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "code that adds no analysed Ada, so the VC total stays at the Platinum bar."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "The <code>Route</code> expression function gains one more <code>elsif</code>"
       & " for the <code>/docs/</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "trailing-slash spelling and remains proved by definition.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""traceability""><a class=""header"" href=""#traceability"">Traceability</a"
       & "></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-DOC</code> / <code>HLR-DASH</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " C1 mdBook manual + Read the Docs, C2 bundled"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "offline manual at <code>/docs</code>, H2 footer links, <code>tools/gen-docs."
       & "py</code>, and the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>make book</code> target.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-DASH</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " C3 API playground clickable links, C4 yace theme variables,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "C6 refreshed Charts preview + new API tab preview and the completed"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dashboard walk-through.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-SBOM</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " H1 vendored yace.js in the SBOM and the vendored/dashboard"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "JavaScript layout separation.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-ARCH</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " C5 complexity-check <code>book</code> directory exclusion, C7 the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "book-links-check gate and the complete-book restructure, H4 the chunked"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "blob that keeps the bundled manual provable.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-SERVER</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " H3 the <code>Docs_Subpath</code> off-by-one fix.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>See <code>docs/dashboard.md</code>, <code>docs/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md</co"
       & "de>, and <code>.readthedocs.yaml</code>.</p>"
