       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""adacovex-150""><a class=""header"" href=""#adaco"
       & "vex-150"">adacovex 1.5.0</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Date: <em>2026-08-05</em></p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Version bumped 1.4.0 -&gt; 1.5.0.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""changes""><a class=""header"" href=""#changes"">Changes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c1-more-standard-docstring-styles""><a class=""header"" href=""#c1-more-"
       & "standard-docstring-styles"">C1: More standard docstring styles</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The source scanner now recognises additional standard docstring conventio"
       & "ns,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "so third-party and code-generated Ada is counted correctly:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Comment prefixes: besides the canonical <code>--  </code> (two dashes + "
       & "two spaces),"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the single-space <code>-- </code> and tab-separated (<code>--&lt;TAB&gt;</co"
       & "de>) styles are recognised"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "as docstrings. A bare <code>--</code> or <code>---</code> divider is still n"
       & "ot a docstring.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Tag aliases: <code>@parameter</code> == <code>@param</code>, <code>@retu"
       & "rns</code> == <code>@return</code>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Summary tags: <code>@brief</code> and <code>@summary</code> mark a subpr"
       & "ogram as documented.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c2-more-test-result-formats""><a class=""header"" href=""#c2-more-test-r"
       & "esult-formats"">C2: More test-result formats</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>Adacovex.Parsers.Tests</code> now also parses the following standar"
       & "d formats"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(additively with the existing Markdown-table parser):</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>TAP</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>ok N - name</code> / <code>not ok N - name</code> lines</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Automake</strong> test-suite "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>PASS: name</code> / <code>FAIL: name</code> lines</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Maven Surefire</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>Tests run: N, Failures: M, Errors: E</code> summaries"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(failed = failures + errors)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Unity</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>N Tests M Failures</code> summaries (the count may be separated"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "from the word by spaces)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c3-longer-source-lines""><a class=""header"" href=""#c3-longer-source-li"
       & "nes"">C3: Longer source lines</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>Max_Line</code> is raised from 8192 to <strong>262144</strong> char"
       & "acters, so single-line"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "declarations from heavily code-generated projects (previously drained"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "silently) are parsed in full.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c4-dev-manifest-proof-swap-prove-subcommand""><a class=""header"" href="
       & """#c4-dev-manifest-proof-swap-prove-subcommand"">C4: Dev-manifest proof swap ("
       & "<code>prove</code> subcommand)</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>When the target project declares <code>gnatprove</code> only in <code>ali"
       & "re-dev.toml</code> (keeping the publishing <code>alire.toml</code> clean), t"
       & "he <code>prove</code> subcommand now runs the proof through a temporary shel"
       & "l wrapper that backs up <code>alire.toml</code> / <code>alire.lock</code> / "
       & "<code>alire/</code>, swaps the dev manifest over the publishing one, runs <c"
       & "ode>alr exec -- gnatprove -P &lt;gpr&gt;</code>, and restores everything (vi"
       & "a <code>trap ... EXIT INT TERM</code>) even on failure or interruption. The "
       & "assessment and SBOM pipeline always scans the publishing <code>alire.toml</c"
       & "ode>, so dev-only tool declarations never leak into dependency graphs or SBO"
       & "Ms. This fixes <code>make run-ada-crdt</code> / <code>make prove</code> agai"
       & "nst projects (e.g.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Ada_CRDT) that keep gnatprove out of their publishing manifest.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c5-ir-layer--bounded-target-type-profiles""><a class=""header"" href=""#"
       & "c5-ir-layer--bounded-target-type-profiles"">C5: IR layer "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " bounded target type profiles</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>New <code>src/ir/</code> layer implements the first stage of an intermedi"
       & "ate"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "representation for cross-compilation assessments:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>Adacovex.Target_Profiles</code> (SPARK On): bounded machine-intege"
       & "r types"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>IR_Int8</code>..<code>IR_Int64</code> (fixed-width signed ranges with "
       & "<code>Size</code> clauses) and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>IR_UInt8</code>..<code>IR_UInt64</code> (modular unsigned), plus <code"
       & ">Word_Size</code> and a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Target_Config</code> record carrying <code>Host_Bits</code> / <code>Ta"
       & "rget_Bits</code> / <code>Pointer_Bits</code>."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Checked_Add32</code> / <code>Checked_Add64</code> perform overflow-che"
       & "cked addition on the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "bounded types.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>Adacovex.IR_Synthesiser</code> (SPARK Off, string generation): <co"
       & "de>IR_Type_Name</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Lower_Type_Name</code> (case-sensitive: <code>int8_t</code>..<code>uin"
       & "t64_t</code>, <code>size_t</code>/<code>usize</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "-&gt; unsigned target-width, <code>isize</code> -&gt; signed target-width, <"
       & "code>ptrdiff_t</code> /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>uintptr_t</code> -&gt; pointer-width), and <code>Synthesize_Package</c"
       & "ode> that splits a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "comma/whitespace-separated type list into synthesized bounded Ada"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "declarations.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>Adacovex.IR_Bounds</code> (SPARK On): a gnatprove fixture that der"
       & "ives"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>int32_t</code> / <code>int64_t</code> from the bounded IR types and pr"
       & "oves the overflow"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "checks on <code>Add32</code> / <code>Add64</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " absence of integer overflow on the lowered"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "types is machine-checked.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c6-google--sphinx-docstring-styles""><a class=""header"" href=""#c6-goog"
       & "le--sphinx-docstring-styles"">C6: Google / Sphinx docstring styles</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The source scanner now also recognises the two most common non-Ada docstr"
       & "ing"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "conventions, so the same subprogram can be documented in Ada, Google, or"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Sphinx style:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Google</strong>: <code>Args:</code> / <code>Args: ...</code> hea"
       & "ders open a parameter block"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(deeper-indented following comment lines count as parameters); a <code>Retur"
       & "ns:</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "header marks the return-value description.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Sphinx</strong>: <code>:param Name:</code>, <code>:parameter Nam"
       & "e:</code>, <code>:type Name:</code>, <code>:return:</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>:returns:</code>, and <code>:rtype:</code> fields are all recognised.<"
       & "/li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""fixes""><a class=""header"" href=""#fixes"">Fixes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h1-unity-summary-count-separated-by-a-space""><a class=""header"" href="
       & """#h1-unity-summary-count-separated-by-a-space"">H1: Unity summary count separ"
       & "ated by a space</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>Number_Before_Word</code> only looked at the character immediately "
       & "before the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "keyword, so <code>1 Failures</code> (number + space + word) parsed as zero f"
       & "ailures and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "overwrote the correct totals. It now skips spaces back to the preceding digi"
       & "t"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "run.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""test-suite""><a class=""header"" href=""#test-suite"">Test Suite</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Test suite extended: Source scanner 40 -&gt; <strong>68</strong> checks ("
       & "comment-style"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "variants, tag aliases, Google/Sphinx styles, 12000-char single-line"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "declaration); Test-result parser 27 -&gt; <strong>35</strong> checks (TAP, A"
       & "utomake,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Surefire, Unity); new <strong>IR synthesis</strong> category (<strong>26</st"
       & "rong> checks). The suite"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "is now <strong>284 tests</strong>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""proof-results""><a class=""header"" href=""#proof-results"">Proof Results"
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Self-assessment: <strong>Platinum</strong> (36/36 VCs proved, AoRTE-free)"
       & " "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the four"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "overflow-checked adds on the bounded IR types"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>Target_Profiles.Checked_Add32/64</code>, <code>IR_Bounds.Add32/64</co"
       & "de>) are all machine"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "proved. Ada_CRDT proof run verified end-to-end via the dev-manifest swap"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(279 VCs, 5 justified).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""traceability""><a class=""header"" href=""#traceability"">Traceability</a"
       & "></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>New HLR <code>HLR-IR</code> (IR type profiles, host/target config, and fo"
       & "reign type-name lowering) covers the new <code>src/ir/</code> packages. Exis"
       & "ting tags continue to cover the changed packages (<code>-- HLR-SCAN</code> o"
       & "n <code>Adacovex. Parsers. Source</code>, <code>-- HLR-TEST</code> on `Adaco"
       & "vex.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Parsers. Tests<code>, </code>"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " HLR-PROVE<code>on</code>Adacovex. Core. Prove`).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                    </main>"
