       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""adacovex-160""><a class=""header"" href=""#adaco"
       & "vex-160"">adacovex 1.6.0</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Date: <em>2026-08-05</em></p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Version bumped 1.5.0 -&gt; 1.6.0.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""changes""><a class=""header"" href=""#changes"">Changes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c1-full-spark-proof-coverage-platinum-0-unproved""><a class=""header"" "
       & "href=""#c1-full-spark-proof-coverage-platinum-0-unproved"">C1: Full SPARK proo"
       & "f coverage (Platinum, 0 unproved)</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The whole SPARK-on codebase is now fully machine-proved. Previously only "
       & "the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "bounded IR types (<code>Checked_Add32/64</code>, <code>IR_Bounds.Add32/64</c"
       & "ode>) carried complete"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "proofs; every other SPARK unit was analysed but not fully discharged. Now"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<strong>all 491 VCs prove</strong> with <code>--prover=z3 --timeout=20</code"
       & ">, including the run-time"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "range checks, assertions, functional contracts, and loop termination:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Renderers</strong>: <code>I2S</code> (fixed <code>10**Pos</code>"
       & " overflow by replacing exponentiation"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "with a constant <code>Pow10</code> power table, loop invariants carrying the"
       & " digit"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "count and value bound, <code>Buf</code> initialized), <code>Pad2</code> and "
       & "<code>Escape_JSON</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(uninitialized-buffer fixes via <code>(others =&gt; ' ')</code>), and <code>"
       & "ISO_From_Epoch</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(chained <code>&amp;</code> concatenation upper-bound proofs replaced by a b"
       & "ounded"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Field</code>-copy buffer procedure). Postconditions now document the r"
       & "esult"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "lengths (<code>I2S'Result'Length in 1 .. 10</code>, <code>Pad2'Result'Length"
       & " in 1 .. 11</code>).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Parsers</strong>: <code>Trim</code>, <code>Trim_Left</code>, <co"
       & "de>Number_After</code>, and <code>Number_Before_Word</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "gained <code>Pre =&gt; S'First &gt;= 1 and S'Last &lt; Natural'Last</code> p"
       & "reconditions plus"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "strengthened loop invariants (carried array-index bounds and the digit-run"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "range <code>for all Q in DStart .. K =&gt; S (Q) in '0' .. '9'</code>).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>IR synthesiser</strong>: <code>Bits</code>, <code>IR_Type_Name</"
       & "code> (<code>Post =&gt; 'Result'Length &lt;= 9</code>),"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Lower_Type_Name</code>, and <code>Synthesize_Package</code> (buffer bo"
       & "unds, <code>Sub</code>/<code>Result</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "initialization, and <code>J &gt;= I</code> for the outer-loop variant) all p"
       & "roved.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Termination</strong>: every <code>while</code> loop across the c"
       & "odebase now carries an"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "explicit <code>Loop_Variant</code> (increasing or decreasing bound), so the "
       & "implicit"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Always_Terminates</code> aspects discharge "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " no loop is left as potentially"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "non-terminating.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The self-assessment is now: 26 packages, 59 subprograms, 100% docstrings,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<strong>Platinum (500/500 VCs, 0 unproved)</strong>, 295/295 tests, DAL-C Ac"
       & "hieved.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c2-host-word-size-auto-detection""><a class=""header"" href=""#c2-host-w"
       & "ord-size-auto-detection"">C2: Host word-size auto-detection</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Fixed-size buffers and the IR host model are now derived from the actual "
       & "host"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "word size instead of being hard-coded to 64-bit assumptions:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>Adacovex.Types.Host_Word_Bits : constant := System.Word_Size</code"
       & ">; the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Max_Path</code> / <code>Max_Line</code> path and line buffers scale wi"
       & "th it"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>64 * Host_Word_Bits</code> = 4096, <code>4096 * Host_Word_Bits</code>"
       & " = 262144 on a 64-bit"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "host), so builds on narrower hosts use proportionally smaller limits. The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "semantic limits (<code>Max_Id_Str</code>, <code>Max_Desc_Str</code>, <code>M"
       & "ax_Filename</code>) stay fixed.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>Adacovex.Target_Profiles.Host_Word_Size</code> auto-detects the ho"
       & "st word size"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(8/16/32/64) from the Ada runtime for <code>Target_Config.Host_Bits</code>, "
       & "with the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dead-branch warning resolved by a <code>case System.Word_Size</code> structu"
       & "re.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Test suite extended: 6 new checks (Types conversion + IR host-word-size"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "detection). The suite is now <strong>295 tests</strong>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c3-conventional-test-result-file-discovery""><a class=""header"" href="""
       & "#c3-conventional-test-result-file-discovery"">C3: Conventional test-result fi"
       & "le discovery</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The test-summary lookup is no longer hard-coded to <code>&lt;target&gt;/t"
       & "est_result.md</code>. A new <code>Parse_Test_Result_From_Project</code> sear"
       & "ches a conventional list of test-result file names at the project root (and "
       & "under <code>docs/</code>) and parses the first file that exists "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>test_result.md</code>, <code>test_results.md</code>, <code>test-resul"
       & "t.md</code>, <code>test_report.md</code>, <code>test_output.md</code>, the e"
       & "quivalent <code>.txt</code> and <code>.log</code> variants, <code>tests.md</"
       & "code>/<code>tests.txt</code>, and the <code>docs/</code> mirrors. The assess"
       & "ment, <code>sbom</code>, and <code>--compare-base</code> paths all use the n"
       & "ew lookup, so adacovex accepts common report conventions (e.g. CI that emits"
       & " <code>test_results.md</code> or <code>test-output.txt</code>) without confi"
       & "guration.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The parser itself already understood Markdown tables, plain <code>Passed:"
       & "</code>/<code>Failed:</code> summary lines, TAP, Automake, Maven Surefire, a"
       & "nd Unity formats. The new candidate search adds one SPARK-proved helper (<co"
       & "de>Trim_Right</code>, fully discharged) and 9 new VCs, taking the self-asses"
       & "sment to <strong>500/500 VCs Platinum</strong>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""fixes""><a class=""header"" href=""#fixes"">Fixes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h1-changelog-link-in-the-release-workflow""><a class=""header"" href=""#"
       & "h1-changelog-link-in-the-release-workflow"">H1: Changelog link in the release"
       & " workflow</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>.github/workflows/release.yml</code> built the changelog permalink "
       & "from the raw tag"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "name (<code>v1.6.0</code>), producing a broken <code>/docs/changelogs/adacov"
       & "ex-v1.6.0.md</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "URL. The link now strips the leading <code>v</code> (<code>${VERSION#v}</cod"
       & "e>) so it points at"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>docs/changelogs/adacovex-1.6.0.md</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The same release step now also:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Links the build-provenance attestation</strong> in the release n"
       & "otes. The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>actions/attest@v4</code> step is captured (<code>id: attest</code>) an"
       & "d its"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>attestation-url</code> output is included as a <em>Build Provenance At"
       & "testation</em>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "entry, so consumers can jump straight from the release to the signed"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "SLSA provenance bundle.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Fixes the <em>Git Changelog</em> compare link</strong> to use th"
       & "e tag form"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>compare/v1.5.0...v1.6.0</code> (previous version keeps its <code>v</co"
       & "de> prefix), matching"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "GitHub"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s tag-to-tag compare URL convention instead of the version-only form"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "produced by stripping the <code>v</code>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h2-honest-sbom-proof-levels--badge-contrast--install-docs""><a class="
       & """header"" href=""#h2-honest-sbom-proof-levels--badge-contrast--install-docs"">H"
       & "2: Honest SBOM proof levels + badge contrast + install docs</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>SBOM proof levels</strong>: Only the root component "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the project adacovex"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "actually assessed "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " now carries <code>adacovex:proof_level</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>Gold</code>/<code>Platinum</code>) and <code>adacovex:dal_target</cod"
       & "e>. Dependency components report"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>adacovex:proof_level = ""Not proved""</code>: adacovex only proves the t"
       & "arget"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "itself, never third-party dependencies, so they no longer claim a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Gold/Platinum level they did not earn. Applied to CycloneDX, SPDX, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Markdown outputs; the <code>Write_SBOM</code> summary line now says "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "root proof level"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & ".</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Platinum badge contrast</strong>: the SPARK badge used white tex"
       & "t on the light"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "platinum background (<code>#E5E4E2</code>), which failed contrast. Added a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Spark_Text_Color</code> selector (<code>#1a1a1a</code> on Platinum/Gol"
       & "d/Silver, white on"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Bronze/Stone) and a <code>Value_Text_Color</code> parameter to <code>Badge_S"
       & "VG</code>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Installation docs</strong>: README now documents installing adac"
       & "ovex via"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>alr install covex gnatprove</code> (add Alire"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s bin dir to <code>$PATH</code>), downloading"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the version-matched release bundle with <code>curl</code> from the GitHub Re"
       & "leases page"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(verifiable with <code>gh attestation verify</code>), or building from sourc"
       & "e. The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>prove</code>-mode GNATprove toolchain resolution order"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(per-project manifest -&gt; <code>$PATH</code> -&gt; cached toolchain -&gt; "
       & "download) is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "documented, including the "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "install Alire first"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " fallback when a manifest"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "declares gnatprove but <code>alr</code> is missing.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>SBOM timestamp to git commit</strong>: documented how to tie the"
       & " deterministic"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH</code> timestamp to the exact commit (<code>git -C &"
       & "lt;target&gt; log -1 --format=%ct</code>); the make targets already do this "
       & "from <code>HEAD</code>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h3-back-to-zero-dependency--gnatprove-moved-out-of-aliretoml""><a cla"
       & "ss=""header"" href=""#h3-back-to-zero-dependency--gnatprove-moved-out-of-aliret"
       & "oml"">H3: Back to zero-dependency "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " gnatprove moved out of <code>alire.toml</code></a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong><code>alire.toml</code> no longer declares gnatprove.</strong> T"
       & "he covex crate is once again"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "fully zero-dependency: no library or tool dependencies. <code>gnatprove</cod"
       & "e> lives"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "only in <code>alire-dev.toml</code> (used by the local make targets), and th"
       & "e <code>prove</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "subcommand resolves it at run time via the dev-manifest swap, <code>$PATH</c"
       & "ode>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>~/.adacovex/toolchain/</code>, or a download. Installing <code>covex</"
       & "code> no longer drags"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "in gnatprove or the proof solvers.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Install docs prefer the per-project manifest.</strong> README/AG"
       & "ENTS now lead"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "with declaring <code>covex</code> (plus <code>gnatprove</code> when proofs a"
       & "re wanted) in the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "project"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <code>alire-dev.toml</code>, keeping <code>alr install covex gnatprove</co"
       & "de> as the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "documented global alternative, alongside the GitHub release bundle and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "from-source installs.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Architecture decision: supported platforms.</strong> Since Alire"
       & " is the packaging"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and delivery mechanism, adacovex supports the platforms Alire itself"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "supports "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " binary distribution on Linux x86-64, Windows x86-64, and macOS"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "x86-64, and building from source on any host with GNAT FSF 9.2+ that can"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "build Alire. Added to <code>docs/architecture.md</code>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Architecture decision: CI tied to release version.</strong> Docu"
       & "mented that the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "GitHub Actions action is version-matched to the binary (the release workflow"
       & " bundles <code>adacovex-vX. Y. Z.tar.gz</code> for each tag, and the action "
       & "downloads the binary for the tag it is referenced by, with floating <code>vM"
       & "AJOR</code> / <code>vMAJOR. MINOR</code> / <code>latest</code> tags force-pu"
       & "shed at release time).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>CI runs on <code>ubuntu-latest</code> with the pinned <code>gnat-version<"
       & "/code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Release/index manifest templates</strong> (<code>alire/releases/"
       & "covex-0.0.0.toml</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>index/ad/covex/covex-0.1.0-dev.toml</code>, and the 1.6.0 variants) dr"
       & "opped the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "gnatprove dependency; <code>alire/alire.lock</code> regenerated accordingly."
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>The toolchain-resolution and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES wording now state plain"
       & "ly"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "that adacovex declares no gnatprove dependency and resolves it at run time.<"
       & "/li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h4-compilerproof-warning-cleanup--gnatprove-standard-companion""><a c"
       & "lass=""header"" href=""#h4-compilerproof-warning-cleanup--gnatprove-standard-co"
       & "mpanion"">H4: Compiler/proof warning cleanup + gnatprove standard companion</"
       & "a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Remaining build warnings fixed.</strong></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>Adacovex. Renderers. SBOM</code>: the compiler inlined <code>Field"
       & "</code> and constant-folded its <code>Sep /= ASCII. NUL</code> guard, so the"
       & " check reported "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "statement has no effect"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " at the call sites.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Kept the original single-loop form and wrapped it in <code>pragma Warning"
       & "s (Off/On, ""statement has no effect"")</code>; the two-loop <code>String</cod"
       & "e> alternative was tried and reverted because it cost 35 unproved VCs. Proof"
       & " remains intact: 500/500 VCs, Platinum, 0 unproved. - <code>Adacovex. Target"
       & "_Profiles</code>: <code>Host_Word_Size</code> is now a return-expression <co"
       & "de>case</code> (instead of an unreachable multi-branch <code>case</code> sta"
       & "tement on the 64-bit archive host), eliminating the "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "statement is never reached"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " warnings at lines 10/13/16. - Forced rebuild: <strong>0 warnings</strong>. "
       & "<code>make prove</code>: <strong>Platinum, 500/500 VCs, 0 unproved, 0 justif"
       & "ied</strong>. <code>make test</code>: <strong>295/295</strong>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong><code>gnatprove</code> is now the standard companion in every co"
       & "vex TOML usage.</strong>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "README (Option 1) and AGENTS (install item 1, dev-manifest usage) declare"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>covex = ""*""</code> with <code>gnatprove = ""^15.1.0""</code> in the same"
       & " manifest. The GitHub"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Actions <code>action.yml</code> no longer passes <code>gnatprove</code> to <"
       & "code>alr toolchain</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>gnatprove</code> is not a toolchain component; that failed CI with "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "The requested"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "crate is not a toolchain component"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & ") "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " it selects only <code>gnat_native</code> and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>gprbuild</code>, and the <code>prove</code> subcommand resolves gnatpr"
       & "ove via the target"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "project"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <code>alire-dev.toml</code> (README-preferred method), falling back to"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>$PATH</code>, the cached toolchain, or download. The "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "if you also want proof runs"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & ASCII.LF
       & "phrasing was removed.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>GitHub Actions attestation migrated to <code>actions/attest</cod"
       & "e>.</strong> The release"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "workflow now uses <code>actions/attest@v4</code> with <code>subject-path: ad"
       & "acovex-*.tar.gz</code> (kept <code>id: attest</code> + <code>attestation-url"
       & "</code> output);"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>attest-build-provenance@v2</code> is gone. All prose references (READM"
       & "E, AGENTS,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>docs/architecture.md</code>, Makefile) updated.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Crate tags expanded to 11</strong> across <code>alire.toml</code"
       & ">, <code>alire-dev.toml</code>, the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "release templates, and the index templates: <code>ada</code>, <code>spark</c"
       & "ode>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>formal-verify</code>, <code>cli</code>, <code>gnatprove</code>, <code>"
       & "sbom</code>, <code>tests</code>, <code>code-coverage</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>do-178c</code>, <code>compliance</code>, <code>developer-tools</code>."
       & " (<code>formal-verify</code> is used because"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Alire caps tag strings at 15 characters.)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Remaining badge contrast fixed.</strong> The bright-green (<code"
       & ">#4c1</code>) and yellow"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>#dfb317</code>) badge values used white text. Added a <code>Badge_Tex"
       & "t_Color</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "selector: dark <code>#1a1a1a</code> text on <code>#4c1</code>/<code>#dfb317<"
       & "/code>, white on the red"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>#e05d44</code>, matching the SPARK badge"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s approach. <code>tests.svg</code>, <code>do178c.svg</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and <code>docs.svg</code> regenerate with dark value text; SVG tests still p"
       & "ass.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong><code>install.sh</code> documents <code>curl | bash</code> and c"
       & "hecks for Alire.</strong> README Option"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "3 now leads with the one-liner"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>curl -fsSL .../main/install.sh | bash</code>), and the script warns w"
       & "hen <code>alr</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "is missing from <code>$PATH</code>, pointing at <code>curl https://alire.ada"
       & ".dev -sSf | sh</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and the remaining gnatprove fallbacks (<code>$PATH</code>, cached toolchain,"
       & " download).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "zero-library-dependency"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " -&gt; "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "zero-dependency"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & ".</strong> Renamed across README,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "AGENTS, and the <code>alire.toml</code> long-description (the published 1.0."
       & "0-1.5.0"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "release records keep their historical wording).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""test-suite""><a class=""header"" href=""#test-suite"">Test Suite</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Test suite extended: IR synthesis 26 -&gt; <strong>27</strong> checks plu"
       & "s six new word-size"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "checks (Types conversion + IR host-word-size detection); the suite is now"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<strong>295 tests</strong> (passing).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""proof-results""><a class=""header"" href=""#proof-results"">Proof Results"
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Self-assessment: <strong>Platinum</strong> (500/500 VCs proved, 0 unprove"
       & "d, AoRTE-free)."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Every SPARK-on unit is fully discharged "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " run-time checks 358/358,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "assertions 60/60, functional contracts 13/13, termination 44/44, flow"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "69/69. Proof invocation: <code>gnatprove -P adacovex.gpr --prover=z3 --timeo"
       & "ut=20</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""traceability""><a class=""header"" href=""#traceability"">Traceability</a"
       & "></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>No new HLRs. Existing tags continue to cover the changed packages: <code>"
       & "-- HLR-SCAN</code> on <code>Adacovex. Parsers. Source</code>, <code>-- HLR-T"
       & "EST</code> on `Adacovex.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Parsers. Tests<code>, </code>"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " HLR-PROVE<code>/</code>"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " HLR-METRICS<code>on</code>Adacovex. Types<code>, </code>"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " HLR-IR<code>on</code>Adacovex. Target_Profiles<code>and</code>Adacovex.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>IR_Synthesiser<code>, </code>"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " HLR-SBOM<code>on</code>Adacovex. Renderers. SBOM`. The HLR-SBOM wording was"
       & " tightened to reflect that only the root component carries proof-aware prope"
       & "rties while dependencies are reported as "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "Not proved"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & ".</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                    </main>"
