       & " no silent partial parses</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A physical line longer than <code>Max_Line</code> (262144 bytes on 64-bit"
       & ") was previously"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "silently truncated by the source scanner: the tail of the line was drained a"
       & "nd"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "discarded, and the remaining (partial) line was parsed as if it were the who"
       & "le"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "line. GNATprove, test-result, HLR/LLR, and manifest parsers had a related bu"
       & "g"
       & ASCII.LF
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " a full buffer was drained for the <em>next</em> physical line, misreading t"
       & "he"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "following content. Both behaviours could silently produce wrong metrics.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>All parsers now share an overflow-aware <code>Read_Line</code> helper on "
       & "the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Adacovex.Parsers</code> parent package:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Exact detection.</strong> A line that fills the buffer exactly ("
       & "end-of-line"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "reached) parses normally. A line that genuinely exceeds the buffer is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "detected via <code>End_Of_Line</code>, drained, and reported to stderr as"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Error: &lt;path&gt;:&lt;line&gt;: line exceeds Max_Line buffer (&lt;N&"
       & "gt; bytes)</code>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Explicit failure, never partial output.</strong> The scanner sto"
       & "ps parsing the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "offending file (no partial AST), and the GNATprove / test-result / HLR/LLR"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "parsers clear their output and fail. The manifest, lockfile, and GPR"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "parsers abort dependency-graph resolution.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>DAL is forced Unmet.</strong> <code>Scan_Project</code> returns "
       & "a new <code>Skipped_Ct</code>; when any"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "source file is skipped, the assessment appends <code>""N source file(s) skipp"
       & "ed: line exceeds Max_Line""</code> to the DAL failure reasons, sets the statu"
       & "s to"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Unmet</code>, and exits 1 "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " no compliance claim can be made for unread code.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Paths over <code>Max_Path</code> are reported and skipped</stron"
       & "g> instead of raising"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Constraint_Error</code>; <code>Push_Dir</code> warns on over-long dire"
       & "ctory paths rather"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "than silently dropping them.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Differential modes.</strong> <code>--compare-base</code> and <co"
       & "de>--coverage-delta</code> gain a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Skipped</code> field; a current tree with skipped sources is always a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "regression, and the diff reports <code>sources skipped</code>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Auto-SBOM exit-code fix.</strong> The automatic SBOM emission no"
       & " longer resets"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the assessment exit code to 0 on success (it now never touches <code>Exit_St"
       & "</code>),"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "so a DAL failure is reported correctly even when an SBOM is written.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c2-proof-scope-and-justification-policy-docs--reporting""><a class=""h"
       & "eader"" href=""#c2-proof-scope-and-justification-policy-docs--reporting"">C2: P"
       & "roof scope and justification policy (docs + reporting)</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Proof scope is the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s own units.</strong> GNATprove <code>Units_Analyzed</code> and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Units_Skipped</code> were parsed but never surfaced; they now appear i"
       & "n the ANSI"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "report and in <code>VERIFICATION.md</code>. Skipped units (standard library "
       & "/ vendor"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "code that GNATprove does not analyse) are explicitly out of proof scope, not"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "a proof failure.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Justifications never downgrade the level.</strong> A <code>Total"
       & "</code> row"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <code>Justified</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "count is counted neither as proved nor as unproved"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>Proved = Total - Justified - Unproved</code>), and only unproved VCs "
       & "cap the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "SPARK level. Pinned by new unit tests.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Gold is the minimum compliance baseline; Platinum is the ideal.<"
       & "/strong> The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Min_SPARK_For</code> thresholds are unchanged (A=Gold, B=Silver, C=Bro"
       & "nze,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "D/E=Stone); the API docs that previously claimed A=Platinum / B=Gold were"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "corrected to match the code, and the proof-scope / justification policy is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "documented as an architecture decision.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c3-gnatprove-prove-subcommand-options""><a class=""header"" href=""#c3-g"
       & "natprove-prove-subcommand-options"">C3: GNATprove <code>prove</code> subcomma"
       & "nd options</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code>prove</code> subcommand now forwards parallelism and proof-effo"
       & "rt options to"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "GNATprove instead of running a fixed invocation:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>--jobs=N</code> / <code>-j N</code> (or <code>-jN</code>): paralle"
       & "lism. Defaults to the detected host"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "core count (<code>/proc/cpuinfo</code>), so CI and the local make targets us"
       & "e every"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "core with no flag; <code>--jobs=0</code> forwards <code>-j0</code> (all core"
       & "s); <code>--jobs=12</code> pins 12.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>--level=N</code> (0-4), <code>--timeout=N</code> (s), <code>--step"
       & "s=N</code>, <code>--memlimit=N</code> (MB):"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "forwarded only when configured, leaving the tool defaults otherwise.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>-f</code> / <code>--force</code>, <code>--no-loop-unrolling</code>"
       & ", <code>--no-inlining</code>: mapped to the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "corresponding GNATprove switches.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Works across all three gnatprove resolution paths (alire-managed, dev-ma"
       & "nifest"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "swap, and direct binary).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c4-sbom-dependency-scopes-and-proof-level-property-fix""><a class=""he"
       & "ader"" href=""#c4-sbom-dependency-scopes-and-proof-level-property-fix"">C4: SBO"
       & "M dependency scopes and proof-level property fix</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Dependencies are now classified into <code>base</code> (publishing manif"
       & "est), <code>dev</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(dev manifest only), <code>transitive</code> (neither), and <code>vendored</"
       & "code> (overlaid by a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>.adacovex/patches/</code> docstring patch) via the <code>adacovex:dep_"
       & "scope</code> property;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "vendored packages are discovered by walking <code>&lt;target&gt;/.adacovex/p"
       & "atches/</code>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Fixed an unsatisfiable contract in <code>Scope_Property</code>: <code>""d"
       & "ev""</code> is 3 chars, so"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the postcondition <code>Length in 4 .. 10</code> was false for <code>Scope_D"
       & "ev</code> (and kept"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "GNATprove from proving the function). Corrected to <code>Length in 3 .. 10</"
       & "code>, which"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "restores the self-assessment to <strong>Platinum</strong>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c5-fixed-buffer-clamping--no-constraint_error-on-adversarial-input"">"
       & "<a class=""header"" href=""#c5-fixed-buffer-clamping--no-constraint_error-on-ad"
       & "versarial-input"">C5: Fixed-buffer clamping "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " no <code>Constraint_Error</code> on adversarial input</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Semantic text fields are clamped to their fixed buffers instead of raisin"
       & "g"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Constraint_Error</code> on oversized input, matching the two-tier over"
       & "flow contract"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(lines/paths fail loudly; identifiers/descriptions/tags clamp):</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Source scanner: HLR tag IDs (<code>Max_Id_Str</code>), docstring tag nam"
       & "es (64) and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "values (<code>Max_Desc_Str</code>), and subprogram names (<code>Max_Desc_Str"
       & "</code>) all clamp;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the full token is still consumed so following tokens are not misparsed.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>HLR/LLR markdown parser: entry IDs, descriptions, and HLR references cla"
       & "mp"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "with their <code>_Len</code> fields recorded as the clamped prefix.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>CLI config: <code>Set_String</code> clamps over-long option values (e.g."
       & " a <code>--target</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "path longer than <code>Max_Path</code>) instead of crashing.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Pinned by new regression tests (scanner 76 -&gt; 79, DAL 2 -&gt; 7).</li"
       & ">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""test-suite""><a class=""header"" href=""#test-suite"">Test Suite</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Suite extended from 295 to <strong>336 tests</strong>: source scanner (68"
       & " -&gt; 79, incl."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "over-Max_Line rejection, exact-buffer-fit acceptance, <code>Skipped_Ct</code"
       & ">, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "oversized-name/tag/value clamping), DAL compliance (2 -&gt; 7, incl. oversiz"
       & "ed"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "HLR/LLR entry clamping), GNATprove parser (38 -&gt; 52, incl. justified-VCs-"
       & "keep-"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Platinum, units analysed/skipped parsing, and overflow rejection), test-resu"
       & "lt"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "parser (40 -&gt; 43, incl. overflow rejection), and CLI config (11 -&gt; 19,"
       & " incl."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "prove-option defaults). All 336 pass.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""proof-results""><a class=""header"" href=""#proof-results"">Proof Results"
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Self-assessment remains <strong>Platinum</strong> (all VCs proved, 0 unpr"
       & "oved, AoRTE-free)."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "The parser bodies are non-SPARK units (as are all parser bodies); no proof"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "metrics regress. The corrected <code>Scope_Property</code> postcondition (C4"
       & ") is the one"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "proof change "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " it is now dischargeable and the sbom renderer proves clean.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""traceability""><a class=""header"" href=""#traceability"">Traceability</a"
       & "></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>No new HLRs. Existing tags continue to cover the changed packages: <code>"
       & "-- HLR-SCAN</code> on <code>Adacovex. Parsers. Source</code>, <code>-- HLR-P"
       & "ROOF</code> on `Adacovex.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Parsers. GNATprove<code>, </code>"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " HLR-TEST<code>on</code>Adacovex. Parsers. Tests<code>, </code>"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " HLR-COMPLIANCE<code>on</code>Adacovex.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Types<code>and</code>Adacovex. Compliance. DAL<code>, </code>"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " HLR-DIFF<code>on</code>Adacovex. Diff<code>, </code>"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " HLR-RENDER-ANSI<code>on</code>Adacovex.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Renderers. ANSI<code>, and </code>"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " HLR-SBOM<code>on</code>Adacovex. Renderers. SBOM`.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                    </main>"
