       & "                    <main>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""platform-support""><a class=""header"" href=""#p"
       & "latform-support"">Platform support</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex is a zero-dependency Ada/SPARK binary. It uses only the GNAT run"
       & "time and the standard library. As a result, any platform with a working GNAT"
       & "/Alire toolchain can build and run it.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex makes no OS-specific assumptions beyond the CPU-core and CI dete"
       & "ction described below. These features fall back to single-core operation whe"
       & "n the host cannot be probed.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""supported-platforms""><a class=""header"" href=""#supported-platforms"">S"
       & "upported platforms</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><th>Platform</th><th>Status</th><th>Notes</th></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>Linux x86-64</td><td><strong>Primary</strong></td><td>CI, releases, "
       & "and the proof toolchain bundle all target it.</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><strong>WSL</strong></td><td><strong>Supported</strong></td><td>Runs"
       & " on the Linux/WSL targets below: <code>man</code> installs to the WSL man ro"
       & "ot and <code>mandb</code> refreshes it; VCS snapshot commands run via <code>"
       & "sh -c</code>.</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>Linux aarch64</td><td>Supported</td><td>Builds from source; the preb"
       & "uilt toolchain bundle is x86-64 only.</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>macOS</td><td>Supported</td><td>Builds from source (Intel and Apple "
       & "Silicon).</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>FreeBSD</td><td>Supported</td><td>Builds from source.</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>Windows</td><td>Supported</td><td>Builds from source; core detection"
       & " uses the Windows env var + PowerShell fallback.</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""release-binaries""><a class=""header"" href=""#release-binaries"">Release"
       & " binaries</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The CI release binary is Linux x86-64 only. The <code>adacovex-vX. Y. Z.t"
       & "ar.gz</code> bundle (<code>adacovex</code> and the <code>covex</code> alias)"
       & " and the prebuilt GNATprove toolchain asset are built on <code>ubuntu-latest"
       & "</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Every other platform builds adacovex from source via Alire (<code>alr bui"
       & "ld</code>). See <a href=""https://github.com/bladeacer/adacovex/blob/main/REA"
       & "DME.md#installing-adacovex"">Installing adacovex</a>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""cpu-core-count-detection""><a class=""header"" href=""#cpu-core-count-de"
       & "tection"">CPU core-count detection</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>Adacovex.CPUs.Detect_Core_Count</code> returns the number of logica"
       & "l processors on the host. It falls back to <code>1</code> when the host cann"
       & "ot be probed. Detection order (pure GNAT runtime, no external library):</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Linux</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " count <code>processor</code> entries in <code>/proc/cpuinfo</code>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>macOS / FreeBSD</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>sysctl -n hw.ncpu</code>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Linux fallback</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>nproc</code>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Windows</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the <code>NUMBER_OF_PROCESSORS</code> environment variable.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Windows fallback</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " a PowerShell CIM query (<code>Get-CimInstance Win32_ComputerSystem</code>)."
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Each stage falls through to the next on failure. If all stages fail, the "
       & "function returns <code>1</code>. adacovex still runs when this happens. It r"
       & "uns single-threaded.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""ci-detection-and-prove-parallelism""><a class=""header"" href=""#ci-dete"
       & "ction-and-prove-parallelism"">CI detection and prove parallelism</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>Adacovex.CPUs.Is_Running_In_CI</code> detects the CI markers set by"
       & " GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, Azure Pipelines, Buildkite, CircleCI, Travis CI,"
       & " AppVeyor, Jenkins, and the generic <code>CI</code> variable.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>GNATprove parallelism resolves as:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>--jobs=N</code> (<code>N &gt; 0</code>) "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " exactly <code>N</code> jobs.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>--jobs=0</code> / <code>-j0</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " all cores (<code>gnatprove -j0</code>).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>default (<code>--jobs</code> omitted) "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <strong>all cores inside CI</strong>. Otherwise it uses <code>max(1, cores "
       & "- 2)</code>. As a result, a developer machine keeps two cores free for the s"
       & "ystem.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The chosen basis is printed in the verbose log (<code>Jobs_Justification<"
       & "/code>) and in the <a href=""#status-subcommand""><code>status</code></a> repo"
       & "rt. As a result, a proof run is auditable.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""status-subcommand""><a class=""header"" href=""#status-subcommand""><code"
       & ">status</code> subcommand</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>adacovex status</code> reports the toolchain and platform state wit"
       & "hout running any assessment and <strong>without downloading or deploying any"
       & "thing</strong>:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code>adacovex status --target=PATH"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>It checks and prints:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Alire</strong> (<code>alr</code>) is installed on <code>$PATH</c"
       & "ode>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>gnatprove</strong> is dependency-managed (target manifest pin) o"
       & "r detectable (global pin, on <code>$PATH</code>, or cached in <code>~/.adaco"
       & "vex/toolchain</code>). See <a href=""architecture.html#gnatprove-toolchain-re"
       & "solution-prove-subcommand"">Architecture "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " toolchain resolution</a>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>The <strong>logical CPU count</strong>, <strong>CI status</strong>, and "
       & "the resulting default <code>-j</code> parallelism are reported.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>A <strong>VCS report</strong> lists the VCS command-line tools available"
       & " on <code>$PATH</code> for the differential modes. The tools are git, mercur"
       & "ial/<code>hg</code>, subversion/<code>svn</code>, fossil, jj, and the man-pa"
       & "ge tool <code>mandb</code>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>The VCS report shows the VCS detected for the target repository.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>The VCS report notes when the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s VCS tool is missing.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>The VCS report notes when man-db (<code>mandb</code>) is absent. You the"
       & "n know that <code>adacovex man</code> can install the page but cannot refres"
       & "h the man database.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>The release note states that the CI binary is Linux x86-64 only.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Base adacovex functionality does not require a version control system. Th"
       & "e functionality includes scanning, proof analysis, test parsing, compliance "
       & "assessment, SBOM generation, dashboards, and caching. A VCS is only needed f"
       & "or the differential modes (<code>--compare-base</code> and <code>--coverage-"
       & "delta</code>).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The status command returns exit code <code>0</code> when a usable gnatpro"
       & "ve is detectable without a download. <code>alr</code> must be present when t"
       & "he deploy path is the only option. Otherwise, the command returns exit code "
       & "<code>1</code>. The VCS report is informational and does not affect the exit"
       & " code.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""local-man-page-linuxwsl""><a class=""header"" href=""#local-man-page-lin"
       & "uxwsl"">Local man page (Linux/WSL)</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>adacovex man</code> installs the man page into the local man databa"
       & "se without root. The default root is <code>$XDG_DATA_HOME/man</code> when se"
       & "t. Otherwise it is <code>~/.local/share/man</code>. This is the standard Lin"
       & "ux/WSL per-user man tree.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The index is refreshed with <code>mandb</code> when <code>mandb</code> is"
       & " present. Ubuntu and WSL ship <code>mandb</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>When man-db is not installed, or when <code>mandb</code> fails, adacovex "
       & "prints a warning. The warning states that the database was not refreshed. Th"
       & "e page is still installed. You can read it with <code>man -l ~/.local/share/"
       & "man/man1/adacovex.1</code>. <code>adacovex status</code> reports whether <co"
       & "de>mandb</code> is on <code>$PATH</code> up front.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>--dir=PATH</code> overrides the root. The page embeds the binary ve"
       & "rsion. <code>adacovex man --check</code> compares it to the installed page a"
       & "nd exits <code>0</code> or <code>1</code>. As a result, a prompt hook can au"
       & "to-install when a newer version is available. See <a href=""cli-reference.htm"
       & "l#man"">CLI reference</a>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""vcs-support-linuxwsl""><a class=""header"" href=""#vcs-support-linuxwsl"""
       & ">VCS support (Linux/WSL)</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>--compare-base</code> and <code>--coverage-delta</code> snapshot a "
       & "base revision across git, Mercurial, Subversion, Fossil, and jj. See <a href"
       & "=""vcs.html"">VCS support</a>. The snapshot commands run through <code>sh -c</"
       & "code>, which WSL provides. All temporary snapshots live under <code>/tmp/ada"
       & "covex-diff-&lt;pid&gt;</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>For VCS with poor snapshot UX (Subversion and Fossil), adacovex prints a "
       & "note. The note recommends conversion to git.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>See the <a href=""cli-reference.html"">CLI reference</a> for the full flag "
       & "surface.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                    </main>"
