       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""proving-and-writing-spark-proofs""><a class="""
       & "header"" href=""#proving-and-writing-spark-proofs"">Proving and writing SPARK p"
       & "roofs</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex runs gnatprove, reads its summary, and grades the result against"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the <a href=""api-docs/adacovex-spark-levels.html"">SPARK assurance levels</a>"
       & ". This page"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "is the guide to both halves: <strong>how proving works</strong> under adacov"
       & "ex, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<strong>how to write proofs</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " contracts in your own code, and "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " when the code"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "is vendored and cannot be modified "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <strong>proof patches</strong> that add the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "contracts for you.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""proving-a-project-with-adacovex""><a class=""header"" href=""#proving-a-"
       & "project-with-adacovex"">Proving a project with adacovex</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code class=""language-bash"">adacovex prove --target=."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code>prove</code> subcommand (full options:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a href=""cli-reference.html#the-prove-subcommand"">CLI reference "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the <code>prove</code> subcommand</a>):</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Resolves gnatprove</strong> without requiring the target to decl"
       & "are it:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "manifest pin &gt; global pin &gt; <code>$PATH</code> &gt; cached toolchain &"
       & "gt; download. Full"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "order and per-method detail:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a href=""architecture.html#gnatprove-toolchain-resolution-prove-subcommand"">"
       & "Architecture "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " GNATprove toolchain resolution</a>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Runs gnatprove</strong> against the target (or against a patched"
       & " tree copy"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "when proof patches are present "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " see"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a href=""#proof-patches-proving-vendored-dependencies"">Proof patches</a> bel"
       & "ow) and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "writes the summary to <code>&lt;target&gt;/obj/gnatprove/gnatprove.out</code"
       & "> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the same"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "location the assessment pipeline discovers.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Falls through to the full assessment</strong>. The assessment pa"
       & "rses the fresh"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "summary. One command both proves and assesses. The <code>--require-*</code> "
       & "CI gates"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "apply to the proof run directly (<code>--require-spark=Platinum --require-pr"
       & "oof=100</code> and more; see"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a href=""cli-reference.html#ci-threshold-gates---require-"">CLI reference "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " CI threshold gates</a>).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The result cache serves unchanged targets so repeated runs are cheap."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>--force</code> bypasses the cache and forces a full gnatprove reanalys"
       & "is. A target"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "without a <code>gnatprove.out</code> at all is graded <code>Stone</code> wit"
       & "h proof metrics <code>N/A</code>."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Run <code>prove</code> to generate one.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""what-a-proof-contains""><a class=""header"" href=""#what-a-proof-contain"
       & "s"">What a proof contains</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>gnatprove reports verification conditions (VCs) per check category. The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "summary in <code>gnatprove.out</code> breaks them down as:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><th>Category</th><th>What it covers</th></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>Run-time checks</td><td>Index bounds, overflow, division-by-zero, ra"
       & "nge checks "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " absence of run-time errors</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>Assertions</td><td>User <code>pragma Assert</code> statements and pr"
       & "e/postcondition checks</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>Functional contracts</td><td><code>Pre</code> / <code>Post</code> / "
       & "<code>Global</code> contract satisfaction</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>Data dependencies</td><td>Flow analysis: uninitialized reads, effect"
       & "ive <code>Global</code> contracts</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>Initialization</td><td>All objects initialized before first use</td>"
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>Termination</td><td><code>Loop_Variant</code> / recursion bounds (su"
       & "bprograms proved terminating)</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The honest <strong>proved</strong> count is <code>total - justified - unp"
       & "roved</code> (flow plus"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "provers). The <a href=""api-docs/adacovex-spark-levels.html"">assurance level<"
       & "/a> is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "derived from how many of each category were discharged:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Stone</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " no proof run or nothing analyzable;</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Bronze</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " flow analysis clean (data dependencies, initialization);</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Silver</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " run-time checks proved, assertions proved;</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Gold</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " functional contracts proved on top;</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Platinum</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " every VC proved: <strong>0 unproved</strong> (and, in adacovex"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s own"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "gate, <strong>0 justified</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " no <code>pragma Annotate</code> justifications).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Justified VCs count neither as proved nor as unproved. Only unproved VCs"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "downgrade the level. For a DAL assessment, the level must meet the requireme"
       & "nt"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "of the tier (<code>--dal=C</code> needs Bronze, <code>--dal=A</code> needs G"
       & "old, and more) "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " see"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a href=""api-docs/adacovex-dal-levels.html"">DAL levels</a>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""writing-proofs-spark-contracts""><a class=""header"" href=""#writing-pro"
       & "ofs-spark-contracts"">Writing proofs: SPARK contracts</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A proof starts with contracts in the source, written as Ada aspects:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code class=""language-ada"">package Body_Vec is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   function Clamp (Value : in Integer; Lo : in Integer; Hi : in Integer)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "     return Integer"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "     with Pre  =&gt; Lo &lt;= Hi,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "          Post =&gt; Clamp'Result in Lo .. Hi;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "end Body_Vec;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Rules that matter in practice:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong><code>SPARK_Mode =&gt; On</code> selects what gnatprove analyses"
       & ".</strong> Without it a unit"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "is out of proof scope. It can be declared on the package"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>package P with SPARK_Mode =&gt; On is</code>), on individual subprogr"
       & "ams, or"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "both "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " adacovex"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s own source uses package-level On on pure units and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "per-subprogram On aspects inside default-off bodies.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>A body is analysed only when the body itself opts in.</strong> D"
       & "eclaring"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>SPARK_Mode =&gt; On</code> on the <em>spec</em> does not make gnatprov"
       & "e analyse the body."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "The body must declare it too (on the <code>package body</code> line or per s"
       & "ubprogram)."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "This is the rule that makes proof patches necessary for vendored code "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " see"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "below.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>I/O bodies are skipped by design.</strong> A body that calls <co"
       & "de>Ada.Text_IO</code> (which"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "is <code>SPARK_Mode Off</code>) cannot be analysed. gnatprove reports the un"
       & "it out of"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "proof scope. This never drags the assessed level down "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " it means those"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "bodies are not proved.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Contracts are proved against the body.</strong> gnatprove proves"
       & " that every"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "possible body execution satisfies the declared <code>Pre</code>/<code>Post</"
       & "code>. Callers must in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "turn establish the <code>Pre</code> before calling.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong><code>--steps</code> controls the proof budget.</strong> gnatpro"
       & "ve"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s default step limit can"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "produce solver-timeout false negatives. adacovex runs with <code>--steps 100"
       & "00</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "by default so such timeouts are not reported as unproved. An explicit"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>--steps=N</code> overrides.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The goal for a clean proof: every VC in every category proved, 0 unproved"
       & ","
       & ASCII.LF
       & "0 justified.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""proof-patches-proving-vendored-dependencies""><a class=""header"" href="
       & """#proof-patches-proving-vendored-dependencies"">Proof patches: proving vendor"
       & "ed dependencies</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Patch files at <code>&lt;target&gt;/.adacovex/patches/</code> exist so ve"
       & "ndored code you"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cannot modify still counts toward the audit. Their best-known job is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "overlaying <strong>docstrings</strong> for strict-mode coverage. A patch can"
       & " also carry"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<strong>SPARK proof aspects</strong> so vendored dependencies participate in"
       & " the proof"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "with real contracts "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " without forking or touching their sources.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""why-proof-patches-are-necessary""><a class=""header"" href=""#why-proof-"
       & "patches-are-necessary"">Why proof patches are necessary</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Three facts force the design:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Strict mode counts vendored code.</strong> By default adacovex s"
       & "cans every"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "directory except the always-excluded ones. The excluded directories are"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>.git</code>, <code>obj</code>, <code>tests</code>, <code>config</code>"
       & ", and <code>.adacovex</code>. A vendored dependency"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "missing docstrings and missing contracts count against the target."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>--relaxed</code> skips vendored dirs but drops the audit to a quick pa"
       & "ss "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " not"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "an option for a compliance assessment.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>gnatprove analyses a body only when the body itself opts in.</st"
       & "rong> (The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "rule from <a href=""#writing-proofs-spark-contracts"">Writing proofs</a> above"
       & ".) A"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "vendored spec with no contracts contributes nothing to the proof. A"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "vendored body without <code>SPARK_Mode</code> is skipped entirely.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>The vendored sources are immutable.</strong> The dependency ship"
       & "s as-is. You"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cannot add contracts to it. Re-publishing a patched fork defeats the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "point of vendoring.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A proof patch is the merge of these three constraints. It re-declares the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "vendored spec with contracts (<code>.ads</code> patch). It opts the vendored"
       & " body into"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the proof (<code>.adb</code> patch). The <code>prove</code> subcommand merge"
       & "s both into a patched"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tree copy before running gnatprove "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the originals are never touched.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""how-proof-patches-are-applied""><a class=""header"" href=""#how-proof-pa"
       & "tches-are-applied"">How proof patches are applied</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>Count_Proof_Patches</code> scans <code>&lt;target&gt;/.adacovex/pa"
       & "tches/</code> for <code>.ads</code> and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>.adb</code> files. A patch carrying any of <code>SPARK_Mode</code>, <c"
       & "ode>Pre =&gt;</code>, <code>Post =&gt;</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "or <code>Global =&gt;</code> is a <em>proof patch</em>. A docstring-only pat"
       & "ch never engages"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the proof machinery. A target with no proof patches is proved against its"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "own tree exactly as before.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>Build_Patched_Copy</code> copies the target tree (excluding <code>"
       & ".git</code>, <code>obj</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and <code>.adacovex</code>) into <code>&lt;target&gt;/obj/adacovex-proof/</c"
       & "ode> and overwrites each"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "proof-patched source with its merged form.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>gnatprove runs against the copy"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s root project and the resulting"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>gnatprove.out</code> is copied back to <code>&lt;target&gt;/obj/gnatpr"
       & "ove/gnatprove.out</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "for the assessment pipeline.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Patch contents are folded into the prove result-cache key, so a patch"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "edit invalidates the cached proof and forces a re-prove (<code>--force</code"
       & "> also"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "bypasses the cache).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The patched copy lives under the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <code>obj/</code>, so it is excluded from"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "scanning, manifest graphs, and the prove input hash.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""writing-a-spec-patch-ads""><a class=""header"" href=""#writing-a-spec-pa"
       & "tch-ads"">Writing a spec patch (<code>.ads</code>)</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A spec patch mirrors the vendored spec: same package name, same subprogra"
       & "m"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "declarations (with docstrings, since strict mode requires them), plus the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "aspects you want gnatprove to prove:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code class=""language-ada"">--  .adacovex/patches/demo/deps/vt100/vt100."
       & "ads"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "package VT100 with SPARK_Mode =&gt; On is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   --  Scroll a region of the screen up."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   --  @param From  Starting line of scroll region."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   --  @param To    Ending line of scroll region."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   procedure Scroll_Screen (From : in Natural; To : in Natural)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "     with Pre =&gt; From &lt;= To;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "end VT100;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The merge splices the package-level aspect onto the original package"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "declaration line and replaces each aspect-carrying subprogram declaration"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "with the patch"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s declaration block. Subprograms the patch does not re-declare"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "with aspects are left untouched, so a patch can add a contract to one"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "subprogram without disturbing its siblings.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""writing-a-body-patch-adb""><a class=""header"" href=""#writing-a-body-pa"
       & "tch-adb"">Writing a body patch (<code>.adb</code>)</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The spec patch declares the contracts. The <strong>body patch</strong> is"
       & " what makes"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "gnatprove actually analyse the vendored body (the body-must-opt-in rule). It"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "lives at the body"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s relative path and mirrors the body"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s declarations with"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<em>stub bodies</em> that the merge ignores "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the original implementation is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "preserved:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code class=""language-ada"">--  .adacovex/patches/demo/deps/vecmath/vecm"
       & "ath.adb"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "package body Vecmath with SPARK_Mode =&gt; On is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   function Clamp (Value : in Integer; Lo : in Integer; Hi : in Integer)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "     return Integer with SPARK_Mode =&gt; On is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   begin"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "      null;  --  stub: the original body's implementation is kept"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   end Clamp;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "end Vecmath;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The merge replaces the original declaration (up to its <code>is</code>) w"
       & "ith the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "patch"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s aspect-carrying declaration and keeps the original body proper, so"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the copy gnatprove sees is <code>package body Vecmath with SPARK_Mode =&gt; "
       & "On is ... &lt;original implementation&gt; ...</code>. A fully SPARK-clean bo"
       & "dy needs only the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "package-level aspect. The per-subprogram aspect covers bodies with a mix of"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "clean and I/O-bound subprograms.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""matching-rules""><a class=""header"" href=""#matching-rules"">Matching ru"
       & "les</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The merge matches each patched declaration against the original by <stron"
       & "g>name and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "normalised parameter profile</strong>:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Matching is whitespace-insensitive. A single-line parameter list matches"
       & " a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "multi-line one.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>The default <code>in</code> mode is equivalent to a bare mode (<code>X :"
       & " in Integer</code> matches"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>X : Integer</code>). <code>in out</code> and <code>out</code> are dist"
       & "inct modes.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>an overloaded subprogram patches its exact signature "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " a patched"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "two-argument <code>Scroll_Screen</code> replaces the two-argument original, "
       & "never a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "same-named sibling;</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>a spec declaration terminates at its <code>;</code>, a body declaration "
       & "at its <code>is</code>;</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>a patched subprogram with <strong>no match</strong> in the original fail"
       & "s loudly (the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "patch is skipped and reported) rather than silently dropping the contract.</"
       & "li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""worked-example-vecmathclamp""><a class=""header"" href=""#worked-example"
       & "-vecmathclamp"">Worked example: <code>Vecmath.Clamp</code></a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A vendored package whose spec and body carry no contracts:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code class=""language-ada"">--  demo/deps/vecmath/vecmath.ads (vendored,"
       & " unmodified)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "package Vecmath is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   function Clamp (Value : in Integer; Lo : in Integer; Hi : in Integer)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "     return Integer;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "end Vecmath;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code class=""language-ada"">--  demo/deps/vecmath/vecmath.adb (vendored,"
       & " unmodified)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "package body Vecmath is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   function Clamp (Value : in Integer; Lo : in Integer; Hi : in Integer)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "     return Integer is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   begin"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "      if Value &lt; Lo then"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "         return Lo;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "      elsif Value &gt; Hi then"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "         return Hi;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "      else"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "         return Value;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "      end if;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   end Clamp;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "end Vecmath;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The two patch files from above (spec with"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Pre =&gt; Lo &lt;= Hi, Post =&gt; Clamp'Result in Lo .. Hi</code>, and"
       & " body with"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>SPARK_Mode =&gt; On</code>) merge into the copy unchanged in behaviour"
       & ". gnatprove"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "proves the contract: 2 VCs (the <code>Clamp</code> postcondition and its ter"
       & "mination"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "check), 0 unproved. A caller in the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s own code can then rely on the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "contract without the vendored sources ever changing.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""when-contracts-prove--and-when-they-are-skipped""><a class=""header"" h"
       & "ref=""#when-contracts-prove--and-when-they-are-skipped"">When contracts prove "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " and when they are skipped</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>SPARK-clean body + body patch</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " gnatprove proves the patched"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "contracts outright (the example above).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>I/O-bound body</strong> (calls <code>Ada.Text_IO</code>, which i"
       & "s <code>SPARK_Mode Off</code>) "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & ASCII.LF
       & "gnatprove skips the I/O bodies by design and reports the unit out of proof"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "scope. The contracts are still <em>declared</em> and the mechanism is exerci"
       & "sed,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "but the body is not proved "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " and crucially, it never drags the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "proof level down. This is the VT100 dogfood case in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a href=""https://github.com/bladeacer/Ada_CRDT"">Ada_CRDT</a>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""common-pitfalls""><a class=""header"" href=""#common-pitfalls"">Common pi"
       & "tfalls</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Spec patch without a body patch.</strong> A SPARK-clean vendored"
       & " body stays out"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "of proof scope. gnatprove reports "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "no checks generated"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " or skips the unit."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Add the <code>.adb</code> patch to opt the body in.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>A patched declaration that does not match anything.</strong> Che"
       & "ck the name and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the parameter list (modes included) against the original. The merge reports"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>could not be merged ... (unmatched subprogram or oversized file)</code"
       & "> and skips"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the patch.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Patching the wrong overload.</strong> The match is profile-aware"
       & ", so a patch"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "entry replaces exactly the signature it re-declares "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " verify you wrote the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "same parameter list as the overload you mean.</li>"
