       & "                <div id=""mdbook-content"" class=""content"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                    <main>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""the-sbom-subcommand""><a class=""header"" href="
       & """#the-sbom-subcommand"">The <code>sbom</code> subcommand</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""when-and-why-to-generate-an-sbom""><a class=""header"" href=""#when-and-"
       & "why-to-generate-an-sbom"">When and why to generate an SBOM</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A Software Bill of Materials (SBOM) is a structured inventory of every"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "component in your project, plus its provenance, licence, and (in adacovex"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "case) its SPARK proof level and compliance context. Generate one in these"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cases:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Auditing or certifying</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " an SBOM is a standard artifact for safety"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "certification (DO-178C, ISO 26262, IEC 62304). It shows the auditor exactly"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "which Ada/Alire components are in scope and which are proved / not proved.</"
       & "li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Shifting left on supply-chain security</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the dependency graph exposes"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "transitive dependencies, their licences, and their PURLs so you can review"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "them before a release.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Embedding in CI</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the proof-aware SBOM carries the assessed standard and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "level, so downstream tooling (policy engines, compliance dashboards) can"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "consume it without re-parsing markdown reports.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Reproducible builds</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " adacovex honours <code>SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH</code>, so the SBOM"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "timestamp is deterministic when tied to a git commit.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>adacovex sbom</code> resolves the target project"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s dependency graph from its Alire"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "manifest (<code>alire.toml</code> / <code>alire-dev.toml</code>), the solved"
       & "-crate list in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>alire/alire.lock</code>, and the root <code>.gpr</code> <code>with</co"
       & "de> clauses, then writes a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "proof-aware software bill of materials in CycloneDX 1.5 JSON, SPDX 2.3 JSON,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "or Markdown.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""how-to-read-the-output""><a class=""header"" href=""#how-to-read-the-out"
       & "put"">How to read the output</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Choose the format that matches your toolchain:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>CycloneDX 1.5 JSON</strong> (<code>--format=cyclonedx-json</code"
       & ">) "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " drop into any CycloneDX"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "consumer (Dependency-Track, OWASP Dependency-Check, and more). The root"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "component"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "carries <code>adacovex:proof_level</code>, <code>adacovex:standard</code>, <"
       & "code>adacovex:dal_target</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and <code>adacovex:level</code>. Every dependency has a <code>language</code"
       & "> field inferred from"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "file extensions or declared ecosystems.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>SPDX 2.3 JSON</strong> (<code>--format=spdx-json</code>) "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " compatible with SPDX-aware tools"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(FOSSA, Snyk, ScanCode). The adacovex properties appear as"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>attributionTexts</code> on the root package.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Markdown</strong> (<code>--format=md</code>) "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " human-readable table, useful for audits and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "reports. Default path is <code>&lt;target&gt;/docs/compliance/SBOM.md</code>"
       & ".</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""key-fields""><a class=""header"" href=""#key-fields"">Key fields</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><th>Field</th><th>Where it appears</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>adacovex:proof_level</code></td><td>Root component</td><td>Ass"
       & "essed SPARK level (<code>Stone</code> .. <code>Platinum</code>)</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>adacovex:standard</code></td><td>Root component</td><td>Compli"
       & "ance standard (<code>DO-178C</code>, <code>ISO 26262</code>, <code>IEC 62304"
       & "</code>)</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>adacovex:dal_target</code></td><td>Root component</td><td>Shar"
       & "ed rigour tier (<code>DAL-A</code> .. <code>DAL-E</code>)</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>adacovex:level</code></td><td>Root component</td><td>Standard-"
       & "specific label (<code>DAL-C</code>, <code>ASIL B</code>, <code>Class A</code"
       & ">)</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>language</code></td><td>Every component</td><td>Implementation"
       & " language(s) inferred from file extensions</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>purl</code></td><td>Every component</td><td>Package URL for re"
       & "gistry linking</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Dependencies report <code>adacovex:proof_level = ""Not proved""</code> beca"
       & "use adacovex only"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "proves the target itself. The SBOM is mutually exclusive with <code>--compar"
       & "e-base</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and <code>--coverage-delta</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""usage""><a class=""header"" href=""#usage"">Usage</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code>adacovex sbom [--format=cyclonedx-json|spdx-json|md] [--out=PATH]"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "           [--standard=NAME|--dal=LEVEL|--asil=LEVEL|--class=LEVEL]"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Default output</strong>: <code>&lt;target&gt;/sbom.json</code> f"
       & "or <code>cyclonedx-json</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>&lt;target&gt;/sbom.spdx.json</code> for <code>spdx-json</code>, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>&lt;target&gt;/docs/compliance/SBOM.md</code> for <code>md</code>. The"
       & " containing directory is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "created automatically.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Exit code</strong>: <code>0</code> when the SBOM was written, <c"
       & "ode>1</code> otherwise. If the target"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "has no Alire manifest the SBOM cannot be generated (the GitHub Action"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "reports this as a warning without failing the job).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""standard-awareness""><a class=""header"" href=""#standard-awareness"">Sta"
       & "ndard-awareness</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code>sbom</code> subcommand accepts the same standard flags as the a"
       & "ssessment"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>--standard</code>, <code>--dal</code>, <code>--asil</code>, <code>--c"
       & "lass</code>) and <strong>defaults to all"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "standards</strong>: without an explicit standard flag the SBOM carries the j"
       & "oined"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "DO-178C / ISO 26262 / IEC 62304 properties at the shared DAL tier."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>--standard=iso26262</code> / <code>--asil=B</code> narrows it to ISO 2"
       & "6262 at ASIL B, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>--class=A</code> to IEC 62304 at Class A. See <a href=""standards.html"""
       & ">Standards</a> for the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cross-standard tier mapping.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""properties""><a class=""header"" href=""#properties"">Properties</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Only the root component "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the project adacovex actually assessed "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " carries:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>adacovex:proof_level</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>Stone</code>..<code>Platinum</code>, the honest assessed level.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>adacovex:standard</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>DO-178C</code> / <code>ISO 26262</code> / <code>IEC 62304</code>.</li"
       & ">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>adacovex:dal_target</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>DAL-A</code>..<code>DAL-D</code> (omitted for <code>DAL-E</code>).</l"
       & "i>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>adacovex:level</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the standard-specific label (<code>DAL-C</code> / <code>ASIL B</code> /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Class A</code>, omitted for <code>DAL-E</code>).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Dependency components report <code>adacovex:proof_level = ""Not proved""</c"
       & "ode> (adacovex"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "only proves the target itself, never third-party dependencies). Properties a"
       & "re"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "encoded as <code>attributionTexts</code> in SPDX.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""determinism""><a class=""header"" href=""#determinism"">Determinism</a></"
       & "h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code>metadata.timestamp</code> / <code>creationInfo.created</code> f"
       & "ield honors the <code>SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH</code> environment variable (reprodu"
       & "cible-builds convention). When set to a Unix epoch second count, the timesta"
       & "mp is derived from it in UTC via pure integer math. As a result, SBOM output"
       & " is byte-for-byte deterministic across runs and machines. To tie it to a spe"
       & "cific git commit, run <code>export SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH=$(git -C &lt;target&gt;"
       & " log -1 --format=%ct)</code> before adacovex.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The bundled <code>make</code> targets (<code>run-self</code>, <code>run-a"
       & "da-crdt</code>, <code>prove</code>, <code>release</code>, and Ada_CRDT"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <code>prove</code>/<code>badges</code>) already set it from the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s git <code>HEAD</code> commit time.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""exclusivity-and-ordering""><a class=""header"" href=""#exclusivity-and-o"
       & "rdering"">Exclusivity and ordering</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>sbom</code> is mutually exclusive with <code>--compare-base</code> "
       & "and <code>--coverage-delta</code>. It"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "scans sources, parses proof/test results, and assesses DAL first. As a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "result, the emitted properties reflect the real assessment state.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Both formats validate against the official"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a href=""https://github.com/CycloneDX/specification"">CycloneDX 1.5</a> and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a href=""https://spdx.dev"">SPDX 2.3</a> JSON schemas (see"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a href=""THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.html"">THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md</a>).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""language-detection""><a class=""header"" href=""#language-detection"">Lan"
       & "guage detection</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Every dependency component carries a <code>language</code> field (Cyclone"
       & "DX JSON /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>components[].properties</code> under <code>""name"": ""adacovex:language"""
       & "</code>, or the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Markdown table"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <code>Language</code> column) describing the implementation language(s)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "of that dependency.  Detection follows the component"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s origin, most specific"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "first.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""manifest-declared-ecosystems""><a class=""header"" href=""#manifest-decl"
       & "ared-ecosystems"">Manifest-declared ecosystems</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A vendored manifest maps directly onto its language and PURL type:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><th>Manifest file</th><th>PURL type</th><th>Language</th></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>package.json</code></td><td><code>pkg:npm</code></td><td>JavaS"
       & "cript</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>Cargo.toml</code></td><td><code>pkg:cargo</code></td><td>Rust<"
       & "/td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>go.mod</code></td><td><code>pkg:golang</code></td><td>Go</td><"
       & "/tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>pyproject.toml</code></td><td><code>pkg:pypi</code></td><td>Py"
       & "thon</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>requirements*.txt</code></td><td><code>pkg:pypi</code></td><td"
       & ">Python</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>composer.json</code></td><td><code>pkg:composer</code></td><td"
       & ">PHP</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>Gemfile</code></td><td><code>pkg:gem</code></td><td>Ruby</td><"
       & "/tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>pom.xml</code></td><td><code>pkg:maven</code></td><td>Java</td"
       & "></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>Package.swift</code></td><td><code>pkg:swift</code></td><td>Sw"
       & "ift</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>Alire manifest</td><td><code>pkg:alire</code></td><td>Ada</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>.gpr</code> project file</td><td><code>pkg:gpr</code></td><td>"
       & "Ada</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""extension-based-inference""><a class=""header"" href=""#extension-based-"
       & "inference"">Extension-based inference</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>For every other component "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " vendored trees, <code>vendor/</code>, <code>node_modules</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "resources, loose source drops, and individual files inside <code>resources/<"
       & "/code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>assets/</code>, and <code>.adacovex/patches/</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " adacovex infers the language from the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<strong>file extensions actually present</strong>.  The extension is the sou"
       & "rce of truth: a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>.py</code> file reports Python even when a <code>Cargo.toml</code> sit"
       & "s next to it, and the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "manifest language only breaks ties.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Supported extensions:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Ada</strong>: <code>.ads</code>, <code>.adb</code>, <code>.ada</"
       & "code>, <code>.gpr</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>JavaScript</strong>: <code>.js</code>, <code>.mjs</code>, <code>"
       & ".cjs</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>TypeScript</strong>: <code>.ts</code>, <code>.tsx</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>CSS</strong>: <code>.css</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>HTML</strong>: <code>.html</code>, <code>.htm</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Python</strong>: <code>.py</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Go</strong>: <code>.go</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Rust</strong>: <code>.rs</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>C</strong>: <code>.c</code>, <code>.h</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>C++</strong>: <code>.cpp</code>, <code>.cc</code>, <code>.cxx</c"
       & "ode>, <code>.hpp</code>, <code>.hh</code>, <code>.hxx</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>C#</strong>: <code>.cs</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Java</strong>: <code>.java</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Ruby</strong>: <code>.rb</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>PHP</strong>: <code>.php</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Swift</strong>: <code>.swift</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Kotlin</strong>: <code>.kt</code>, <code>.kts</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Scala</strong>: <code>.scala</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>OCaml</strong>: <code>.ml</code>, <code>.mli</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Lua</strong>: <code>.lua</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Perl</strong>: <code>.pl</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Haskell</strong>: <code>.hs</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Elixir</strong>: <code>.ex</code>, <code>.exs</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Erlang</strong>: <code>.erl</code>, <code>.hrl</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Clojure</strong>: <code>.clj</code>, <code>.cljs</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Dart</strong>: <code>.dart</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Shell</strong>: <code>.sh</code>, <code>.bash</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>PowerShell</strong>: <code>.ps1</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>SQL</strong>: <code>.sql</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Fortran</strong>: <code>.f</code>, <code>.f90</code>, <code>.f95"
       & "</code>, <code>.f03</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Assembly</strong>: <code>.s</code>, <code>.asm</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>R</strong>: <code>.r</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Julia</strong>: <code>.jl</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Zig</strong>: <code>.zig</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>VHDL</strong>: <code>.vhd</code>, <code>.vhdl</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Tcl</strong>: <code>.tcl</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A directory that mixes languages reports its <strong>top 3</strong> langu"
       & "ages by file count"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(for example <code>""Ada; C; C++""</code>), so a mixed-language vendored drop "
       & "is summarised"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "by what it actually contains rather than by a single guess.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""licence-resolution""><a class=""header"" href=""#licence-resolution"">Lic"
       & "ence resolution</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Vendored manifest ecosystems report their licence from the local manifest"
       & ":"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>package.json</code> (<code>license</code>) for npm/pnpm, <code>Cargo.t"
       & "oml</code> for cargo,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>pyproject.toml</code> / <code>composer.json</code> for pypi / composer"
       & ". When the local"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "manifest carries no licence, adacovex resolves the version, website, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "licence from the package registry as a best-effort, online fallback. The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "resolver dispatches on the ecosystem (the PURL type) through a single static"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "table, so adding a language is one row rather than a new code path:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>npm</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>npm view &lt;pkg&gt; version license homepage --json</code>, parsed f"
       & "or the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "three fields from one JSON object.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>pnpm</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>pnpm show &lt;pkg&gt; version license homepage --json</code>, likewis"
       & "e.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>cargo</strong> (Rust) "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>cargo search &lt;pkg&gt;</code>, with the SPDX id read from the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>(license: ...)</code> token in the output.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>go</strong> and other ecosystems with no portable, reliable regi"
       & "stry query keep"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "an empty licence; the vendored manifest scanner still reads any in-repo"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "licence file for them.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The npm and pnpm rows answer for all three fields with a single <code>--j"
       & "son</code> call,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "so each component boots node once instead of once per field "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " a 3x reduction"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "in subprocess starts that keeps the graph build responsive on vendored"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "JavaScript trees. The fallback runs only when the offline read finds nothing"
       & ","
       & ASCII.LF
       & "so a vendored package that ships a licence never touches the network. The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "resolved licence flows into every SBOM format (CycloneDX <code>licenses</cod"
       & "e>, SPDX"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>licenseConcluded</code> / <code>licenseDeclared</code>, Markdown <code"
       & ">License</code> column) and the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dashboard detail panel; the resolved version and website appear in the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dashboard detail panel and the <code>/api/deps</code> JSON.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The resolver caches each answer in a per-project store under the project"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "result cache (the same <code>--cache-dir</code> the scan uses), keyed by the"
       & " target"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "directory as well as the ecosystem and package name, with a 7-day TTL, the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "same scheme as the system-tool version probes.  The content-addressed result"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cache does not cover these registry calls (each one boots node for npm/pnpm)"
       & ","
       & ASCII.LF
       & "so without this layer a warm run still re-paid them; the meta cache makes ev"
       & "ery"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "repeat run serve the licence, version, and website from disk with no subproc"
       & "ess"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "spawn, and two projects that share a cache directory never serve each other"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "resolved licence or version.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Bundled dashboard assets (FlexSearch, nomnoml, graphre) resolve"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "their licence and website live from the package registry when a loose vendor"
       & "ed"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "copy is scanned, preferring <code>pnpm show &lt;pkg&gt; license</code> and f"
       & "alling back to"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>npm</code>, <code>yarn</code>, then <code>bun</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the same preference chain as every JavaScript"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "component (see <a href=""#licence-resolution"">Licence resolution</a>).  The S"
       & "BOM and the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Credits tab therefore track the real upstream licence instead of a hard-code"
       & "d"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "copy.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""system-dependencies""><a class=""header"" href=""#system-dependencies"">S"
       & "ystem dependencies</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>Discover_System_Dev_Deps</code> scans the project"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s build and dev files (Makefiles,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "shell scripts, Python tools, CI workflows, GPR files, Ada sources) for a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "curated set of known system binaries, then keeps only the tools that are"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "installed on <code>PATH</code>. Each becomes a <code>system</code>-scope com"
       & "ponent of the root with"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "a <code>pkg:generic/&lt;name&gt;</code> PURL, a resolved <code>version</code"
       & "> (from <code>&lt;tool&gt; --version</code>),"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and no external link or licence "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " by design adacovex provisions only the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "version for system tools and never guesses a repository or licence for them."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>system</code> is a first-class dependency scope, distinct from <code>b"
       & "ase</code>, <code>dev</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>transitive</code>, <code>vendored</code>, and <code>test</code>; the d"
       & "ashboard gives it its own filter"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "checkbox, badge colour, and legend entry, and the SBOM lists it under"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>system</code> scope.  The dashboard marks these with a <code>system</c"
       & "ode> scope badge and a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "note in the detail panel.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The result shows up in the dashboard Dependency tab (per-dependency detai"
       & "l"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "popup) and in every SBOM renderer: CycloneDX <code>components[].language</co"
       & "de>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "SPDX/JSON <code>adacovex:language</code> property, and the Markdown table"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Language</code> column.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""test-dependencies""><a class=""header"" href=""#test-dependencies"">Test "
       & "dependencies</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A dependency used only by the project"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s tests is classified <code>test</code> (the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>adacovex:dep_scope</code> property value <code>""test""</code>).  adacov"
       & "ex recognises"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "test-only declarations in every supported ecosystem"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s manifest, in addition"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "to the Alire <code>[[test-depends-on]]</code> sections and test project file"
       & "s:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><th>Manifest file</th><th>Test label</th></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>package.json</code></td><td>a dependency section whose key con"
       & "tains <code>test</code> (for example <code>testDependencies</code> or <code>"
       & "devTestDependencies</code>); a name whose last segment starts or ends with <"
       & "code>test</code> (for example <code>@playwright/test</code>, <code>vitest</c"
       & "ode>)</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>Cargo.toml</code></td><td>the <code>[dev-dependencies]</code> "
       & "section (Cargo"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s test-only section); any section whose name contains <code>test</code> (for"
       & " example <code>[target.'cfg(test)'.dependencies]</code>)</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>go.mod</code></td><td>no native test-only section: the name he"
       & "uristic is the signal (a module path whose last path segment starts or ends "
       & "with <code>test</code>, for example <code>github.com/stretchr/testify</code>"
       & ")</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>composer.json</code></td><td>the <code>require-dev</code> sect"
       & "ion</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>Gemfile</code></td><td>gems inside a <code>group :test</code> "
       & "block (any group name containing <code>test</code>)</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>pom.xml</code></td><td><code>&lt;dependency&gt;</code> blocks "
       & "whose <code>&lt;scope&gt;</code> is <code>test</code></td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>pyproject.toml</code></td><td>optional-dependencies extras who"
       & "se name contains <code>test</code> (for example the <code>test</code> extra)"
       & "; Poetry sections such as <code>[tool.poetry.group.test.dependencies]</code>"
       & "</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>Package.swift</code></td><td>dependencies declared inside a <c"
       & "ode>.testTarget(...)</code> block</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>requirements*.txt</code></td><td>no native test section: the n"
       & "ame heuristic is the signal</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A vendored component (for example a package under <code>node_modules</cod"
       & "e> or"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>vendor/</code>) is classified <code>test</code> when the project manif"
       & "est that owns the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "vendor directory declares it under one of these test labels, or when its"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "name carries the test label.  The name heuristic works across every"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "supported ecosystem "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " not just npm: it checks the full name and then the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "last segment after any <code>/</code> or <code>:</code>, so <code>@playwrigh"
       & "t/test</code>, <code>test-case</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>github.com/stretchr/testify</code> and <code>org.testng:testng</code> "
       & "are all"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "test-labelled.  The heuristic also applies to <strong>lockfile-resolved name"
       & "s</strong>:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>pnpm-lock.yaml</code> / <code>package-lock.json</code> / <code>yarn.lo"
       & "ck</code> entries next to an"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "owner <code>package.json</code>, <code>Cargo.lock</code> crate names, and <c"
       & "ode>alire.lock</code> crates"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "that the manifest sets leave transitive.  The e2e fixture"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>@playwright/test</code> is the canonical example: it stays a <code>dev"
       & "Dependencies</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "entry of <code>tests/e2e/package.json</code> (and a <code>pnpm-lock.yaml</co"
       & "de> entry) and is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "classified <code>test</code> by name.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                    </main>"
