       & "<p><strong>DO-178C</strong> is the avionics software standard. It defines ho"
       & "w to design,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "implement, verify, and certify software that flies airplanes. Every line of"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "safety-critical flight software is assessed at one of five <strong>DAL</stro"
       & "ng> (Development"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Assurance Level) tiers, from <strong>DAL-E</strong> (no safety effect) to <s"
       & "trong>DAL-A</strong>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(catastrophic failure can bring down the aircraft).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>ISO 26262</strong> is the automotive functional-safety standard. "
       & "It applies the same"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "rigor to road-vehicle software (braking, steering, powertrain). Its integrit"
       & "y"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "levels are called <strong>ASIL</strong> (Automotive Safety Integrity Level),"
       & " from <strong>QM</strong>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(quality management, no hazard) to <strong>ASIL D</strong> (highest hazard)."
       & "</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>IEC 62304</strong> is the medical-device software lifecycle stand"
       & "ard. It classifies"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "software into <strong>safety classes</strong> A, B, and C based on the sever"
       & "ity of harm a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "failure can cause.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>All three demand the same underlying evidence:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Requirement traceability</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " every high-level requirement (HLR) is traced"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "by a <code>-- HLR-XXXX</code> tag in source.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>No orphan tags</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " every tag in source maps to a defined HLR.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Tests passing</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the test suite has zero failures (except at the lowest"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tier).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Minimum SPARK level</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the formal-proof bar for the selected rigor tier.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex computes all four checks once and re-labels the result per stand"
       & "ard."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "The same inputs feed the same outputs. Only the integrity-level label change"
       & "s.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""when-to-use-which-standard""><a class=""header"" href=""#when-to-use-whi"
       & "ch-standard"">When to use which standard</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><th>Domain</th><th>Standard</th><th>CLI flag</th><th>Levels</th></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>Avionics</td><td>DO-178C</td><td><code>--dal=</code></td><td>A, B, C"
       & ", D, E</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>Automotive</td><td>ISO 26262</td><td><code>--asil=</code></td><td>A,"
       & " B, C, D, QM</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>Medical</td><td>IEC 62304</td><td><code>--class=</code></td><td>A, B"
       & ", C</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>If your project targets multiple domains, <code>--standard=all</code> run"
       & "s one assessment"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and emits badges and reports for every standard without re-scanning.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""what-the-rigor-tiers-mean""><a class=""header"" href=""#what-the-rigor-t"
       & "iers-mean"">What the rigor tiers mean</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><th>Rigor tier</th><th>DO-178C</th><th>ISO 26262</th><th>IEC 62304</th><"
       & "th>Min SPARK</th><th>Tests</th><th>HLRs</th></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>Catastrophic</td><td>DAL A</td><td>ASIL D</td><td>Class C</td><td>Go"
       & "ld</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>Hazardous</td><td>DAL B</td><td>ASIL C</td><td>Class B</td><td>Silve"
       & "r</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>Major</td><td>DAL C</td><td>ASIL B</td><td>Class A</td><td>Bronze</t"
       & "d><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>Minor</td><td>DAL D</td><td>ASIL A</td><td>"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "</td><td>Stone</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>No safety effect</td><td>DAL E</td><td>QM</td><td>"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "</td><td>"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "</td><td>No</td><td>Yes</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The tier placement is a per-project policy choice. The standards do not d"
       & "efine a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "one-to-one correspondence. adacovex"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s default mapping is shown above. Use"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>--standard=NAME</code> to select the labelling standard. Use <code>--d"
       & "al=LEVEL</code> to pin"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the shared rigor tier.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""rigor-tier-mapping""><a class=""header"" href=""#rigor-tier-mapping"">Rig"
       & "or-tier mapping</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><th>Rigor tier</th><th>DO-178C</th><th>ISO 26262</th><th>IEC 62304</th><"
       & "th>Min SPARK</th><th>Tests</th><th>HLRs</th></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>Catastrophic</td><td>DAL A</td><td>ASIL D</td><td>Class C</td><td>Go"
       & "ld</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>Hazardous</td><td>DAL B</td><td>ASIL C</td><td>Class B</td><td>Silve"
       & "r</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>Major</td><td>DAL C</td><td>ASIL B</td><td>Class A</td><td>Bronze</t"
       & "d><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>Minor</td><td>DAL D</td><td>ASIL A</td><td>"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "</td><td>Stone</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>No safety effect</td><td>DAL E</td><td>QM</td><td>"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "</td><td>"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "</td><td>No</td><td>Yes</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The exact tier placement of each standard"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s levels is a per-project policy"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "choice. The standards do not define a one-to-one correspondence. The table"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "above is adacovex"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s default mapping. <code>--standard=NAME</code> selects the labelling"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "standard. <code>--dal=LEVEL</code> pins the shared rigor tier (see"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a href=""#implementation"">Implementation</a>).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""assessment-criteria-shared""><a class=""header"" href=""#assessment-crit"
       & "eria-shared"">Assessment criteria (shared)</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The four checks stay identical across standards. Only the names change:</"
       & "p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Requirement traceability</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " every HLR defined in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>docs/compliance/HLR.md</code> is traced by a <code>-- HLR-XXXX</code> "
       & "tag in source.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>No orphan tags</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " every in-source HLR maps to a defined HLR.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Tests passing</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " zero failures (not enforced at the lowest tier).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Minimum SPARK level</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the proof bar for the selected rigor tier.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Because the checks are shared, <strong>the compliance artifacts are ident"
       & "ical too</strong>:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "ISO 26262 and IEC 62304 require no different evidence or documents than"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "DO-178C. The same inputs (<code>HLR.md</code>, source traceability, proof su"
       & "mmary, test"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "summary) feed the same outputs (<code>VERIFICATION.md</code>, <code>TRACE.md"
       & "</code>, the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "proof-aware SBOM, and the compliance SVG badges) for every standard. Only th"
       & "e"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "integrity-level label printed inside them changes (<code>DAL-C</code>, <code"
       & ">ASIL B</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Class A</code>).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""selecting-a-standard-on-the-cli""><a class=""header"" href=""#selecting-"
       & "a-standard-on-the-cli"">Selecting a standard on the CLI</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Each standard has a dedicated level flag, so your intent is unambiguous o"
       & "n the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "command line (full flag details in the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a href=""cli-reference.html"">CLI reference</a>). The flags all resolve to th"
       & "e same shared"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "rigor tier:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><th>Standard</th><th>Flag</th><th>Levels</th><th>Example (tier)</th></tr"
       & ">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>DO-178C</td><td><code>--dal=</code></td><td>A, B, C, D, E</td><td><c"
       & "ode>--dal=C</code> -&gt; DAL-C (Major)</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>ISO 26262</td><td><code>--asil=</code></td><td>A, B, C, D, QM</td><t"
       & "d><code>--asil=B</code> -&gt; ASIL B (Major)</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>IEC 62304</td><td><code>--class=</code></td><td>A, B, C</td><td><cod"
       & "e>--class=A</code> -&gt; Class A (Major)</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>You can also use <code>--standard=iso26262 --dal=C</code> to get the same"
       & " result as"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>--asil=B</code>. The dedicated flags exist so a reader of the command "
       & "line can see"
       & ASCII.LF
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "ASIL B"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " (or "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "Class A"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & ") without decoding the shared tier.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>--standard=all</code> runs <strong>one</strong> assessment at the s"
       & "hared tier and emits badges"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and reports for <strong>every</strong> standard "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>do178c.svg</code>, <code>iso26262.svg</code>, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>iec62304.svg</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " without re-scanning, re-proving, or re-parsing anything. The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "evidence is identical across standards. The three badges therefore always"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "agree on Achieved/Unmet. Only the level label changes.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""dashboard-and-sbom-standard-awareness""><a class=""header"" href=""#dash"
       & "board-and-sbom-standard-awareness"">Dashboard and SBOM standard-awareness</a>"
       & "</h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The served <a href=""dashboard.html"">dashboard</a> (<code>--serve</code>) "
       & "and the proof-aware"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a href=""sbom.html"">SBOM</a> both record the assessment standard and its nat"
       & "ive level"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "label, so a browser or a CycloneDX / SPDX / Markdown consumer sees the right"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "name for the selected standard."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Like the <code>sbom</code> subcommand, <code>--serve</code> <strong>defaults"
       & " to all standards</strong> when no"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>--standard</code> / <code>--asil</code> / <code>--class</code> flag is"
       & " given. The dashboard renders"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "every standard"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s level at the shared tier. An explicit standard flag"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "narrows it. The SBOM"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <code>adacovex:standard</code> / <code>adacovex:level</code> properties:</"
       & "p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><th><code>--</code> flag</th><th><code>adacovex:standard</code></th><th>"
       & "<code>adacovex:level</code></th></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>--dal=C</code></td><td><code>DO-178C</code></td><td><code>DAL-"
       & "C</code></td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>--asil=B</code></td><td><code>ISO 26262</code></td><td><code>A"
       & "SIL B</code></td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>--class=A</code></td><td><code>IEC 62304</code></td><td><code>"
       & "Class A</code></td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>--standard=all</code></td><td><code>DO-178C, ISO 26262, IEC 62"
       & "304</code></td><td><code>DAL-C / ASIL B / Class A</code></td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code>adacovex:dal_target</code> property always carries the shared t"
       & "ier (<code>DAL-A</code>.."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>DAL-D</code>) regardless of the labelling standard. <code>--standard=a"
       & "ll</code> joins all"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "three standard names and level labels into the single <code>adacovex:standar"
       & "d</code> and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>adacovex:level</code> properties. One document carries every standard"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "assessment.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""implementation""><a class=""header"" href=""#implementation"">Implementat"
       & "ion</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>Compliance_Standard</code> type (<code>DO_178C</code>, <code>ISO_2"
       & "6262</code>, <code>IEC_62304</code>) with"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>To_String</code> / <code>To_Standard</code> / <code>Standard_Slug</cod"
       & "e> conversions and the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dedicated <code>To_ASIL</code> / <code>To_Class</code> level parsers in <cod"
       & "e>Adacovex.Types</code>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>--standard=NAME</code> CLI flag (default <code>do178c</code>, plus"
       & " <code>all</code>) selects the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "labelling standard. <code>--dal=LEVEL</code> is the shared rigor tier (A"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "E). The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dedicated <code>--asil=LEVEL</code> / <code>--class=LEVEL</code> flags set b"
       & "oth the standard and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the tier in one step.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>Types.Standard_Level_Name</code> maps a standard + tier to its lab"
       & "el (<code>DAL-C</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>ASIL B</code>, <code>Class A</code>, and more). <code>Assess_Standard<"
       & "/code> runs the same evidence"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "checks as <code>Assess_DAL</code> while recording the standard. Every render"
       & "er"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(ANSI report, SVG badge, HTML dashboard, JSON API, Markdown report, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "SBOM) then prints the standard-specific level without re-running scanning,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "proof parsing, or test parsing.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>Min_SPARK_For</code> still drives the per-tier proof bar. The tier"
       & "s share one"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "lookup because the standards only re-label the levels.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Each standard has a dedicated reference page with its level definitions a"
       & "nd"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "criteria:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><a href=""api-docs/adacovex-dal-levels.html"">DO-178C DAL levels</a></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><a href=""api-docs/adacovex-asil-levels.html"">ISO 26262 ASIL levels</a></"
       & "li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><a href=""api-docs/adacovex-class-levels.html"">IEC 62304 safety classes</"
       & "a></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                    </main>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
