       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""target-project-requirements""><a class=""heade"
       & "r"" href=""#target-project-requirements"">Target project requirements</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex assesses an <strong>Ada/SPARK project</strong>. The target root "
       & "can be the repository root or a subdirectory (via <code>--target=PATH</code>"
       & "). For a meaningful report, the target must provide the items that follow. A"
       & "ny missing item shows as <code>N/A</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>DAL checks that depend on the missing item report <code>Unmet</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""what-the-target-provides""><a class=""header"" href=""#what-the-target-p"
       & "rovides"">What the target provides</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>Ada source files</strong> (<code>.ads</code>) under the target ro"
       & "ot "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " scanned for"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "subprogram declarations, docstrings, and HLR traceability tags. See the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a href=""api-docs/adacovex-docstring-spec.html"">docstring spec</a> for the a"
       & "nnotation"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "format and coverage rules.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>GNATprove output</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " a <code>gnatprove.out</code> summary, discovered in this"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "order:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>&lt;target&gt;/obj/gnatprove/gnatprove.out</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>&lt;target&gt;/gnatprove.out</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>&lt;target&gt;/gnatprove/gnatprove.out</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Or run <code>adacovex prove</code> (or the GitHub Action with <code>prove"
       & ": true</code>) to"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "generate a fresh summary before you assess.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>Test results</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " a test-summary file, auto-discovered from a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "conventional name at the project root or under <code>docs/</code> (for examp"
       & "le"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>test_result.md</code>, <code>test_results.md</code>, <code>test-result"
       & ".md</code>, <code>tests.md</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>test_result.txt</code>, <code>test_results.log</code>, <code>docs/test"
       & "_result.md</code>, "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(166)
       & ")."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Supported formats come from your runner"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s log or a summary file:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Markdown tables: the native <code>test_runner</code> layout"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>| Category | N | PASS |</code> and the AUnit-report layout"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>| - | Category | N | PASS |</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>TAP (<code>ok</code>/<code>not ok</code>)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>GNU Automake (<code>PASS:</code>/<code>FAIL:</code>)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Maven Surefire (<code>Tests run: N</code>)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Unity (<code>N Tests M Failures</code>)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>See the <a href=""api-docs/adacovex-test-format.html"">test format spec</a>"
       & " for the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "detailed rules (what each line looks like and which line wins when formats"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "mix).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>HLR / LLR documents</strong> (for DAL assessment) "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>&lt;target&gt;/docs/compliance/HLR.md</code> and optionally"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>&lt;target&gt;/docs/compliance/LLR.md</code>, following the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a href=""api-docs/adacovex-docstring-spec.html#hlr-traceability-tags"">HLR tr"
       & "aceability-tag format</a>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""missing-data""><a class=""header"" href=""#missing-data"">Missing data</a"
       & "></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><th>Missing</th><th>Effect</th></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>No <code>.ads</code> sources</td><td>No packages scanned; metrics re"
       & "port zero</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>No <code>gnatprove.out</code></td><td>SPARK level <code>Stone</code>"
       & ", proof metrics <code>N/A</code></td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>No test summary</td><td>Test metrics <code>N/A</code>; DAL <code>Tes"
       & "ts passing</code> criterion <code>Unmet</code></td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>No <code>HLR.md</code></td><td>HLR coverage <code>N/A</code>; DAL tr"
       & "aceability criteria <code>Unmet</code></td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""non-ada-projects""><a class=""header"" href=""#non-ada-projects"">Non-Ada"
       & " projects</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex currently targets Ada/SPARK sources. Non-Ada projects (C/C++, Py"
       & "thon,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "JS, and more) that want the compliance/SBOM tooling provide their own"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>alire.toml</code> / <code>alire-dev.toml</code> to manage the Ada depe"
       & "ndencies needed to build"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "adacovex itself. Running <code>adacovex</code> from such a repo scans it and"
       & " uses its"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "manifest.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<blockquote>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>We are working on support for other languages. Watch for updates.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</blockquote>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""vendored-code-and-strict-mode""><a class=""header"" href=""#vendored-cod"
       & "e-and-strict-mode"">Vendored code and strict mode</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>By default (strict mode) adacovex scans and counts every directory except"
       & " the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "always-excluded ones. Vendored code is included. For third-party code you"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cannot modify, use docstring <strong>patch files</strong> at"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>&lt;target&gt;/.adacovex/patches/&lt;relative-path&gt;</code> (see"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a href=""architecture.html#patch-system"">Architecture "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " Patch System</a>). Or run in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "relaxed mode (<code>--relaxed</code>, skip dirs, no patches) (see"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a href=""cli-reference.html#strict-vs-relaxed-mode"">Strict vs relaxed mode</"
       & "a>).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Vendored code can also take part in the <strong>SPARK proof</strong>. A p"
       & "atch carrying <code>SPARK_Mode</code> / <code>Pre</code> / <code>Post</code>"
       & " / <code>Global</code> aspects is a <em>proof patch</em>. The <code>prove</c"
       & "ode> subcommand merges it into a patched tree copy. The copy uses <code>.ads"
       & "</code> spec contracts and <code>.adb</code> body patches that opt a SPARK-c"
       & "lean vendored body into the proof.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>See <a href=""proving.html#proof-patches-proving-vendored-dependencies"">Pr"
       & "oving and writing proofs</a> for how to write them. See <a href=""architectur"
       & "e.html#proof-patches-spark-contracts-over-vendored-dependencies"">Architectur"
       & "e "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " Proof patches</a> for the design.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                    </main>"
