       & "                    <main>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""vcs-support-and-differential-assessment""><a "
       & "class=""header"" href=""#vcs-support-and-differential-assessment"">VCS support a"
       & "nd differential assessment</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>A version control system is not required for base adacovex functi"
       & "onality.</strong></p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>This covers scanning, proof analysis, test parsing, compliance assessment"
       & ", SBOM generation, dashboards, and caching.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A VCS is only needed for the differential modes below. They snapshot a ba"
       & "se revision to compare against the current tree.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>We assume that the audited project lives in a VCS. The base tool never re"
       & "quires one.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex works on <strong>Linux and WSL</strong>. The snapshot commands r"
       & "un through <code>sh -c</code>, which WSL provides.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""when-to-use-differential-modes""><a class=""header"" href=""#when-to-use"
       & "-differential-modes"">When to use differential modes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Differential modes are useful when you want to enforce that changes do no"
       & "t regress quality gates:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>PR checks</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>--coverage-delta</code> makes sure that docstring coverage does not d"
       & "rop between the base branch and the PR head. This is the lightest check. It "
       & "works even when the base does not commit proof or test artifacts.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Release gates</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>adacovex --compare-base=v1.2.0</code> compares the current tree again"
       & "st the last release tag. It fails if a metric regressed. These metrics are p"
       & "ackages, docstrings, HLR tags, SPARK level, tests, and DAL status.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Audit trails</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " a side-by-side report shows exactly what changed between two revisions. Thi"
       & "s is useful for compliance audits that need a narrative diff.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""supported-vcs""><a class=""header"" href=""#supported-vcs"">Supported VCS"
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The differential modes run against the VCS that manages the target. Detec"
       & "tion is marker-file based, with a command-probe fallback:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><th>VCS</th><th>Marker</th><th>Base snapshot mechanism</th></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>git</td><td><code>.git</code></td><td><code>git worktree add --detac"
       & "h</code> (linked worktree)</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>jj</td><td><code>.jj</code></td><td><code>jj git export</code> into "
       & "the internal git store, then a git worktree against <code>.jj/repo/store/git"
       & "</code> (jj commits are git commits)</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>Mercurial</td><td><code>.hg</code></td><td><code>hg archive -r REF D"
       & "IR</code> (pure export)</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>Subversion</td><td><code>.svn</code></td><td><code>svn info --show-i"
       & "tem url</code> + <code>svn export -r REF URL DIR</code></td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>Fossil</td><td><code>.fslckout</code> / <code>_FOSSIL_</code></td><t"
       & "d>copy the repo DB and <code>fossil open</code> it at REF in a scratch dir</"
       & "td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>For colocated git+jj repos, git wins (exact interop). All snapshots land "
       & "in <code>/tmp/adacovex-diff-&lt;pid&gt;</code> and are cleaned up afterwards"
       & ". The working tree is never touched.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>UX recommendation</strong>: Git gives the best experience. Jj is "
       & "its git-compatible sibling. Mercurial is fully supported. For VCS whose snap"
       & "shot UX is poor, adacovex prints a note. The note recommends that developers"
       & " convert the repository to git (or a git-compatible VCS):</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Subversion</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " no local history, network-dependent checkouts, slow <code>svn export</code>"
       & " per snapshot. Converting gives local branches, offline history, and faster "
       & "diffs.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Fossil</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " workable, but the tooling is niche and the single-file DB model complicates"
       & " CI integration.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>These notes are informational only. The assessment still runs and gates s"
       & "till apply on every supported VCS.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>adacovex status</code> reports the VCS command-line tools on <code>"
       & "$PATH</code>. These tools are git, mercurial/<code>hg</code>, subversion/<co"
       & "de>svn</code>, fossil, jj, and <code>mandb</code>. It reports the VCS detect"
       & "ed for the target repository. It prints a note when the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s VCS tool is missing.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>See <a href=""platforms.html#status-subcommand"">Platforms</a>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""--compare-baseref""><a class=""header"" href=""#--compare-baseref""><code"
       & ">--compare-base=REF</code></a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Differential mode: adacovex snapshots a base revision in a temporary dire"
       & "ctory (<code>/tmp/adacovex-diff-&lt;pid&gt;</code>). It prints a side-by-sid"
       & "e comparison against the current tree. The comparison shows packages, subpro"
       & "grams, docstring percentage, traced HLR, orphan tags, SPARK level, proved VC"
       & "s, tests, and DAL status.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code>--target</code> directory must be a supported VCS repository. T"
       & "he VCS command-line tool must be on <code>PATH</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Exit <code>0</code> only if there are no regressions and the current DAL "
       & "is Achieved. Otherwise, exit <code>1</code>. Artifacts that the base does no"
       & "t commit report <code>N/A</code> and are not compared. These artifacts are <"
       & "code>gnatprove.out</code> and a test-result summary.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""--coverage-deltaref""><a class=""header"" href=""#--coverage-deltaref""><"
       & "code>--coverage-delta=REF</code></a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Lightweight docstring-coverage gate for PR-style CI checks. It scans sour"
       & "ces, patches, and computes docstring metrics on a base revision and the curr"
       & "ent tree. It does not use GNATprove, tests, or DAL. Thus it works when the b"
       & "ase does not commit build artifacts.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>It prints a compact coverage table and a machine-parseable <code>coverage"
       & "_delta:</code> line. Then it cleans up the snapshot.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Exit <code>0</code> if the current docstring coverage is <code>&gt;=</cod"
       & "e> the base. Exit <code>0</code> also if the base has no sources. Exit <code"
       & ">1</code> if coverage regressed. This mode is mutually exclusive with <code>"
       & "--compare-base</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>make release</code> runs the same gate against the last release tag"
       & ". For example, <code>--coverage-delta=v1.1.0</code> aborts if docstring cove"
       & "rage regressed between releases.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                    </main>"
